us,United States,10700708228,2023-12-15T22:24:48-07:00,Recent updates seem to have lost the people’s interest,"Recently the app has gone through many changes, and here I am. I’d like to say with the update that was pushed to my phone today, it is extremely hard to do much. The media list of people online was hard to find, the separation between servers and messages feels just plain wrong, the removal of numbers. I’ve been using discord since 2018, so maybe I’m being picky. But it seems Discord as a company doesn’t want to listen to its ‘consumer’ anyways. There was negative feedback about the removal of the number system for usernames, the altering links feature which can lead to scamming and hacking, and the lash back about the most recent UI changes.
While I understand that company has to have integrity and be able to reason, I feel that in some stances the Discord company can’t see that certain changes might affect their platform negatively. 
My number one concern is that Discord isn’t listening to its users, you can be firm and have a middle ground. Some of the changes aren’t the end of the world, none of them are. But sometimes the changes can seriously endanger the users, if said users aren’t careful enough.
That being said, the new update of separation of servers and DMs is annoying, the almost inability to find server members and their current online status is so, so infuriating as someone who checks this feature often. Oh, and to put it rather blunt, the new UI is very ugly.
Discord is my number one app, it’s my messaging app, my notes app, I use this app more than I use the general texting app. Please, listen to your users.",5,208.1,StawberryIcicle,0
us,United States,12895610863,2025-07-15T11:43:29-07:00,Wifi vs Data,"I’ve had Discord for years, since 2017 and not had a lot of issues with the site other than bots at the time which has gotten a little better ig. I’ve always been able to use Discord with fairly easy use and consistency for the past years, but I’ve also have had wifi for the most part and even being off wifi in the past it has been good before with little issues.
Now, recently, I’ve been coming across multiple issues. I now have no Wifi and have been using Data full time and it has become such a pain to use.
I have Nitro and had it for a year now and for the past 6 months on data and it uses so much Data for one, I’m glad the clear cache is added but doesn’t do much or even really work and still have to uninstall the app when necessary ( apple problem ). The issues I have is messages refusing to load and send at all and can take up to an hour to send one message and have had messages continuously duplicate after each hard reset which is really annoying. Hard resets to the app does not reset the app all the time and takes many and multiple attempts even after waiting a minute or two. Trying to send photos which can and will take longer than an hour just to send or even load and gods forbid I send more than one photo at a time. I’ve had issues with false notifications, and issues with them not going away even after checking and hard restarting the app, multiple times. 
This wouldn’t be as irritating if I wasn’t paying for Nitro, and not the basic at that, and it struggle so hard to do the basic tasks above.",3,288.0,SOAPGAVSSUSHWWJHEVEV,0
us,United States,10745749911,2023-12-25T22:26:33-07:00,Don’t fix what ain’t broke— unless it’s to make it better.,"I honestly can’t understand what is so WRONG with this new ui. First of all, it is now infinitely easier to see what your friends are playing. I used to have so much trouble seeing whether my friends were online, and it just became so much easier (I also LOVE that the icon of the game they're playing is now so much bigger and more visible). I also like how you separated your DMs and your servers. I used to hate having to scroll up the server list to access my DMs, as I am in a ton of servers, so thank you, discord. I do admit it is a bit weird how now you cannot simply swipe left to see who is online in a server, but you can easily adjust to that. I also love how when you enter a server, the server bar just disappears. It makes things look so much less cluttered and makes it a lot easier to navigate the channels. So really, this new ui is awesome, and I have no idea what people are on about.

I also noticed that people are saying this new update is… buggy? I have no idea what they are on about, as I currently own an iPhone 11 that has been in heavy use by me AND my sister over the last ten years, including multiple cracks on the back due to the multiple times my sister has dropped it, but discord runs perfectly fine. It is most likely a software problem if discord is crashing— just update your software to at least iOS 16 (for apple users, samsung users, sorry you’re on your own ;P)

So overall, I think this was an awesome update, and it really made the mobile discord a whole better experience. If you’re complaining, boohoo, deal with it. :3",5,209.0,GameChangee,1
us,United States,4335888774,2019-06-18T13:45:10-07:00,Please listen Discord,"I love using you as a platform. You’re awesome, you do well, but with some of these recent updates for ios, I think everyone I know feels the same way when I say it’s concerning. Let me explain: so for maybe a month now, you introduced call kit. You guys may have seen this as a bright idea, and on paper, it is. But this kind of change was unneeded, unwanted, and thus had a more negative effect overall. It got so annoying to the point I decided to never call someone unless I was on PC. Because otherwise, I’d feel like my privacy could be “breached” as others could see I was on discord, didn’t feel right, and it was glitchy, along with it showing up in the calls section of the phone app. I don’t want that. And now, changing how leaving a call or vc works. I understand it’s a move to make it more like PC so when you leave, it gives a little notification, but not everyone wanted that on phone. Where it can be loud and irritating. And worse: no option to turn it off unless you remove it from PC then turn off sync. I do believe this could 100% be a 5 star app (in my eyes, I understand a 4.8 is good enough), but making these out of no where changes without warning or second thoughts feels... off. I’m gonna try and do the little sync trick I thought of and hope it works. I really hope this changes. I doubt I will leave currently, this still is a great platform, but I hope this does not get out of hand. I mean this from the bottom of my heart, I wanna see this app do well",4,3.0.3,CyursLight,0
us,United States,2097667386,2018-01-17T02:59:15-07:00,I Love Discord,"I have never written a review before, for anything. But Discord has become one of the best ways to communicate to my teams that I have built over the past year, I just can’t not write a review about this app. Discord itself has changed my life as cliche as it sounds, but it’s true. Discord has been the stepping stones that led to bigger things, exponentially. First starting using it to keep in touch with a couple friends, which turned into a hangout for a few more friends I met online, to turning into making a server for a clan for clan related stuff, which has now developed into a server for development of a game in production, that can earn me real money doing what I love to do, with those same few people I mentioned earlier. This means of communications is terrific. The app version doesn’t have as many features compared to PC (access to audit logs, not as easy to navigate in, ), but it is pretty much just as good if those things are overlooked, or if mobile is just temporary while you are away from your keyboard. Not only are you able to make your own servers for your own reasons, you are able to customize your server name, picture, voice chat with others with pristine connection, chat channels to keep your chat organized, permissions to who has access to what whether that is channels, roles, even permissions; what you do with your server is up to you. Great for management, a hangout for your friends, .. a development team, how you use discord is literally only limited to your imagination. Without discord, I wouldn’t be in teams I am today, wouldn’t have met some of the coolest people I know",5,2.2.0,Matts.3,0
us,United States,10854120466,2024-01-23T00:54:16-07:00,Bugs need some work,"I use discord everyday, and I believe discord is one of the best apps to text, talk, and video call on. But does not mean there aren’t a lot of bugs, I have no clue why but sometimes when I’m on voice chat with my friends I try to show them some sound on another device, and they can never hear it? I turn off the Krisp option each time when I’m on vc because it will sometimes block my voice if I talk to quiet. But discord has no problem showing sounds that come from outside my apartment that my friend can hear (planes, cars, etc.) I hope this feature can be fixed because I do not like any other apps to voice chat. Another problem I’ve had is that sometimes features on the Chrome or safari version are not on the app? It’s a major inconvenience to turn off automatic emojis I had to log into discord on chrome, make this option on the app version. There are a lot of small bugs that happen on this app, like sometimes when I change tabs and go back to discord while on vc the app freezes to the point I have to close it and open it again. Messages also will get stuck not sending, I’m not blaming my Wi-Fi for that because I have good Wi-Fi connection and I have data so this is 100% a discord problem. But these small bugs add up and are super annoying and frustrating. I just ask the discord team to fix the app to be better.",4,213.0,izzywizzy2024,245
us,United States,11434162734,2024-06-28T13:13:36-07:00,My general thoughts,"It’s a good overall app, I use it for gaming, entertainment, work, etc. but like another review said, it has a sharp learning curve which is hard to learn for some. Also, there are a lot of scamming bots on the app that pretend to be women that I find on apps like Gamerlink, Psn, Twitch, that say to add their account on Discord. It’s a massive problem for those who battle addiction to porn or people who are gullible (I am not one of them). I think that there might need to be an optional tutorial that pops up when you first get the app that shows you where things are and warns you about bots and such. I enjoy the app because I have learned it, creating servers and adding bots is a very surreal experience because it’s like you make your own little town of people. Many still fall for the chatbots and the incapability of learning  the app. Some of my close friends tried the app and hated it for the reasons I’ve just mentioned. My friends and I agree that the chatbots are more of a nuisance to people trying to experience the immersive capabilities of the app/ community bots. I understand the Nitro/ Subscription, but I feel like there should be the ability to purchase something’s separate, having more tiers of subscription for different usage niches. Overall, this app is very good for hanging out but has some problems that can affect the experience in a major/threatening way.",4,235.0,KingFamily830,130
us,United States,10679418872,2023-12-10T11:03:44-07:00,Follow up to my previous reviews,"Just wanted to say I’m sorry for getting all worked up before. I should have done a bit more research and also could have worded my concerns better. While I may be sorry for how I expressed my concerns, I still stand by what I said overall! Although from what I’ve learned recently, it seems you are currently working on new features that help to keep discord as safe as possible, while also giving users the tools to keep themselves safe as well! While I’m still cautious of course, I’m glad you guys are actually trying to help keep the platform safe, and being more transparent about things and giving users the tools to be as safe as well! (That being said, please try to balance safety and privacy. I’m all for making Discord safer and all, but I don’t want either side to overpower the other!)

One last thing: I noticed that the app was updated on my iPad, and while nothing seems any different from before the update, I do want to reiterate: please fix any bugs that your users are complaining about! For me personally, I haven’t experienced anything different yet. (Even the UI is pretty much the same on my iPad, and honestly, the whole UI thing isn’t too big of a deal. As long as it’s still ergonomic and easy.) so if you guys fixed everything, then thank you! But if the bugs are still a thing, and they’re something that affects the iPhone app and Desktop app, please fix them!",3,207,Invader-mobile,16
