us,United States,7524514881,2021-06-30T14:30:46-07:00,Problem incoming(can you send me the same response I deleted it on accident),"Hello there,I would like to say that discord looks VERY fun but I can not even log in I put my phone number and user but nothing worked same with password and I know they are correct, My friends tell me to look at my bottom left corner on my screen but I see nothing but white I would like to change it where you can just put in what age you are choose your ""name"" so that people who want to get in but are having a hard time logging in can just do that stuff and then they are finished and they are in! I have not even been able to do anything in discord except try to log in and stuff this part is hard for people so I would like you to change it so people can easily get in maybe even a math test for people who are younger then 17+ so that they can not mess with this game and mess around, I think this game needs more protection but less problems, I have stayed up for 3 days no sleep at all just to try to get in this game but failed every time I try my fingers hurt from typing I have typed all day log just to get in this game, it also looks like Tik Tok if you think of it a little bit and that makes me wonder is it like tik tok but looks different? I have been wondering if it is not what I expect either because almost each game I play have problems so I would like to have a answer to this, is this a trash game a little bit? Besides that please change it to a different login please it is getting on my nerves a lot.",2,80.0,Happy halloween 🎃👻💀☠️❤️🧡🖤,0
us,United States,14270581563,2026-07-06T09:19:34-07:00,"I love Discord, but I hate the lack of being able to easily verify your account.","I loved using Discord! It is like the perfect platform to chat with friends, go in different group chats, find what you’re interested in, communicate & collaborate with others, share videos+files, and it is extremely helpful when you are in a debate! That being said, Discord is faulty when it comes to avoiding suspicious activity from others. I remember when approximately 1-2 years ago there was a person pretending to be me in which case I tried to change my email to avoid being susceptible to their actions. However, when in doing so, Discord kept trying to make me verify my email again as well my phone number and because of this I can’t use Discord anymore because it also won’t let me use my phone number because I keep creating several accounts in which case it doesn’t seem to want to let me use my phone number anymore. I miss being able to chat with my friends because it was the perfect place to do it in. I am a video editor and I love chatting with other video editors because it’s sometimes nice to hear what they have to say. And sometimes you develop nice virtual friendships with certain people online. But sometimes all good things come to an end. I just wish I could use Discord again with no issues, but that seems highly unlikely to ever happen.",4,335.0,Sapphirewarlock,0
us,United States,7242279207,2021-04-19T21:59:52-07:00,"Mostly alright, new update is ambiguous","This is mainly to address the ambiguous ness of the NSFW IOS ban, since it’s not very clearly outlined. On IOS alone, servers with NSFW content are unable to be viewed now except by mods and owners. Now, the issue with this is that a server doesn’t necessarily need to be NSFW, but simply have a channel as such that can be accessed on it. One of my friends had an NSFW channel in his server, and told me his server was inaccessible because of it. Now, the issue I have with it is that many channels designated as such are not necessarily pornographic channels, but simply oriented for, let’s say, not very politically correct content. And because of that NSFW marking, servers can be shut down even if it isn’t for porno material. Discord should simply reestablish some form of age verification rather than butcher numerous servers because of an unnecessarily ambiguous and broad label. The main complaint is with the Apple store, who does not allow content with such labels on their store, so rather than monitor who can have what, it’s simply a moniker of nobody is allowed, and that punishes those who are allowed to normally access said content unjustly. Sure, that sort of stuff doesn’t have to be your thing, just as it isn’t mine, but people who do take some interest in it shouldn’t be punished by having servers shut down over an ambiguous rule meant to keep kids out of where they shouldn’t be. If Microsoft and apple had any reasonable sense of mind, they wouldn’t ban stuff outright, but limit who sees what",4,70.0,the great meme war,0
us,United States,13841466707,2026-03-12T13:55:14-07:00,One suggestion,"Everything about this app is great and i have a way to talk with my friends out of school! But I just suggest you change something about your limitations unless users get nitro: please make it so everyone regardless of owning nitro or not can change their banner to an image? I understand if it’s better to have people want to earn nitro with orbs or buy it but it really seems like a shameless cash grab for changing banners to an image. If you let users do this without nitro required i guarantee you WILL see more  people using this app, because when people are able to change their profile banner it shows who they are, because most images people have are from how they feel and their personality, if that makes sense. It shows diversity. And this way it gets people more motivated to talk to others, giving you more people that would want to use your app. So please, make it so those without nitro can also change their profile banner (most people who have nitro mainly get it so they can change the banner to an image!)

P.S. - this may be a lot to ask, and I get that, but if you don’t let people without nitro change their profile banner, your company will be viewed as shamelessly cash grabbing. People will act upon this by not using your app more and this will cause an insane decrease of use across all users.",4,319.0,insert nickname???,45
us,United States,8943477088,2022-08-04T01:45:26-07:00,AAAA I LOVE DISCORD! j one thing tho.. 😕,"tbh discord is j great. i use it ALL the time and it’s a really awesome app. i would TOTALLY recommend it for communicating with friends, family, or for school purposes bc of how great and easy it is to use. i’m pretty sure i have been on discord for 8 months now and so far i haven’t had any problems. well, maybe this teeny tiny bit of a problem.. i wouldn't mark off a star for it though, it’s not that big of a deal. anyways it was j abt when u “report” someone i’m not sure if it actually reports them? if i could j have some clarification on that it would be very well appreciated! i’ve j brought this up bc some ppl from servers im in, or friends of my friends, would always msg me or smt and it would always be smt negative and i didn’t like it very much. so i reported them but it didn’t even give me a clarification on if my report went through or not. and it didn’t even give me a choice to tell them what i was reporting about. like i said, i’m not going to take a star off my review because i really don’t see it as a big deal, but if this tiny tiny tiny tiny tiny tiny little ‘problem’ could be fixed, it would definitely satisfy me! OVERALL THOUGH, discord is just freaking awesome. i love it sm. thank you for such a wonderful app!",5,138.0,Ånîmęłøvęr0622,54
us,United States,5310346811,2019-12-23T13:50:19-07:00,Integrated Phone Calls,"Discord is an amazing app that lets you do casual conversations without the loud notifications you would usually get from text messages. It does an amazing job at keeping notifications hidden when you want them to be.
But I cannot say the same for calls. Recently, Discord started integrating their calls with actual phone calls. This means that every time I get called on Discord, it goes through to my ringtone. The whole reason I use Discord is to keep my online life separate from my personal life. 
Although there is a setting that allows you to disable this feature, I still get the ringtone. Whenever I get called on Discord, even though the app is closed, I still get a ringtone. I even have all notifications turned off in my settings. The ringtone only lasts about 2 seconds before it realizes that it should not be there, but it gets pretty annoying, since it forces me to stop whatever i’m doing on my phone.
What annoys me the most is that this issue has been fixed before. The previous update had the setting that disabled the integrated phone calls, but it actually did its job, unlike this recent update. I had no calls going through no matter how much I was getting spammed with calls. 
I thought this problem would be gone forever, but it still managed to find its way back. I’ve resorted to having to delete the app just to avoid the ringtone...again. Please fix this issue.",3,3.1.9,SpareGuitar,236
us,United States,4112995489,2019-05-07T02:14:24-07:00,"Please, please bring back the private call option","Sure, Discord is much better in terms of quality, but by far my biggest complaint is the removal of the private mode option while calling people. I deserve a right to privacy, as does everyone else, and it’s too loud for that to be an option. Other people can hear my conversations and it’s very bothersome. I miss having the option between the two. Don’t fix something that isn’t broken please! Otherwise, there’s this constant bug with webcams/ turning on your camera. sometimes it never loads and you have to turn it off and on to get it to work properly. I’ve had to do this up to 3 times maximum to get it to work finally, which is nothing at first, but becomes annoying. Finally, (most likely not 100% discord’s fault, you can ignore this if you want) the connection seems to be getting worse. I used to love discord for the quality of the calls, but several times a week the quality becomes so bad that I have to restart the call several times to understand a sentence the recipient. The most common connection issue is definitely the that audio seems to skip out entirely for a few seconds sometimes. I understand that this could also be due to my own connection and the recipient’s connection, so take this with a grain of salt. Considering that, many times before there has been nothing wrong with our internet and this still happens.",3,3.0.0,Grumpis D'Gringus,321
us,United States,11438413692,2024-06-29T16:25:04-07:00,I’ve been swatted 3 times now from this app,It’s a good app but if you join the wrong discord servers like I remember I joined one with Roblox there was a guy threatening to murder people by swatting them and the admins on that server were the people swatting others I would always use a VPN when using this app people all the time of different discord servers threaten to pull my IP address a good 28 times maybe I’ve used this app for years and I’ve had to report people swatting to the police cause getting swatted on the platform does happen to people there is tons of porn on discord so if you don’t like porn don’t download this app and there are servers were they allow minors to join the porn which hopefully those people are in safe now I don’t like it either but that’s been a problem for years now discord is my favorite app used for gaming groups I wouldn’t join discord servers that are illegal if you click a few tabs then leave the server you will still get banned discord tracks everything you click on I’ve heard this from many people if there’s a way I can report murder or swatting on the platform cause when I report they still continue swatting people I’ll give you five stars if there’s a good way to report this by calling discord to report this to the police use a VPN on big big discord servers wild things can happen,4,235.0,Bubby7788,23
us,United States,11663088769,2024-08-28T10:32:34-07:00,Still missing needed features,"Months after the UI update, many features are still missing. Swiping right to left in a chat to open the member list still is missing, and an experiment appears to show they want that to function as some kind of search, rather than be at parity with how discord works on desktop and mobile web. Compact mode doesn’t exist in the app, making tons of unused space and large profile icons, when on desktop and mobile web you can focus on whats important; the actual messages. There is no theme as far as i can tell that uses the same coloration as desktop and mobile web; instead of the iconic greys, theres light, black, and amoled black. The text input remains tiny with multiple unused buttons that could be folded into the “+” menu already on the bar. The ui has made some improvements, like servers being in a column like on desktop and mobile web, but hasnt come as far as one would expect after several months of feedback. Besides loading faster than mobile web, i cant see any benefit to using the app at this point.
Edit after response: a link to a help page explaining basic features of the new UI doesn’t address any of the missing features and functions i talked about in my review. Feels like a boilerplate response after reading “UI” four words in, instead of reading the actual feedback. Would appreciate an actual acknowledgement of the feedback.",2,244.0,dijonMM,7
us,United States,11579958315,2024-08-06T12:32:07-07:00,Used to be better,"I am going to say this off the bat, discords desktop app is great and I have, thus far, no complaints. The mobile app is a different story. Things started going downhill when swiping to the left stopped showing server members. It’s been years and I have yet to unlearn the muscle memory from this switch. Now swiping left allows you to reply to messages (when you can just type in the chat but idk). Now you have to tap on the text channel you’re in to view the server members. 

Now text chat is almost unusable. Being told that multiple messages haven’t been posted when they are obviously visible when views in desktop. Seeing duplicates of the same post after you delete the “message couldn’t be posted” prompt. Those same prompts moving to the bottom of the chat each time I open the app so I have to scroll up to view new messages. It’s slowly becoming a nightmare to keep tabs on the servers I’m active in when I’m away from my pc. I don’t care about SpongeBob skins I have to pay for (I have nitro btw) when your mobile app is a broken mess that gets worse with each update. If I hadn’t built my friend groups around discord during covid I would’ve moved apps by now. 

On an unrelated note, tying number of soundboard sounds to server boosts is dumb. If I want more sounds in my server, I shouldn’t need to be popular or have rich friends.",3,240.0,David of the Light,3
us,United States,10668570984,2023-12-07T17:02:26-07:00,Absolutely awful new mobile layout,"Look, I get that Discord is known to get criticized for every new feature they add before people eventually move on because they realize it wasn't that bad (think back to when when they made the logo symmetrical or when they changed the font). But this is the first time in my three years of using Discord that I've genuinely felt that an update made me want to uninstall the app.  Yesterday I'd have rated the app 5 stars, and today I rate it a 2. The app went from great to clunky, messy, and less usable overnight, which makes me wonder: How? How is this even slightly necessary for improving user experience?

I have many complaints, but my biggest issue is that the swiping doesn't make sense anymore. You can swipe right in DMs, but you can't swipe left to make it go back. The members list is now hidden in the oddest place, the message previews in DMs make the layout look incredibly busy, you can no longer open the list of your friends to see people's statuses and who's online, and you can only use the search function to find things in one channel at a time. It's objectively not a good update, and you'll just end up losing current users like myself.

I don't see why this layout couldn't have remained an optional feature like it used to be. The only thing I maybe enjoy about the change is the color, athough that alone is certainly not enough to make this a good update.",2,207,‼️ \(•o•)/,33
us,United States,8218661202,2022-01-08T09:37:57-07:00,"Okay, but mobile keeps glitching","I like Discord because the app allowed me to meet many people and get myself involved with different activities but during texting sometimes the “connecting” makes it glitch and then my messages can’t be sent at all. I could easily leave the app and refresh it but it’s a pain when it happens all the time. I’m afraid one day the app would kick me out and all of my text would disappear, my time wasted. Every update I hope this gets fixed but I heard Discord isn’t very efficient in fixing their app compare to their desktop version. I do update it, but it’s no use when the same issue arises over and over again. Please fix it. It used to not do this before and if I knew this was going to happen I wouldn’t have updated the app. But then that would prevent me from other perks like background gifs and each individual server pfp from Nitro. I’m usually on mobile because of how convenient it is to bring around the house and when I go out so I use it more than desktop. So if Discord could please keep up with the updates on the app as much as the desktop, that would be greatly appreciated. Especially this buffering of sending messages, since it’s an annoying hiccup that keeps coming up despite being small. Otherwise, it’s a great app that has me spending on it even though I told myself I would never spend on an app.",3,106.0,LolaTheAwesomeMii,41
us,United States,4092026245,2019-05-02T17:39:10-07:00,Please read this,"From the very beginning, I have had numerous problems with this app. The only reason I am giving it two stars is because when it does work, it is phenomenal. 
When I first got the app, it wouldn’t let me join the server I wanted to and said I was banned (even though I’d never used the app before). I re-downloaded the app recently because I was joining a clan and they required discord. I got the app and I was still logged into my old account, which was glitched, so I created a new one. I actually had to create that account on my browser because the app didn’t even let me do that. I created my account and tried to login on the app, no success. I’ve re-downloaded the app numerous times since then and still, no success logging in. Luckily, my browser still works and I use that to chat with my clan. Unfortunately, even when I turn my phone sideways, I can’t see all of the writing because it shows all the members of the group on the right hand side and it takes up half of the screen. Then, I have to read downwards one letter at a time and I don’t have the patience for that, especially with all of the scrolling it requires. If I could get on the app and not have to worry about that, I would have no complaints, but this simple fix is ruining the entire app for me. If you want people to use your app, they have to be able to create an account, but so far I haven’t had any luck with that.",3,3.0.0,Snewcomer22,108
us,United States,11852713490,2024-10-19T15:25:20-07:00,New Ui,"I hate this new tedious member list making me have to hit search than members just to DM someone if I need to about something since I’m not going to friend every single person I’m going to talk to and I’ll most likely keep forgetting how to access the new members list since I used the old right scroll for multiple years. Why when I turn off the new Ui tab swiping left on right side of the screen that use to be the members list that I don’t care about anyways or the new stupid reply feature when holding a message worked perfectly fine not just go back to the side scroll for the members list when turned off? It was way faster and made Dming someone super easy now it just annoying and takes me longer for no reason. Also checking to see if a certain person is online or busy on discord became more effort to potentially converse with someone. Let me have the option to view server members by scrolling to the right like before on mobile even if you put it in the settings or something.
The so called help link you sent is straight garbage and saying “it’ll take some getting use to” when the old UI has been thrown away by you guys. I absolutely hate this new UI and would rather have the old UI that seemed to be better in nearly every way in my experience. You had a great UI before and this new one makes me want to use any other messaging app even after using discord for 7 years.",2,251.0,Chris or Paul,1
us,United States,10718182883,2023-12-19T07:59:26-07:00,The latest UI is a step backwards,"The new user interface has a weird flow. It used to be that new direct messages would  appear at the top of your server list, which means you were able to keep your attention on one section of the app. Now direct messages can only be accessed from a separate part of the app that’s accessed from the footer. Now you have to keep your attention not only on the server list to monitor for new activity, but also on the footer, and the footer doesn’t tell you who you’ve received messages from in the same way the old system did (where profile pictures would populate at the top of the server list). Now one must navigate into the direct messages directory in order to see who they’ve received messages from, which takes you out of the familiar Discord interface. You cannot access the server sidebar from here. Before you were able to easily return to the server listing by swiping your direct message to the right, just as you would a server channel. Now swiping away a message reveals the direct messages listing. Now one must take the additional step of tapping on the servers icon in the footer. This may not sound so bad, but it really breaks the seamless flow prior versions of the app had, not only because of the additional inputs, but because of the added spatial and relational complexity. Discord’s UI used to give me the sense that I was in one place, choosing to move things in and out of that place. Now it feels like two places.",1,209.0,Irockman1,29
us,United States,10665116313,2023-12-06T17:05:15-07:00,"Good app, but the recent design decisions have been abhorrent.","I have been using the app since 2016 or 2017. The recent layout update on mobile is extremely counter-intuitive, and they have switched everything around and honestly it just looks way too much like a copy of Instagram. These designers are pretty much sucking what made Discord unique and nice to use out of it, turning it into any other bog standard chatting platform. Recently, they have switched around where the DMs are (which I can understand for accessibility reasons), but have removed the ability to swipe to see member lists of servers and group chats, instead putting that under a button at the top of the screen which is quite counterintuitive and only makes it more annoying to check. Additionally, they have removed the intuitiveness of the DMs part, where you can swipe back and forth--Instead, now you can only swipe back out of a chat and do not get to partly see the chat you were most recently in on the side and swipe back in to quickly respond to a new message. Additionally, clicking on the Messages button also no longer brings you directly back into the chat you were last in, requiring one extra click which becomes really inconvenient if, like me, you often tab between messages and servers. I would love to see this and the other small ease-of-use features added back, they were among my favorite parts of the app and what made it unique to me. All in all, long-time supporter, but just cannot agree with recent executive decisions at all.",1,207,BrayDawg17,0
us,United States,11295910922,2024-05-22T14:00:43-07:00,Each update makes the UI worse,"Exactly as title says. Removal of buttons, removing swipe to see userlist and replacing it with making a thread (which is annoying at best and actively detrimental at worst, especially for those with disabilities), shrinking the size of text, changing the location of server settings, user settings, and user settings WITHIN a server, changing how search functions (you have to click the main server’s search bar to search through the whole server. If you click the search in a channel it exclusively searches that channel. for a while i thought it was now impossible to search an entire server because of how unintuitive this is. The search works worse now, too.).
Most things now require you to click two separate things just to get there, much less actually perform the action you want. Again, this is annoying at best, and actively detrimental at worse. What about people that struggle with fine motor function? What about the visually impaired? Everything is small and inconvenient. It’s way too easy to misclick, or to not know where something is and have to fruitlessly search a bunch of menus just to realize it was somewhere else entirely. The fact Discord keeps changing the location of buttons (and outright removing the dm button from the button of the screen, most recently) certainly doesn’t help. 

I wouldn’t be as upset if there was an option somewhere to use a previous version of the app. Right now I’m stuck using something that apparently tries to be as unusable as possible.",1,230.0,EJEckenrode,0
us,United States,10667854534,2023-12-07T11:45:58-07:00,Yeah okay uhm what,"Usually Discord is great, I’ve had it for several years and it’s pretty great for most things. But this new mobile app style update has got me all messed up. It looks bulky and gross, it seems that discord has fallen victim to the Facebook effect where every (mobile) app tries to look the same. It has its pros but to be blunt it’s not good looking and the interface is hard to use especially with the separate tabs for severs and messages. All of the available options being in separate places makes it feel very bulky and the way calls look now is just honestly bad and the message options/information interface is even worse. I appreciate they are trying to change and the time it must have taken but it’s just outright bad. Discord, like all apps, need bug fixes and such like the status’ being weird, but the actual user interface and styling of the app was simple and easy to use so why it’s been changed is beyond me. (TLDR: new mobile update is bad, otherwise the app has been (/was) great and easy to use. Would be 5 stars if the new mobile update did not exist.) 

-as someone who uses Discord daily and has used Discord for YEARS to form and keep some of the best and strongest relationships (relationships included friendships guys) I’ve ever made/had. 
Thank you for reading.",4,207,Oslo Nicole,12
us,United States,8850615682,2022-07-07T11:06:35-07:00,I understand why it’s 13+ but you also have to understand:,"I understand why this app is 13+ but you have to understand that there are minors who are more mature then most. Like me for example, at the age of 12 I already knew everything there is to know about internet safety and everything about sex. Ex. At the age of 10 I already knew about safety, how to do it properly and everything else. Now these minors of this generation have access the the internet and learn things faster. There could be a 5 year old with the mind and maturity of a 21 year old. These minors are now maturing faster the the people of the older generations because they have access the the internet and can learn things. Also, when someone is reported for being under 13 don’t ban their account. You’re trying to keep minors safe but most just use this platform to make friends and get support. And tbh I’ve been on discord since 9, I’ve only had a few conversation that made me uncomfortable I’m dm’s other then that discord is insanely safe. And if you want to keep it safer maybe look at the reports people put on accounts. Please consider lowering the age limit to 11+. I want my child to be able to come on here because he’s mature enough to do so. I didn’t teach him any of these things but he found out due to the internet and honestly he doesn’t care. I want to be able to have my 12 year old make friends from all over but your age limits stop that. Please consider this, you should have already though about how these new generations are already maturing at the age they get a phone. You can’t protect everyone and you have to understand that.",3,134.0,Xanthus.,0
us,United States,10771743012,2024-01-01T10:52:53-07:00,Mobile UI Change,"The new Discord app UI is user unfriendly, unintuitive, and even harmful to light-sensitive users. The new dark theme causes headaches because of the poorly balanced contrast. Navigating the app feels clunky and slow, and makes me frustrated trying to talk to friends and stay on top of conversations in servers. Why have reply be an option in two places: swiping right AND in the tap and hold menu on messages? When on voice, an annoying square pops up and covers part of the UI instead of it being a single swipe away. Losing the easily accessible server members online screen makes me feel like I’ve lost that sense of community that Discord in the past has so well fostered. Why is the reply feature given priority over an entire side menu when it has another place it already exists? I don’t reply to others that often to use the swipe, and so far it has only made me frustrated that it keeps popping up instead of ever feeling convenient. If I had Nitro I would have cancelled it, and as it is I’m advising my friends who pay for it to cancel because of their own disappointment in the app. I used to love this app, I used it every day, but now I’m going to stay signed in on a mobile browser and use that instead. There was an easy switch between mobile and desktop and one time, matching UIs that were easy to understand and use, and now if anything changes in the desktop UI I know I will bring my business somewhere else. Please, please think of your light sensitive users and those of us who love your app.",1,209.0,omizin,1
us,United States,10674641105,2023-12-09T06:45:35-07:00,New Update,"I’ve had discord for almost a year now, this update is the worst update since I’ve gotten discord! It’s ugly, it’s sm harder to see users in servers I’m in, when I tried to look for pinned messages it’s glitched and they don’t show up, it’s really confusing and just excess buttons everywhere. Discord lost it’s uniqueness! It looks like every other chat app now and trust me that’s not a good thing! Plus I am someone who makes and has made many servers before and the way you took away the feature to add channels without going into server settings is confusing and terrible. And DON’T get me started on the new role icons they look lazy! Also as a server creator, you still haven’t added the feature on mobile how to view the server from different roles and I don’t have my computer around me at all times of the day and this has caused me many issues when I release my servers and stuff. Also my discord is automatically going to midnight theme which is too dark for me and it won’t change to dark. Lastly I don’t know if this is a glitch or not but, the way it now reorganizes my servers without me doing anything in them! I will chat in a server and it’ll automatically move to the top and some servers I really don’t talk in much and I don’t want them on the top! Listen I am a very active user, I basically am on discord 24/7, this is my main chat app to connect me, my friends, and my community and idk what to really do anymore as it’s now very difficult to use the app!",1,207,narlie111,14
us,United States,7868244460,2021-10-02T00:23:01-07:00,Issues/maybe add-ins,"I love using discord, great to talk to friends on here, but i have one problem is that whenever I’m on call with my friends and I’m away from my phone either they wanna call a group chat or someone calls me I don’t hear it saying that this person or group chat name is calling me and I never know until I go to my phone and notice it later that someone call me or I have to manually go back to my phone and join the call, I don’t know if it’s just me but it’s been happening for a while and when I’m not in a call and off of discord and someone calls me I hear it saying that this person is calling me, just not when I’m already in a call, which it did before. Also I think maybe they could add in where we can record our private or group chat calls to like record for memories or something cause you’d always want to remember those moments and I know you can in servers but not in private calls, which I think it should, to record the funny moments going on and not just audio but maybe record when we turn our cams to cause we all be doing funny things and also for security too if someone calls someone in private chat and keep harassing a lot of people and need to record the audio or camera too incase if they do have their camera on and doing something wrong.",4,93.0,chicken nuggies 3826,12
us,United States,14242203918,2026-06-29T12:38:24-07:00,The Absolute Gold Standard of Chat Apps (5/5 Stars),"Discord easily earns a full 5-star rating for completely revolutionizing how we connect and build communities online. Its brilliant server design allows you to organize different topics into dedicated text channels and low-latency voice rooms with absolute ease. Whether I am hopping into a quick screen-share session with friends or managing a massive public group, the platform handles it all flawlessly. The crystal-clear audio and video quality make virtual hangouts feel incredibly seamless and responsive. I also love the endless selection of custom bots, which effortlessly handle everything from playing music to automated moderation. While the dense interface can have a slight learning curve for total beginners, it quickly becomes incredibly intuitive to navigate. It is amazing that the core free experience is so incredibly robust, never forcing you behind an annoying paywall just to talk to your friends. It also runs flawlessly across PC, mobile, and consoles, keeping everyone synced up no matter what device they are using. Ultimately, Discord sets the absolute gold standard for modern communication, making it an essential download that I cannot recommend highly enough.
5 stars",5,335.0,2017loric@ gmail .com,1
us,United States,10759055690,2023-12-29T07:04:17-07:00,Discord’s Doom,"Discord was fine before, I don’t know why they bothered to take this unnecessary action. Before I never got bots/spammers somehow adding my account even though there’s no suggestions on adding accounts like Snapchat for example. Even so I still shouldn’t even be getting added by said bots/spammers because there’s this safety thing they make you do to verify if you’re not a bot which is completely useless I’m already seeing because even apparently bots can bypass it. The main issue is that I can’t even use my Discord account because they are forcing me to “change” my email that I didn’t even put in because I registered with my phone number, and they’re saying that my email is somehow already registered when I’m putting in my email and password to verify. I don’t remember registering in with my email and I’m pretty sure I never did. Also I don’t understand why/how putting in my email (personal information) on my Discord account is going to protect me from bots/spammers. I read on why/how but it still didn’t make any sense. In the old version I never put in my email like I said before and I didn’t get any bots/spammers like I said before as well. They made this app absolutely awful and I recommend not downloading this app unless you want to share your personal information to the world because that’s apparently what they want you to do and that’s their definition of “protection”. Developers, you have a lot of fixing and/or explaining to do.",1,209.0,LocoLobo666,5
us,United States,10668268571,2023-12-07T14:45:18-07:00,If it’s not broken don’t fix it.,"I really do not understand why discord even changed their ui but here we are. In all 5 years I have been on discord, over 1826 days, I have not once ever seen anyone complain about how the ui works. It was fine the way it was. In the beta for this you were able to switch back to the original but I don’t see why they removed the option to switch back. It over complicates so many things which were once able to be done in one swipe and a tap. Searching for stuff is absolutely horrific to do, it’s very glitchy sometimes and I had troubles looking up messages from certain people. It used to take about 8 seconds to search something up but now it feels like it takes forever. Checking dm lists is very overwhelming as well, it feels like it’s popping out of the screen and scooping my eyes out with a metal spoon. The color change is an odd choice as well, again, I’ve never once see someone complain about the color of dark mode. I feel like the new dark mode is too dark, especially since there’s a night mode which is basically pitch black.

 If you want to change the ui, at least give people a break or listen to people’s complaints. When this ui was in beta I did not see one good thing about said from other people. People looked at it for about a minute, complained to someone about how weird it looked, then left it to be forgotten. Save your developer’s time and don’t fix things that aren’t broken.",1,207,Prettykittens,13
us,United States,10661133611,2023-12-05T13:02:23-07:00,The new layout.,"I’m going to start this off by saying, I love Discord. I love using it and it has always been one of my go to apps. But, the new layout is not good. And saying it is not good is an understatement. Hence why I give this review only 2 stars. The only reason I have given this review 2 stars and not 1 or no stars at all is because of my respect for Discord. Previously, I would’ve given it all 5 stars, but with the recent update with the new layout it has lost most of my respect. The new layout looks trashy and has made Discord lose its unique charm. Previously, before the new layout update, Discord was unique, aesthetically pleasing, and easy to navigate, but with the new layout it looks tacky, trashy, it is difficult to understand and navigate, and most importantly, it has caused Discord to loose it’s unique touch. Now Discord looks like every other social media app you come across, and that is disappointing and a disgrace. When I first started using Discord (around 2 years ago) it was easy to learn how to use it and I really liked how it looked, as in, it looked different from other apps, but now I find it extremely difficult to navigate the app, and as someone who has used Discord for that long I should not have that issue under any circumstance. My best recommendation is to make it so that the new layout is an option. So that users can enjoy Discord in the layout they prefer. Making everyone use the same layout when a big majority of us don’t even like the new layout makes us feel as if we are trapped in a prison cell.",2,207,aph.imperial.llamas,0
us,United States,11710704680,2024-09-10T15:14:46-07:00,Good app,"Discord is a versatile communication platform that excels in fostering community and collaboration. Its combination of text, voice, and video chat features allows users to connect in various ways, whether through casual conversations or organized meetings. The app supports creating and managing multiple servers, which can be tailored with channels and roles to suit different interests or projects. Additionally, Discord integrates with various bots and tools to enhance functionality, making it a robust choice for gaming groups, study communities, or professional teams. Its user-friendly interface and strong focus on community-building make it an excellent choice for diverse communication needs. With these pros, though comes multiple flaws and downsides including latency problems, lack of more free servers, and voice chat system being flawed. With the latency issues, discord can be at times frustrating for its customers. Many times have I lagged while on call with companions. Further more, the calling and voice chat system has experienced multiple flaws throughout its history. Some of these include poor audio quality, lag in voices/ static voice, and the occasional kicking out of voice chats. Finally, the freedom of customers has been restrained by the devs ever since the beginning of this apps creation.",4,245.0,Poppfartsmella69,0
us,United States,11140780390,2024-04-09T18:52:45-07:00,Please read this Developer/Community service,"This reason for this 1star is because i’m very dissatisfied. My friend provided the things she needed for her account to be appealed. And she was falsely accused of fraud. Even the people that reported apologized and stated that it was the wrong person. So i don’t understand why y'all don’t have the ability to make her have her account back and she’s very sad. Most people made friends and memories in this app and even I did, and i’m sad to see that she can’t go back in the messages to see that. And it’s disappointing to know that you’ll couldn’t even help other appeal their accounts when falsely accused of something. And it’s disappointing to see my friend crying and still crying now. It hurts to see that. And knowing i cant do much but what i know is that i can make a comment and share what just happened.  Maybe you could try and actually help the discord community with situations like this because it seems like you guys lack helping people who actually want their accounts back more than people reporting an account that has been falsely accused of fraud. Even with evidence of it being true that that account wasn’t the one that caused it. I’m just very disappointed and sad to see my loved ones not being able to see and look in the past memories. I hope this comment helps you do better in the future. Because you might end up being the reason why some people get depression. I hope you have a nice day.",1,224.0,RubyTe,1
us,United States,10689845668,2023-12-13T05:44:04-07:00,The new UI is bad,"The old UI was easy to navigate. You could actually leave the search menu  easily and enter it again. The search menu actually worked. The search menu showed your previous search history and let you simply tap on one search in it to search that same thing again. The old UI had a similar feel to the desktop app. The new UI is difficult to navigate. I find myself having to leave the app and reenter it every time I enter the search menu because I cannot figure out how to leave it otherwise (if there even is a way). It doesn't show your search history anymore, and doesn't show the most recent messages. The desktop app doesn't feel the same as the mobile app anymore, especially since the search menu actually works on desktop. I frequently find myself needing to look back on messages in different channels at the same time by the same person on a server for multiple reasons, including but not limited to, checking an IRL friend of mine's messages to be sure he isn't suicidal because he had a depressive episode last year and stopped going to school for a bit. He's fine now, but I don't want to be forced to use a crappy system that doesn't work to check his discord messages and directly ask him how he's doing when his phone cannot receive my texts or calls if it ever happens again and I don't have access to my laptop.",2,208.0,GD Tomboy,11
us,United States,10667076314,2023-12-07T06:59:50-07:00,New UI Update,"I absolutely hate that the messages like group chats and DMs are in a different tab than servers now. there was absolutely nothing broken about the way that it was laid out and displayed before, so there's no reason to ""fix"" it!! I also am sorely missing the ability to swipe left to look at all members of a server, the having to click on the top feels clunky and visually unpleasant. I hate being taken to an entirely different screen just to see who's online! it's an entirely unnecessary extra step that helps no one. the idea of ""prioritizing messaging"" by putting private messages and group chats in a tab seperate from servers is completely asinine when discord as a whole is a messaging service in and of itself! also, it's a small aesthetic change but rounding the corners of the servers when swiping to look at the servers at the side is unnecessary and unwelcome and overall incredibly displeasing to look at. speaking of swiping, making it so swiping left creates a reply to a message is the most unnecessary, confusing, and almost MALICIOUS feeling change yet, especially when swiping left had an entirely different function before. please listen to your user base and stop making so many changes that absolutely NO ONE is actually asking for and actively make the user experience worse. you have a good app, it is not broken, stop trying to fix things that don't need to be changed because you've continually only made things worse.",1,207,Gatlii,8
us,United States,10668851335,2023-12-07T19:05:23-07:00,overwhelming and disorienting new layout,"My main issue is the new layout. Everything is spread out and hidden away in other tabs and buttons making it very overwhelming. Discord is trying to hard to be like other social platforms when it doesn't need to. The old layout worked wonderfully with this new one just being a ripoff of imessages. It might work for other sites but for discord it is completely unnecessary. The size everything takes up is far more for no additional amount of information. The new update makes finding members annoying. Before you could just swipe left and see all the members of a group chat or server. Now it's hidden away at the top which is unnecessary. Not only is it an useless change but the members list is way bigger. This makes it look overwhelming searching for people. The main feature that this update takes away from is the search button. Before it was clear and easy to search for whatever you needed. Now it is more disorganized and unnecessary. My main issue is that you can not search in the entire server anymore and is limited to one channel at a time. This is a major flaw that takes away from the fluidity of the search feature. For servers with many channels, which is most of them, it is a pain to find what you were looking for. It would be gladly appreciated if you would reconsider these flaws to optimize our user experience on discord to make it a better app.",1,207,miyurii,11
us,United States,10668215596,2023-12-07T14:21:15-07:00,New Mobile layout,"I get your trying to make the new Discord layout more convenient for everyone, but some people find the old layout more convenient than this one. This update isn't like your other discord updates that have minor fixes and upgrades, this completely revamped how things work on discord. Layout is very important for any app company to have it efficient and convenient for users. I know this is what you tried to do but it really isnt doing well. The discord layout has been the same for a very ling time and a sudden change like this makes it seem very clunky and annoying. I hate how all the notifications and everything are so up front and big as well as the buttons. The new layout completely ruins the uniqueness that many people liked about the old Discord layout. The new layout looks a lot like other social media layouts and is incredibly off putting as the old discord layout was very iconic. If you were going to make such a sudden change like this at least give us the opportunity to switch layouts like you had in a previous version. Another thing worth noting would be when you slide to the side to see who in a server is online and what roles they have, that was before but now you have to slide up which is way less convenient. Overall all Im saying is that removing the option to switch between the layouts seems like an inconvenience to many people as this new layout is incredibly crowded and clunky.",1,207,a worried stormtrooper,7
us,United States,8932350005,2022-07-31T19:02:26-07:00,Great app except for a couple of issues,"I’ve been using Discord for quite a while now and overall it’s a really good app. However, although it’s mostly accessible with screen readers it needs some improvements. For one, when a person sends a text even if they wind down a couple of times it’ll still read the text as one complete block. This is a problem because for super long posts it is really hard to read the whole thing. The second problem is that when using voiceover if you try to move the cursor automatically jumps to the button to exit the channel you are in. For me at least, this can make it very difficult to scroll through the channels messages and it’ll do this while I’m trying to write a message as well. Again, overall really good app and I’m so glad that I downloaded it because it has helped me connect with all of my friends. Edits. Thank you so much discord for fixing see bug with the screen readers. I guess that the paragraph thing is a little bit harder to do so I’m not even going to complain about that. If you can fix it eventually great, if not that’s completely fine and what you’ve done so far with fixing the buttons has been great. Thank you so much for creating this app that’s provided me with so many great experiences.",4,137.0,🦅🐷🐨gg,4
us,United States,7820701032,2021-09-18T17:48:22-07:00,This discord talent show should be shut down,"So these people were making a discord talent show and when my sister was up she was in the middle of talking and they stopped her. They said “alright have a nice day thank you for coming!” And my sister was so sad. We actually arranged at this certain time to go to a talent show together and I was there to support them so they were gonna tell dad jokes together. So like they’re here calling me just upset and embarrassed sad, and I already reported the discord server. I’m livi#5618 reporting the server and can u please shut it down. Me and my friends weren’t the only one experiencing this bad disrespectful behavior, this guy was complaining about how they kicked his friend out and I heard them kick a lot of people out while they were talking. I’m just thinking: give them some time to talk! I reported livi#5618 that’s me, so I hope u the server I reported as well. I was super mad about it and right now I think they’re kicking out more people. Please shut it down and give them a warning because this behavior is not respectful and for the first time I hate one of these talent shows. I think a lot of people are upset about this to and honestly I’m not gonna accept this. I don’t know if they’re gonna make another one just shut it down please. Thank you!",4,91.0,crazy cracie,12
us,United States,11108398212,2024-03-31T22:00:10-07:00,Okay but always bugs,"I love the idea of discord and it is my primary communication choice when gaming or on my pc. However, every update brings more and more bugs that just never seem to get fixed. Some of the most frustrated bugs/features right now are when you are in a video call on mobile and leave the app or leave the full screened mode and then return to the call it makes your camera the full screen and your friend the smaller one. Then double tapping their picture doesn’t always make them bigger you have to double tap then click the full screen button. It’s really annoying. There has also been a bug that causes the camera to be upside down and you can’t even lock your phone and flip it over because it’ll change the rotation anyway. Now, if I have discord open I. The back ground for too long and go on to it to make a call, it freezes and I have to completely restart it. Besides the bugs, there have been some unnecessary changes that really lowered the quality of life the app has. Like changing your video from a rectangle shape to a square… now I can’t tell what is in frame unless I make myself the full screen video… definitely a great idea of an app but I just feel like every time I use it I say “I hate discord” right when I get in a call because of all of these challenges.",3,221.0,Paige182,1
us,United States,8342110079,2022-02-10T19:28:13-07:00,No customer service,"I will start this review by saying that I haven’t actually been able to use discord. I downloaded the app for a school class but when prompted to verify my number, it wouldn’t accept it because it was linked with another account. So, I went through the process of trying to find an account I had created years prior. In the meantime I contacted support and got a very quick robot response telling me to do exactly what I had just done. I found the old accounts and deleted them. However, that wasn’t enough. Apparently when you press delete on an account it takes an additional 14 days before discord actually deletes it. A day later, support for back to me and told me that I needed to send a copy of the error message I was receiving (even though I had already stated it in the last email). So I did. And a day later I still have received no response. I had to sort this issue out myself and eventually found that simply deleting the account wouldn’t remove the phone number associated with it. Finally to remove a phone number from an account I had to add ANOTHER email in the process - further convoluting the account issue. And finally, after 20 to 30 “account verifications”, 4 password resets, zero help from discord- I had access to a discord account. A whole 3 days later. All of this could’ve been resolved if I had access to someone at discord who knew a lick about user accounts and how to immediately delete them.",1,113.0,fuqmyassunderarmor,10
us,United States,10677669671,2023-12-10T01:25:57-07:00,Change for the sake of change.,"I’ve been using discord for about 5-6ish years now and it’s been home to a ton of great friendships and stories, or rather, it’s been my home on the internet if you will. I appreciate some of the new features that were added in the latest update, but it also feels like Discord is loosing its identity and is now trying to be like the various other chat platforms available across the AppStore. The iconic grey was changed to a boring blueish color that makes the app have some visual accessibility issues in many places. The intuitive card layout from before is now broken with swipe gestures for the reply feature. I think some of this is just because it’s hard to get used to change, but I really feel like discord is changing things away from what their initial experience was. It used to be home, and now I see no reason to use it over something like telegram or Snapchat, seeing as it’s trying to just be some other chat app. 

Devs at Discord, thank you for the work you’ve put in. I appreciate all the little animations and how hard you’ve probably worked on this, but creating so much change all at once was not the way to do it. A great way to fix this all would be to add more personalization to the app in settings; a toggle to go back to the old grey color for people who have a hard time reading with this new one, a toggle to switch layouts, something like that. I think there’s a fine line between keeping the charm of discord and making it be just a boring old chat app that people don’t want to use, and you’re certainly leaning towards the latter half right now.",2,207,aleconline,0
us,United States,1906883178,2017-11-08T13:12:41-07:00,Keeps crashing and marking unread messages as read.,"I like Discord for what it offers, but the iOS app crashes randomly whenever I try to load a picture, gif, song, or other upload someone else posted, and crashes when I try to post pictures quite frequently. I know that a lot of people upload stuff, so the fact that it crashes as often as it does is a major concern for me. 

Another issue is that the app has decided to randomly mark all messages in random chat channels as read when I open them, even though I’ve still got dozens to read before I reach the end of the string. Or I’ll be reading the messages, and suddenly it marked all messages as read, to include ones that happen while I’m reading, and not even remotely caught up. It happens randomly, so I don’t even know what might be the issue. It might happen to a chat every time I open it, or just once in a while but it’s a bug I want to see gone. Being tagged in a message, and then having that indicator removed randomly is an issue. I don’t always have time to read everything in one sitting, so I want to be assured that I can read it later. It is a major issue when it starts you over at the end of the conversation, and doesn’t save from where you had to leave off. (This is mostly for my admin duties on servers.)

I like that I have the ability to take Discord with me, but if I can’t use it half the time, then it’s like I don’t even have it at all.",2,1.9.5,Gorogokvi,92
us,United States,13519245526,2025-12-15T23:35:40-07:00,Boring app 👍🏼,"They messed up when they added verification and limited system I see the future of discord will be down in the near future if they don’t remove the limiter and verification and just have a face verification checker would be much better instead of ID. Like a face checker that can know if you’re a real person or not by going left or right like how Instagram does it. We should go back to 2018 discord version where it was the most highest and popular at that time. I could send over 1,000 friend requests without getting my account limited or muted for spam because adding random people shouldn’t be a cause for spam just spamming direct messages should be a cause of spam. Now this will be the biggest issue why no one will use discord in the year of 2028 is my prediction. I hope discord takes this feedback and let us go back to the 2018 version it was very good I loved back then how I can send unlimited friend requests without having my account limited or muted. Such as I need to for my businesses like making music or gaming. Or collaboration on creating servers. If discord doesn’t take this feedback seriously then my prediction will say discord will be ending up like that one application KIK absolutely fumbled. Come on Discord if you want to make it up in the stocks bring back unlimited friend requests without account being limited or muted. Same goes for when you join other servers.  A big issue is when I join multiple issue I get muted for 24 hours lol. Fix this and your rating will go up 5.5 i guarantee it.",1,309.0,Reviewkingnow,1
us,United States,7528310444,2021-07-01T13:50:03-07:00,Recent problems,"I’ve been using discord for about 2 years now and recently I’ve been having multiple problems, be it screen share not working as intended and closing my application, over heating problems or discord closing while I’m in other apps. Usually I fixed these problems by just redownloading the app, but just yesterday it wouldn’t even let me open discord after redownloading it and so I thought “maybe it’ll work after I shut down my phone and it that doesn’t work I’ll wait until tomorrow.” Now today the app doesn’t open so I try redownloading it and it still does not open, (by the way when I mean the app doesn’t open, I mean that it gets stuck in a loading type animation and no matter how long I wait it seems to be infinite) so now I’m sitting here writing about the recent problems discord has been having and asking if the developers are even caring about mobile discord or is it really just a case where I should just get a mic and use discord on my pc.

Despite my 3 star score I’ve still used discord for 2 - 3 years and it’s always been working as intended and it’s worked well up until like 8 months ago. Maybe this is just a problem with my phone despite me having an iPhone XS Max, maybe it’s just an iOS side problem, but discord team keep up the work maybe you’ll find a fix.
Thank You",3,80.0,i hate loading screens,11
us,United States,5928870861,2020-05-10T13:06:47-07:00,"Amazing, with several missing opportunities","Discord is a great app, as I myself have been using it since 2018, and it hasn't given me any problems. However, there are some things I wish Discord had that it currently doesn't. Here's some I could think of:
-In servers it would be great if you could mention a role without the person(s) that have that role being notified (maybe a different prefix, like $).
-If, for example, I want to ping people with a certain assortment of roles, such as Moderators that are online at the moment, or Friends that are also Server Boosters. Some way to combine role pings to capture the attention of a more precise bracket of people would be nice.
-I'm in so many servers that it's extremely difficult to navigate through each of them, even with folders. I really think there should be an option to lower the size of server icons, and a new folder functionality, instead of appearing on the same row as others, servers in open folders would travel to the right of other servers, giving space to be able to see every server and navigate with ease
-Slightly similar to the previous point, but there should be an option to make channel tabs smaller. Same reason.",5,20.0,LacroixWasTaken,8
us,United States,12102339470,2024-12-24T18:27:28-07:00,Great app but.....,"I got this app roughly a year ago and it is great, you can connect to any counity you want and even create your own server if you are selling or promoting something. On the other hand, there are things called ""server nukes"" or some people call it ""raids"" and basically people will join into your server abd somehow gain permissions to edit channels and completely destroy your server. There are easy ways to protect against this like adding security apps but I won't get into that. My main problem is how many payments are required for basic work, if you want to send a file larger than 10mb then you have to buy discord nitro which isn't cheap, along with that you have to buy discord nitro in order to customize your profile and make it more like your style. Another issue is ""server boosting"", if you want to unlock special perks for your server, you or other people can boost your server and reach different levels that unlock special features for your server. Not that bad right? Wrong. Each boost runs out after a very short amount of time and boosting costs quite a bit, this means that it would cost like $100 a month to maintain your server perks. Overall it is a good app if you are just looking to find a certain community and talk to people.",4,259.1,Emerson B White,0
us,United States,10665770385,2023-12-06T22:13:47-07:00,Stop trying to fix things that aren’t broken. Horrendous mobile update.,"Your original mobile design was flawless. It was easy to navigate through servers, view who is in each server, and message in dms. I found it extremely impressive how well the desktop app translated into the mobile app. This has been my number one go to messaging app, and I gladly support this company by paying for a subscription because I cherish it so much. Now you all just went ahead and ruined it with the new mobile layout and desktop icon designs. What was the reason? Your users are accustomed to using your app in a certain way and they continue to use it because they like the way it’s formatted. The reason we use this app is because of its seamless navigation, intuitive organization, and uniqueness compared to other messaging apps. You took what makes you special and threw it into a dumpster before setting it on fire. The same goes for your icons on desktop. At first glance I could immediately register what each icon was. Their designs were pleasing to the eye, but the new designs are absolutely atrocious. Not every icon needs to be rounded and simplified. The old ones had character and clean crisp lines. I’m not sure why you guys insist on making these “improvements” instead of listening to what your users actually want and putting your time and money into exploring that. I do hope that this company does thorough user testing before releasing new updates, reverts the mobile update, and takes their users opinions into consideration when moving forward with changes.",1,207,MaxRuinedMyDay,0
us,United States,10668173198,2023-12-07T14:02:13-07:00,The new UI update ruins this app,"I’ve used discord since the start of 2018 and I’ve gone through all the ups and downs of this platform, but throughout the entire course of using it, this is the first time I’m considering completely abandoning it and getting all my friends to make the switch to something like Guilded. The UI has changed almost entirely, the backdrop color changed from a easy on the eyes grey to an extremely harsh dark blue. You can no longer swipe left to see the members list, now you must press on the search icon (for God knows why??) to see it and then it seems there’s no way to exit that screen other than jumping to a message someone sent or that was pinned. Instead, swiping left now replies to messages, which is very unnecessary as you can just hold tap on a message and press reply—very little of the time do I actually need to reply to a message to even need a quicker action for it, as most conversations flow naturally with very few uses of the reply feature. The friends list has been moved completely, which isn’t the worst thing, but it’s just more inconvenient and unnecessary. I haven’t tried streaming or voice calls yet since this change, but I imagine they’ve been messed with as well. Frankly, the app just makes me feel incredibly claustrophobic now and it’s so infuriating to use now. If they reverse the UI update, I will bump this up to 5 stars, as the app has been great until now.",1,207,LeEpicDoge27,30
us,United States,9735598641,2023-03-20T22:48:53-07:00,Big problems for motion sensitivity.,"I use discord on mobile because it's often inconvenient to get to a PC, and while it is adequate for sending a message in a pinch; there are some meaningful shortcomings. I am someone who is sensitive to things moving on my phone screen outside my control. I needs gifs to not autoplay, and if the screen jumps around at random, it is stressful, almost painful. On gifs, fortunately discord delivers. Unfortunately, it does so by disabling gifs entirely. Even when I tap on a gif to look at it, it still doesn't play 90% of the time, so in exchange for having a useable client, I can't see the contents of a gif, even when I want to. That's problem number one. The big issue comes up when I want to read a message in a channel in which users are actively posting. Every time a message comes in, my scroll position in the channel moves wildly, up or down, seemingly at random. It makes it literally impossible to read anything in a channel, unless the channel has no current activity. This to me is unacceptable. At no point should I be interrupted from reading something by the text suddenly moving, let alone moving entire page-lengths off of the screen in an unpredictable direction. This has been an issue for years, and somehow it has never been addressed. Gives the impression that the mobile client, and accessibility, are not priorities.",2,169.0,physicssquirrel,2
us,United States,10668033050,2023-12-07T13:00:01-07:00,New update was unnecessary and it hurts my brain,"I’ve been using discord for years. I love discord and it’s my main way of messaging. I love the original layout. My only complaint was that there wasn’t a good purple option for nitro themes. And I certainly had no issues with the original mobile version. This new update is trying a bit too hard to look fancy and I really just don’t like it. Not everything has to have round bubble boxes. Changing the channel symbol to be ‘Aa’ instead of ‘#’ is so weird. At least change it to another symbol like ‘-‘. Not letters. The swipe left to reply is so annoying and I can’t for the life of me figure out how to view the online members. It’s way too different, it hurts my head, I don’t like it.

It’s so much less streamline now and it’s just- eugh. I know companies rarely revert an update, especially one as large as this, but I really want the old one back. It was easier to look at, it was nice and streamline, it was simple. This is way too bubbly, it’s trying too hard, and it just doesn’t look like discord anymore. Opening discord makes me anxious now and *please* at *least* give us the option to have this version or the old one, I am begging you 🙏

It’s so different and hard on the neurodivergent brain ;-;",4,207,BooperDooper999,1
us,United States,8349110889,2022-02-12T16:27:09-07:00,Great Website!,"Discord has been incredible for me, I have been able to talk to and call friends, connect with new people, and it all has been very private and  secure. 
At first, I was a little bit superstitious when it came to discord. It did seem like a very open messaging service, leading to incidents with cyber bullies/child predators. Since getting discord, all of these worries have basically vanished. It is a high quality messaging and calling service (especially for large groups), and it can also serve as a way to meet new people. In my experience, I have stayed on private servers and direct messages with my friends, but I have still gotten a ton of usage out of the app. 
I highly recommend this app to anyone looking for a nice voice calling or messaging service. I would also like to mention to any parents who are nervous to allow their kids to use this to at least give it a chance. If your child stays in groups with just his friends, they will be absolutely safe, and if they do go into a public server, I have found that people are generally very nice. Plus, if you do get into a situation that is uncomfortable, you can simply leave the group or block the caller. 
I hope this helps!",5,113.0,Deco_Urchin,2
us,United States,14000769451,2026-04-26T17:40:17-07:00,Every Update makes everything worse,"I use this app all the time. I’d rate it 5 stars. But something that makes me infuriatingly mad every time is when I update discord, they change every piece of UI, every color, every location where a button used to be, every font, and it ALWAYS is worse. I don’t know how you can make so many bad changes in a row. It seems statistically unlikely but discord pulls through every time to deliver the worst product possible.

Awhile back I started getting notifications every time anyone I was friends with changed their profile picture or status. It wasn’t possible to turn those off without updating. So I updated and I wish I didn’t. I wish I just turned off all notifications for discord. That would be a better solution. Because now all the buttons are in different places. It takes more clicks to get to the settings menu. I can’t find my inbox. The colors are garish and the high contrast hurts my eyes. There are more buttons and tabs that I will never use taking up screen space. I had just gotten used to the fact that you had to scroll up for the search bar to appear, and now it’s a permanent fixture, taking up space? Seriously! What were you guys thinking? 
The colors are my biggest issue. I don’t even want a fancy multi-color nitro background. I just want a grey background between light and dark. The App Store has more pleasant UI than you, discord. Do better.",1,325.0,Q4hehe,0
us,United States,12840967600,2025-07-01T15:04:28-07:00,Consistently worse with each update serious privacy issues.,"I use discord 15+ hours a day and I will say that the mobile version for the iPhone is incredibly broken. I have been using discord on iOS for over a year now and every update it gets worse. The app will consistently mute and unmute me while my phone is across the room, mid conversation. If I have my headphones in and I get a phone call, it will unmute me in discord with no notification sound whatsoever. The number of times that I have had full conversations with people in my household, being completely unaware that everyone in discord could hear me because the app decided to unmute me, is ridiculously high. Half the time I open the app the audio output setting to change to the speakerphone is not even visible or available as a drop-down option and I have to force close the application, or completely restart my phone in order to get the speaker option to appear. The app consistently tries to switch to my mobile data, even though I am in my house with 100% Wi-Fi coverage. I have no issues with any other app, whether I’m using my headphones or not, and no issues with any other app losing signal, but discord is consistently unable to function on a basic level.

I am using a brand new iPhone, and without being able to replicate these issues through any other app, on top of hearing all of my friends in discord who use iPhones complain about the same issues on a daily basis, it’s apparent that the app has serious issues. The privacy issue with the app unmuting on its own, randomly, is a serious concern.",1,286.0,JBWainwright,0
us,United States,12161514663,2025-01-08T17:30:32-07:00,I really love this app,"I absolutely love Discord because it’s the perfect platform for staying connected with my friends, family, and communities. Whether I’m chatting with close friends in private voice channels or hanging out with like-minded people in public servers, it feels like a place where I can truly be myself. The ease of use and versatility of Discord are unmatched whether I’m gaming, collaborating on a project, or just catching up on life, the experience is seamless. I can drop into a conversation at any time, knowing that there are so many ways to communicate, whether through text, voice, or video. 

What really makes Discord stand out is the way it blends socializing with customization. From creating my own servers to tweaking settings for a more personalized experience, there’s so much flexibility in how I organize my interactions. The ability to create channels for specific topics or interests means I can keep conversations organized and clutter-free. Plus, the bots, integrations, and unique features like screen sharing or live streaming make it even more enjoyable. Discord isn't just a chat app it's a community hub, and it’s become an essential part of how I connect, learn, and share with others. ❤️",5,261.0,"Himari, sincerely",0
us,United States,7874983853,2021-10-03T17:55:53-07:00,Disabled My Account Because I canceled my nitro subscription!,"I’ve used discord for a very long time, for 5 years and I really enjoyed using it until I my account had gotten disabled because I decided to cancel my 3 month free nitro subscription. I had canceled because I didn’t really have a need for the subscription. I was rarely on and never really used the perks of their nitro. I had canceled my subscription on September 22nd 2021 and didn’t think they were gonna charge me, but I had checked my bank account to find out they did. I waited a few days thinking maybe it was on an accident and they’ll refund me my money but I had seen they didn’t. On September 25th I had put the request for a refund and got approved. As soon as that happened my account was immediately disabled and I wasn’t able to access it anymore. I contacted discord support to see what the reason why and explained what had happened but they insisted that I had broke their terms of service because I didn’t let them charge me for a subscription I had canceled. 
I had some of my best friends on there and was in a lot of really cool communities and it’s an utter shame that I will never be able to communicate with them again because of their poor customer service and api.
Don’t use discord, they’ll disable and ban your account because they have bad api and customer service won’t listen to what you have to say because they feel like it superior to you.",1,93.0,A PIMP who Loves JP/JW,23
us,United States,11943968291,2024-11-12T20:31:33-07:00,"please fix this, it’s getting to the point i cannot stand discord anymore.","i love discord so much. it’s my main communication platform, i’m autistic so being able to organize my conversations is really great, me and my partner have a server just w each other and me and my best friend also have one and it helps to break things up.
however discord has been SO bad recently. on my laptop it kicks me out every like 5 mins, it’s gotten to the point where it wakes me up in the middle of the night because of the stupid disconnection sound, but everything else works fine so it’s not my wifi, on my phone it will make it to where it won’t even let me enter the call, my bf will be in call and i click it and it does nothing, now when i try to enter a call it completely shuts down the app and CLOSES out the app. along w that, every once and awhile the font sizes will be messed up, i have a hard time reading so my default size is bigger but every once in a while i’ll open discord and the channel names will be HUGE but the actual text will be small. i’ve tried everything to fix it, restarting my phone, restarting my font size settings, changing my font size settings only on discord- the only thing that fixes it is time. i literally just have to wait it out. please PLEASE whatever you guys did- un do it because i never used to have these issues.",2,254.0,grey bonds,0
us,United States,9088580788,2022-09-15T15:52:00-07:00,The support team when it comes to reporting people is lacking,"I was in a discord server that had a rule stating the owner (who is also the admin) is the “dictator” of the server and said that rule was the reason why he could do anything. That rule wasn’t really concerning at first because there was no big instance of him abusing the rule at first. Over time, there were instances here and there of some concern. Things like him spamming, and the entire server spamming. And once he was done with the spam, he would kick a group of people. And others like one day every voice chat except for one was removed from view, and everyone was muted in that one vc (reason why is because this vc was designed so only the mods and the owner can talk). But, he would do more concerning things like making fun of people who Dmed him by blocking them, taking a screenshot of the dm, and posting the dm in the server for everyone to make fun of. The owner has also timed out people for an entire week for dumb reasons like someone calling him William Afton, and that person would be timed out, but that person would also ask for someone else to be timed out as well, to which the owner did so. Because of these actions and others, I reported the owner via the discord website. When I got the actual email concerning the report, the reply asked if the admin is condoning the actions. Him being the admin and the server owner, who is doing these actions, proves that he is condoning these actions and needed to be banned immediately.",1,144.0,Fjcnhxnnf,0
us,United States,8972645637,2022-08-12T17:02:26-07:00,"if this was two weeks ago, i would’ve given 5 stars","i WAS paying for nitro for over a year now, and i didn’t have any issues until my last payment. since then i’ve decided to no longer pay for nitro or give support towards the discord company.
i got an email saying that my automatic payment was late and i needed to pay for nitro or else i would no longer be using nitro. i was confused and quickly paid for nitro while i was at work, i got a confirmation email and i was good to go. the discord app was no longer saying i needed to update my payment plan for three days, before getting pop ups saying, again, that i was going to run out of nitro on the day it was stating in the “late payment” email.

i emailed discord support, didn’t hear anything back until i opened ANOTHER ticket and i finally got a response. they asked for where i paid (?), the email, and what day. although i had stated all of it. i told them and they told me i needed to get transferred to a higher level of management. i didn’t hear back for four days, two days AFTER the day i was told nitro would run out. which it did. 
i opened a new ticket and demanded a refund, and the NEXT DAY i got a response to the second ticket i opened and was informed they fixed the issue and gave the fakest apology i’ve ever seen from a company.",3,139.0,angxlics,4
us,United States,6140953689,2020-06-30T11:13:07-07:00,Near Invaluable,"Since I joined my first server, it took some time for me to get used to all the functionality. There were so many things I didn’t know about, and yet that’s one of Discord’s biggest selling points. Most of the time if you want to do something, you can. Mark a server or channel as NSFW or 18+? You can do that. Change your display name for only one, specific server? You can do that too. But for me the most valuable thing about Discord is the sense of community that you feel almost immediately after logging on. Depending on your server choices you’ll almost always have an unread message, meaning there’s almost always something or someone for you to come back to. And if you don’t want to be bothered? Turn off notifications for servers and channels you don’t want to hear from. Not once have I had a security issue or even fear that I would lose personal information. Setting up 2-factor authentication was the easiest security experience I have had in a long time, and if you still have concerns, you won’t be required to even give Discord your phone number,  much less your name and other personal info. When I’m not using the in-built messages app on my phone or tablet, Discord is my #1 default",5,28.0,BluChange,33
us,United States,11303522616,2024-05-24T17:06:44-07:00,Latest UI Design & Changes Continue to Disappoint,"It's all in the title. These UI changes to both the desktop and mobile versions have been terrible. Mobile Discord UI in particular has taken some extremely heavy hits in UI redesign that did NOT need to happen. I manage a few servers with as few as 10 to a couple hundred people and being able to navigate, edit permissions for channels/users/server/etc., access direct messages, review/open/close/edit threads, etc. on the go are highly important. The changes to tap and swipe on the mobile app makes these gestures counterintuitive and are costing myself (and others) to waste so much time trying to get or do what we actually intended to do. The UI did not need these changes and these changes do not serve to provide the user with a better experience. As these poor decisions continue to be made and do not seem to stop or be rolled back, I am looking for alternatives and will be migrating my communities off of Discord ASAP.

UPDATE: Downgraded my review by 1 star to the lowest rating due to the developer's response that lacks accountability for poor decision making and understanding of what the issues discussed are. Refusal to admit you made bad, unwanted, and very poorly received changes to a previously functional and intuitive UI is not a good look nor inspires confidence in the developer's ability to resolve such issues or make innovative changes to the app.",1,230.0,Asmodeí,1
us,United States,9563939149,2023-01-30T06:24:13-07:00,"Good, but message requests is aggravating","Overall, discord is a good app to keep in touch with my friends, especially as we’ve stopped playing the games we’ve met in or fallen off other social media sites! It’s an alright platform for us F2P folks since none of us particularly NEED extra emojis and it’s really just for communication (although I’ll admit the video length threshold is a little low, I think most people consider a “short” video to be about Vine length)

But this “message requests” thing is AWFUL. I was told it was a newer thing, but I’d like to be able to set my messages to just “if you’re in my servers you’re probably messaging me for a reason, approved automatically”.  I’m sure you’re trying to protect me but I can block anyone being annoying pretty easily.  Or, at the very least, let the message requests NOTIFY me I HAVE a request.  The pm icon doesn’t pop up an alert at ALL and there’s no request push notification either.  It’s a pretty good way to miss someone in your server messaging you about time-sensitive stuff and it’s really not helpful if you’re the unlikely-to-message-first-unless-they-do introvert sort :( If there could be a fix on the notifications for it, or a setting that bypasses it, that would be great!",4,162.0,Brenna of House Targaryen,1
us,United States,11335176748,2024-06-02T07:26:23-07:00,Constant UI changes,"There is not a day that goes by where the discord team does not shoot themself in the foot by changing ui to be less functional. When you are on the channel navigation screen you used to be able to see part of the actual channel you were just in, allowing you to tap any part of the side of your screen to go back to the channel you were in. Now the channel list takes up your whole screen! Which is not necissary. I have only two channels in servers that I’m in that need that much room and their names are joke names that are long for the bit! And this hasn’t even gotten into how they made it so that you swipe to reply which swiping already had a use! You used to be able to swipe to see who was active, now things like joke statuses nobody sees because it is a lot harder now to see who is online! It made a whole feature essentially obsolete unless you tap the top of the channel which talking to friends, no one does. Then finally they have moved where DMs are four times in the past few months! There is constant change so any muscle memory you build up ruins you! You are actively being punished for using their app often! It is terrible. Stop changing your app discord team. You had fine, I’d go so far to even say, perfect UI but you’ve ruined it",3,231.1,CREEEPER AWW MAN,1
us,United States,8200306683,2022-01-03T09:21:09-07:00,Great! Except for one thing…,"This app is great! I gave the app a 5 star only so this could be seen, but I truly rate this a 3 But I give it that rating over one thing… THE PHONE NUMBER! Discord randomly asked me to put in my phone number in order to proceed so I did, when I finished that process I went right back over to delete the number because I did not want my number in my account. However when I did press “Remove Phone Number” It took me right back and said “Something’s fishy here, we need your Phone Number” So I realized I had no choice but to keep my Phone Number in my account. So, I put it in once again and then it said “This number can’t be used because it was used recently in another account” I was furious! Discord Devs, you’re not slick, this was basically you guys just saying “We don’t want you to remove your Phone Number, so yeah lol” That’s honestly not cool, you’re forcing people to put in their information they aren’t comfortable putting in! Others have been having this same problem, and some different reason why they don’t want their phone number in their account. This is not cool Discord Devs! Please remove this! Other than that… I love the app!",5,106.0,AnimeHokage,5
us,United States,10699336958,2023-12-15T17:12:32-07:00,Downgraded,"I love Discord, I’ve used it for years with the same layout, automatic 5 stars with that, without fail I would be on Discord 24/7 chatting and calling friends, having fun, chilling by myself, making servers for fun and. I had a organized system and everything worked perfectly, then these new updates came out changing the layout, and whole idea of Discord. My whole organization system became ruined. I try to swipe to get to the right side where everyone’s profiles and tabs for pinned messages are supposed to be but instead I start replying to a message. My friend tried calling me and I didn’t get any notification and now no matter how much/many times i go in and out of their chat the dumb red notification won’t go away. I’m also not a big fan of how the calls now look, I think the only two things I like about Discord now is the logo and how the only thing that didn’t completely change was the now known as the “server” tab with how all the servers are lined up on the side. The anonymity likability of it is gone. The calming swiping side to side ability, gone. The organization with the pinning ability, gone. I love Discord and have been using it as my main communication/organization platform but this layout has made me revolted by how it works and honestly I don’t think I will be using it as often as I had in the past.",2,208.1,x_shadix,5
us,United States,6567916631,2020-10-23T23:21:15-07:00,Wonderful app from a member of the Discord Role-play Community!,"Honestly, this app is what gets me through a lot of boredom in my day. It’s great, and even on the occasions there’s a problem, the devs tend to fix it rapidly with surprising speed. I use Discord to Role-play a lot, in fact it’s become my favorite pass time for the last year or so. The only thing I kind of wish was a bit better, is the character limit.

As a member of a few role-play servers I find myself often constricted by the 2000 character limit, especially considering I tend to write out 10K+ messages in google docs that I then post for characters that I role-play. As I’m sure is obvious, when I do several of these posts an hour the process of copying and pasting fragments of the messages becomes tedious. Not something that I generally hate, because with how wonderful discord servers are, allowing for many channels to be set up in ways that allow role-play servers to set up several settings, the limited characters per message is far outweighed in my preference. But, in a future update, if at all possible, I’m sure I, and the large amount of Novella Role-play members would certainly enjoy and appreciate an extended or unlimited message character limit.",5,44.0,Opus' Sepulchre,7
us,United States,10702735655,2023-12-16T06:26:52-07:00,Updates and changes,"Not that I believe this will be seen by the right people, but I seriously hope that the discord team is seeing the outcry for many of its users. After the most recent update for mobile, the app has become almost completely unusable for those who run massive servers or use the app as their only way of communication. Taking away the simple swipe of the side bar has been probably the most problematic and annoying part about this change, and one I pray will be added back soon. However, for those who manage servers and can’t get to where their going quick enough— this feature feels clanky and uncomfortable. The search feature as well, hardly works like it’s supposed to. You wanted to look for a gif in an ongoing conversation? Be prepared for it to cover your whole screen, then by the time you’re already picking one, you’ve gone and sent it at an inappropriate time because the conversation moved on without you knowing. The messages, sure, I can give the benefit of the doubt that they work like iMessages now, but the eyesore it is to open the message tab up and see everything crammed there is pretty uncomfortable and annoying. At least with the old features you didn’t have to open every message when clicking on messages— you’d just see their icon. Overall, I believe discord should be a place where people come to gather and express themselves, and the one thing that made discord stand out was their accessibility and easygoing style of layout. Now that it has changed so dramatically, I truly hope that the discord teams will hear their communities voices and meet us half way.",1,208.1,Littles inc.,0
us,United States,11151695079,2024-04-12T19:48:33-07:00,New UI,"{new message below this} This new UI is HORRIBLE. At least give users the option to switch it back. It’s so overwhelming to look at and you can’t even see as many DMs as you used to. The fact that you can’t see what servers have messaged unless you click servers and the fact that you can’t see servers with a simple swipe WHILE being in DMs is so annoying. My small servers barely get checked now because it’s much more of a hassle to look at. There was no need to change it. I don’t care to see how long it’s been since I’ve messaged someone either. This new layout is atrocious and you need to SERIOUSLY reconsider it. None of your users like it. If you’re not gonna get rid of it, again, at least give users the OPTION TO SWITCH IT BACK. You talk about wanting to make discord easier, when this new UI literally adds too many unnecessary steps when the old layout was literally easier. The ways to get to pins is ridiculous and I hate the image layout. It’s unnecessarily hard to see things now and the way you have pins set by date and not by the date the pin was added is so stupid. FIX YOUR APP.

(Update): discord can you please stop changing the mobile layout??? you fixed the horrible new layout to look like the old layout which was great and I loved it. it had the old look with a more modern touch and now it’s back to how it was again. like seriously? CHANGE IT BACK",1,224.0,KaityStrawberry,3
us,United States,9262459842,2022-11-06T12:13:02-07:00,Bugs and Glitches,"Discord is great overall but ever since the recent last 3 updates, there has been some bugs and glitches on mobile that needs to be fixed. The first bug I found is getting out of control now. When I am creating my own server and trying to edit a channel, the channel would freeze on my phone and I can’t do anything. I tried refreshing the app numerous of times but nothing happened. I tried deleting the app and redownloading it and it worked, until I go back into my own server with the same channel and it freezes again. I even tried updating my phone and nothing happened. Please fix this bug. It’s so minor and can be so fixable. 

The other bug or glitch is that, it seems like it got changed. When I am trying to make a certain role not see a certain channel while having a specific role that allows you to see it. I moved the certain role above the specific role and apparently the certain role can still see the channel that only the specific role can. I liked it how it was where the certain role was above the specific role and the certain role can’t see the channel that the specific role could. I mean this is up to you to decide whether or not you want to change it back but I am not fully satisfied with this.",3,151.0,puppyisthecoolest101,2
us,United States,5511955185,2020-02-10T01:22:50-07:00,Go back to the old style then having large words in your face.,"In short, it's ugly af, and feels incredibly intrusive. The previous ui design was much nicer to look at, and much less in the way and in your face.

Please remove this asap, or change it to something more akin to the previous design. I'm seeing a lot of other people expressing dislike of it, so I hope that will help convince you to change it back.

On a side note: I'm someone who really needs empty space when using things. Not too long ago, Twitter completely updated their website, and in doing so removed a significant amount of empty space which was previously present. Until a plugin was developed to set it back to the previous design, I actually could not use the website. Something similar happened recently with Discord to a lesser extent, specifically with the friends tab. The recent addition of the ""active now"" section removed a lot of the empty space which was previously present, and as a result I can rarely use that tab without needing to look away or click something else immediately. This new update again takes away more empty space with the new ui changes, albeit to a notably lesser extent, but it's enough for it to instill at least some discomfort for me while using Discord.",4,3.1.10,hsbebeheheh,22
us,United States,7337827961,2021-05-14T07:40:35-07:00,The new discord update is gross,"I’ve been using discord for almost a year now and it was chill and fun to use which it still is. I just can’t get over the new font they are using and the way they highlight pings now it’s so gross, and the logo is fine and all but the color is kinda wonky like it just doesn’t fit the theme for discord as well as the other one did. And I get it though they’re trying to make it marketable to tons of other groups (which it already was) but really what’s so wrong with the app being known for gaming? Come on. I still use the app cause it’s my main way of communicating and gaming with my friends but it’s just really throwing me off now. Before the update I would’ve given it a 4-4.5 cause there are quite a bit bugs and I think it’s annoying I can’t send my friends videos and pictures just because it’s a small bit too big, and if I wanted to send them videos of my dogs being cute I’d have to pay 5-14 bucks (because of tax) to do so, but that isn’t too bad. Anyway now because of the annoying fonts and all the bad things I’ve been hearing coming from the new update, I’m giving it a 2 but it’s an in general great app if you wanna meet to new people online and communicate with your friends. I believe this app has a place for EVERYONE, disboard is a common and easy place to find a server for you.",2,73.0,ColdCorndog.inc,6
us,United States,11454769334,2024-07-04T01:54:07-07:00,The iOS app is garbage now,"The newish update makes your friends list harder to get to, and it can no longer be filtered by who’s online. The new swipable list above the messages doesn’t make sense either. Half the people it shows are offline, and the other half that are online are mixed people that I am and am not friends with. Then when other friends of mine come online, they don’t populate in the list at the top. I’m having trouble figuring out what this list is intended for and why it would suggest people who are offline or who aren’t my friends. If this is the unintuitive way it’s going, then when you suggest people I’m not even friend with, you could at least suggest people I’ve interacted with recently like in other severs I’m apart of versus people I haven’t been friends with in over a year. Furthermore, the only semi-meaningful friends list left is no longer one of the tabs included with the server list. Instead you have to go all the way to your profile page and then click on “Your Friends” which can’t be filtered by those who are online. This is a complete step backwards in intuition. I really wish the option to use the old version of discord on iOS was still available. I was almost willing to pay for nitro until this, but instead I’ll be deleting discord for iOS, and if the desktop version gets this nonsensical, then it’ll be the next to go.",1,236.0,ZachKXF34,1
us,United States,9020549969,2022-08-26T15:07:09-07:00,A Genuinely Outstanding Social Networking.,"Discord is A Genuinely outstanding social network. It’s great for being able to stay in touch with buddies from school, Family, work etc. You can join and create servers with as many people as you wish. Servers can be very useful for a group of 11+ people. They can be themed for School, Work, Business, Game updates, and even just having fun and talking with your pals. Your able to make group chats with up to 10 people in them. And if your worried about other people friending you, it’s no problem unless you have a user name that is a popular funny joke with a predictable number at the end. Discord makes it so you have a four digit number that is  uniquely yours to your account, so you don’t have to worry about random people friending you. There does need to be work done, maybe have it so if it’s a server that is for kids make that a option to tag out or remove any crass or abrasive language although I can see why it’s not necessary since the app is rated 17+. If you want a secure, comfortable Social app, this is the one for you. And there is also a dark mode which makes it very easy on the eyes.",5,141.0,bonnie from splatoin 2,3
us,United States,11021826433,2024-03-08T06:34:54-07:00,This new UI…,"TLDR: The app is great, the new UI is not. I absolutely adore Discord and I’ve been using it for 4 years, so I’m going to try my best to write a quality review that is detailed and helpful. I just got hit with the update for the new UI, I’ve been dreading. This for awhile due to the things I have heard from fellow discord users. And I have to say, they weren’t exaggerating. After picking my theme, the first thing I noticed is how bubbly and clumsy it is. Everything feels very blown up making it difficult to type and navigate servers. When I try to scroll up and down to read chat, I find myself accidentally swiping to reply to messages. Next, the dms. I find it very difficult to navigate as they are not above the servers, this was much preferable to them having their own tab. I very much dislike that the dms take up the whole screen and the last message sent is shown, this makes it difficult to keep private messages private. This also means that less dms are shown so I have to do a lot more scrolling. Time for the mentions tab. There isn’t much I have to say about it other than I wish the mentions, activity feed, and things like accepted friend requests had different tabs like before. I dislike all the round corners and much prefer the previous ones, being sharp and square. This was much more visually pleasing to me. Now for the pros. I find myself enjoying that the friends portion now has separations between the letters ie a b c d. I also enjoy how the editing status and profile is more obvious and simple. Overall, I wish I could reverse the update and go back to the previous UI or have the option to switch between the two as I recognize that some people might enjoy this new UI.",3,219.1,Finn Potts,0
us,United States,8041483674,2021-11-19T12:44:10-07:00,Severely disappointed with Discord Support,"My account was hacked and during the two days it was hacked, three Nitro gifted subs were purchased by the hacker. Discord Support helped me get my account back, but even though I mentioned the false purchases when I explained in detail the whole situation, they didn’t pay any mind to that part at all or offer any solution to my financial dilemma. I didn’t know what to do, so I went to my bank provider and decided to get my money back that way. This was apparently against the Terms and Conditions, so they disabled my account. I tried to appeal by explaining the situation again, but all I got was a cookie cutter response that denied my appeal. I tried one more time; this time I offered to undo the chargebacks because the Discord email that informed me of my account being disabled said I could. I just wanted my account back even if it meant giving back money that was wrongfully taken from me in the first place. All I got was the exact same cookie cutter response denying my appeal.
Are bots running Discord Support? There seems to be zero empathy and zero reading of anything I said. From my POV, I’m getting punished by Discord for trying to get my money back that was stolen from me while using Discord. Although, I didn’t go about getting my money back the “right” way, this still doesn’t sit right with me at all. Now I lose my account of 5+ years. What a joke.",1,101.0,Fluttershy311,12
us,United States,12705652121,2025-05-27T15:33:10-07:00,Great app,"Discord is a good app, I’ve met many new people and made plenty of friends, but there is just one problem. The 2FA system, the 2FA system may help in some sort but it can be very frustrating as well. On my main (now lost) account I had activated the 2FA system. I don’t have a passkey or security key so the only option I had was to use backup codes. Even though it was frustrating to keep log in using backup codes I went on with it. Not too long ago (like 4 days ago?) I forgot about the backup codes and I ended up logging out of my account without it. I never thought to screenshot my backup codes and I’m usually on mobile so there was no other way for me to log in. I don’t have any other devices that are logged into my account either. So I had to go on my alt account. Other apps with the 2FA system has a way to recover your account even if you don’t have backup codes or whatever. If you could make an update to where you could recover your account even if you have lost your 2FA would be amazing and help many others experiencing a similar situation like mine! Either way, if you have read this, thank you for reading this and I hope you take my idea into consideration.",4,281.0,Jaebae😌😍,0
us,United States,12774388072,2025-06-14T11:38:40-07:00,Image transparency no longer works as of recent updates (my patience with this app is being tested),"As an artist, I like to use Discord as my main messaging platform for both friends and clients due to its convenience and widespread usage. However, recent updates have made this difficult for two glaringly apparent reasons.

I’m not certain when exactly this began, but a recent update somehow “broke” image uploads for mobile users — PNGs and other static images that should be high quality and transparent are now given white backgrounds and visible compression artifacts. This is not an issue when sending comedic images, but it absolutely is when sending artwork to my clients. I’ve had to upload them elsewhere and link to them to preserve their intended quality, which is inconvenient and infuriating. A chat platform that I once counted on for keeping my images intact has somehow degraded to the likes of social media platforms I’ve abandoned partially due to similar reasons; I should not have to upload my art elsewhere if Discord is able to handle uploading the same images from desktop without running into compression/transparency issues.

I’ve used this app for nearly a decade now. I have sung its praises endlessly. I have paid for a full Discord Nitro subscription for several years without interruption. However, I cannot tolerate the half-baked, feature-breaking updates that have been pushed out more frequently over the years, even ruining the user experience for actual customers. If it continues to destroy itself in this way, I will be able to say I no longer recommend it. For now, I will just say it is getting harder to support the app’s development.",2,283.0,BEELETH,0
us,United States,6850026085,2021-01-09T09:54:10-07:00,Where is the customer service,"The app itself is a 10/10, the mechanics are great, i’m able to chat with my friends for hours on end, it was overall an incredible time, UNTIL out of the blue “ your account has been suspended for violations against the discord terms and service”,OK what exactly did I do, “we will be investigating your account”.  I emailed them, A bot responds “ The reason your account was disabled was because you violated the discord terms in service” OK, BUT WHAT DID I DO?????? “ you violated the terms and service”. Needless to say I lost about 20 friends because I can’t speak to them anymore.
In their eyes they see someone who’s completely ignoring their messages, it just won’t let me get in. I tried to log back in, and I had to take the robot verification test eight times before it stopped letting me take the test for “Rate Violations” which basically means you tried getting your password in too many times and now we’re not gonna let you do it anymore. The app itself is great, But be warned, your account might get disabled for no reason what so ever. Discord if you’re reading this (a real person that is) WHY IS MY ACCOUNT DISABLED??????????",5,53.0,".,.,...,,plz read",8
us,United States,10667826805,2023-12-07T11:34:38-07:00,Not a fan of the latest mobile Discord update,"I have been a long time mobile Discord user since the day I joined in 2017. I liked the interface and while there was a bit I needed to learn, I enjoyed it due to it not being like other websites. I liked it because it was different than other apps. 

The latest mobile Discord update (December 2023) changed a lot of things around, making it harder for long time Discord users to use. Buttons and menus were changed around, as well as various touch gestures and commands. I have almost accidentally replied to people when I just wanted to check who was online in a given server. 

I understand that you want to make this app easier for new users to use, but I have talked with newer discord users (joining in about 2021 or so) and they got used to the app as it was before pretty quickly. If it wasn’t broken, then why fix it? I really hope that you listen to these reviews and feedback and at least give us a “switch to older Discord” feature. I can’t really move off this platform as I have many friends who use it, I am just not a fan of the latest mobile update at all.",5,207,astrologykat,0
us,United States,11296353757,2024-05-22T17:22:53-07:00,New UI cluttered and upsetting (as of May ‘24),"Look, I disliked the last UI change. I’m the kind of person to dislike change of any kind. But now you change it again right as I had warmed up to the new one?
1) I don’t care that the DM’s button is now far from the reach of my thumb, but ever since you removed swiping to see who’s online (…why would I ever want to prioritize swiping to reply to a message??) I would go to my DM list to check. I can’t do that as efficiently anymore. If you’re doing this, bring back swiping to server list. Perhaps a swipe from the center of the screen could reply to a message and a swipe from the far right side could show server list. I’m not picky, I just want this function back.  
2) more importantly, you don’t even let the list of messages I have fill the entire screen. I don’t need a little bit of screen on the right dedicated to showing me I can swipe onto my most recent dm, I am very capable of just tapping on it myself. My screen now looks cluttered with small text and it’s overwhelming. Please revert this or simplify it to less elements on the screen. I have 20/20 vision and yet I’m squinting at my screen to see what message im selecting. Every update like this I become more and more dissatisfied with this app. I love having easy access to my friends and communities, but constant and ineffective UI changes leave me feeling alienated and confused while using the app. I will not be rating this app higher until UI actually improves in a way that is helpful to the users. 
Even better, just allow your users to pick the UI layout the desire and set their own motion shortcuts (swipe to reply, server list, emote, etc).",2,230.0,Frost Ashdove,0
us,United States,10804743883,2024-01-09T20:51:11-07:00,update.,"i love discord and i’ve been using it for about 5 years now? there’s never been an issue about it until the newest update with the layer format that we see now. i get it, a lot of people don’t like change and all and you want people to get used to it but it was still simpler and unique in the old layout, now it feels like your just trying to be a carbon copy of other apps and that took the fun out of it. another problem is that discords been ignoring everyone who makes a comment about it. They respond to people on twitter, until you make a complaint. they want their app to be picture perfect whenever they’re just kinda copying things. BUT. overall, aside from all that, it is a great app and i continue to use it and i continue to like it, i have a lot of friends and stuff on there and it’s my one app that’s used almost everyday all day. There’s a few bugs here and there but THANKFULLY discord is really good at fixing them, and they fix it as soon as they can, which does make them a lot better than most apps out there that you use to talk to your friends. All the servers you get to make are pretty neat too, i’ve made a lot of friends. but, that’s just my review, lol.",4,211.0,Funimates a good app,0
us,United States,13044115489,2025-08-21T10:44:51-07:00,Easy to navigate,"Discord mobile makes it quick and easy to navigate through servers, respond to messages, update your profile, make calls, organize your servers, and more with only one hand.
The *only* downsides to choosing mobile over desktop would have to be creation and moderation of servers being quite difficult, and receiving push notifications. 
When it comes to server creation, I found many options to be desktop-only. That, or near impossible to find. As for push notifications, they seem to occasionally entirely disappear and after a bunch of troubleshooting, the only solution has been to delete and reinstall the app. It happens a ton more if you are one to switch between browser and mobile often. An unfortunate and common issue for mobile users, but we can only hope it will be fixed in a future update. 
Overall, discord mobile is a secure and convenient way to communicate with friends and connect with others online. It’s an essential app on my phone and I use it more than any other messaging app. If you’re considering downloading it, I highly recommend doing so!",5,293.0,missJGW,0
us,United States,10289803459,2023-08-23T01:54:33-07:00,Good way to interact with friends or family,"I normally do not use discord when I don't have to but I actually have the app just so that I'm able to stay in contact with the people that I know and love. Discord is a pretty safe place as it only allows you to add people that you know personally because when adding someone, it ask for their name of their account and the 4 digit number that comes with it which I personally believe is really good as it doesn't allow for you to just randomly talk to random strangers on the internet. Another thing is that I like it because the app also allows you to play games on there while chatting with friends on discord. Sometimes I would be messaging a friend I know on discord and he'd be playing whatever game and I'd still be able to message him because while he plays and interact with me which I personally think is cool, and convenient as it allows for message interactions and gaming time. And I'm the type of person to message a lot of my friends and family on the app itself. I do believe that this is a good place to stay more connected to those that you know and love.",5,191.0,Laggy person,0
us,United States,11433654724,2024-06-28T10:11:32-07:00,I'm begging you,"Please...please, for the love of all things good in the world, I just need an option to have badge notifications on my app when people send messages in our friend group server. Not just DMs or @'s but all messages. I miss so many conversations because I don't have badges. I don't understand how you can have a setting that makes it so the individual messages show up on my lock screen but can't figure out how to make a badge appear to correspond to each one. Or even just a single badge without a number when there are unread messages. I can't always immediately look at discord when pick up my phone and see the lock screen notifications because I have to do something else first, but by the time I've finished my other task I've forgotten there are messages because there isn't a badge on there. I read somewhere that you don't do it because some servers are so big it would be constant notifications. Well okay then just make it an option for each server or topic within a server whether you get notified or not. Given the incredibly specific notification options I've seen on myriad other apps, it's gotta be doable and I don't get why you don't make your app work like every other app out there since that's how people have learned to interface with their phones.",2,235.0,Optic Complex,0
us,United States,11359131291,2024-06-08T15:03:55-07:00,Best app,"Grass has several functions. We cannot digest it and yet it is one of the most important resources for our food production: animals eat grass and we eat animal products such as meat, eggs and milk. Furthermore, we also use grass in other ways: for sport, recreation and to brighten up gardens and public spaces. This plant also has important ecological functions: it protects against soil erosion, it absorbs water, it purifies the air we breathe and so on.
 
Every variety of grass has its own special properties. The grass family, or Graminae, has about 8,000 varieties. There are suitable varieties of grass for cultivation at almost every temperature and every amount of rainfall. Some grasses can thrive during extreme drought because they have very long roots which can extract water from deep under the ground. Other sorts can flourish in extreme cold or withstand long periods of rain.
 
Most people take grass for granted but we shouldn't forget that grass plays a very important role in our lives. Scientists all over the world are working on research, improvement, breeding and cultivation of this very important crop. Barenbrug does this, too. But that isn't all that we do. We have the entire process at our fingertips: everything from the breeding and the cultivation of grass seed to production and sales.",3,232.0,Jfjfjdichehdhdh,1
us,United States,10708151741,2023-12-17T07:54:29-07:00,The New Update Has Me Frustrated.,"I love Discord and all I’m on it like alot, but I don’t think I will be anymore, and it’s all because of the new update. The update is so confusing, complicated, and hard to navigate stuff. The old layout was so much simpler. I don’t even know how to edit, or delete channels anymore. I can’t even swipe right to see if members are online or offline. 

