us,United States,9849754492,2023-04-22T10:44:24-07:00,Couple of things,Get a response from the developer about my issue being about security and privacy and I need to go to some address and let them know about my issues. First no my review is right here. How about you read it and fix the issue. I’m not gonna go someplace else and post a second review. Second how are push notification you know things that get sent to the user that anyone can see about privacy and security? When I was setting up my account one of the tests to prove I was not a robot was finding the middle of a bears nose. The issue was where I put the icon and took my finger off was not where it was going. I would push and hold get a bubble showing me where the cursor is and when I would put it on the nose and remove my finger it would be on the eye or forehead. Second issue I have is at least twice I selected no to do you want to receive notifications. What happens later in the day. I get a ton of notifications. Why ask if you are gonna ignore what people select. I shouldn’t have to select no then go to my settings and turn off what I did not give permission for. Open the app today the second day using the app and I get an in app notification to add my contacts and the box was already checked. I selected to not do this the first day (yesterday) when I set up my account and nothing has and will change. Stop asking.,1,174.0,Gaspatchosoup,1
us,United States,10832621124,2024-01-17T08:11:19-07:00,New update is whack,"This would be five stars bc obviously the platform is really good and widely known across the internet, but the new mobile update is just… broken. I really appreciate the new UI, I do, but theres a lot of things wrong with the update: - Clicking on something often doesn’t yield feedback, tapping just straight up doesn’t work sometimes - The DMs section is really weird. At the top I have people I haven’t talked to in literally years, and have since unfriended, and below that ofc is the DMs I actually have active, and then below that is “recommended people” that apparently have mutual friends, but when i click on their profiles it turns out we don’t actually. I presume this is because of people I *used* to be friends with, and the system isn’t syncing, but this is still really annoying - Files just don’t upload sometimes. What. - Sometimes the keyboard just doesn’t pop up when I tap on the textbox and I have to restart the app, and sometimes commands stop autofilling and I have to restart the app, and emojis don’t autofill sometimes so I have to… you get it  Hopefully they get this stuff patched, I’m just going to have to wait around for that to happen ig",4,212.0,Wowza…,0
us,United States,10699323591,2023-12-15T17:09:45-07:00,Worst Update Ever,"Where should I begin? The fact that Discord changed the dark mode to be even darker, making all the texts stand out much more harshly without any consideration or option to switch things back to the gray color? That immediately impacts my vision, and I can't help but worry for other people who suffer from sensitive sight. How about the fact that the mobile search bar is now split for every server, making it absolutely awful to search for content because there's server-wide search and channel-wide search (even though in previous iterations we were perfectly fine with the tagging features in the server search bar). How about the fact that we cannot see the full server member list unless we move to a ""general"" chat? Which might not exist depending on the design of the server? The swipe-to-reply instead of swipe-to-show function is unintuitive at best, and absolutely annoying to use on the daily. I'm sure everyone else has their own two cents to add. If Discord doesn't revert this awful update, I'll delete my own app and use desktop instead. I encourage everyone to do the same, because clearly none of the people in charge of this corporation actually gives a toot about functionality. Upgrades for the sake of upgrades, innovation for the sake of innovation, are the antithesis to actual human morals and ethics.",1,208.1,Pomodoko,5
us,United States,6747572910,2020-12-12T21:19:41-07:00,Suggestions for an already great app,"I love the features, I often rescue kids from the Amino Communities and show them the quality differences for communication. There’s a lot of secret quirks you find out from other users and I think it’s a good way of differentiating newbs to the OGs. However with all of the cool things I’d like to be able to have a few features that I’ve seen in other apps added one day. For instance backgrounds for the channels ((could be nitro feature)) make it easier to submit transparent stickers on Apple mobile. I have to get on the PC site and it’s such a hardship when I have to mess around on the site that isn’t meant to be seen on mobile. And for the censors || || maybe keep people from screenshotting the message after you uncensor it. I’ve seen photo editing apps do it so I’m sure we could squeeze the feature into Discord. ALSO:: can we get rid of the emoji conversion? I’m pretty sure if someone wanted to send an actual emoji they would. Otherwise everyone probs want to stick to the keyboard aesthetic. Over all a sturdy and nice app once you get accustomed to it. As a newb things seem very cluttered and you just have to figure it out on your own :/",5,51.0,Kite_Kidd.0,6
us,United States,6811549856,2020-12-30T11:09:06-07:00,"Great, just a few problems.","This app is very very good but has some bugs...

