us,United States,9465249894,2023-01-02T22:24:47-07:00,Used to love you.,"So when I first came across discord I loved it. It was a free social media platform where as long as you didn’t offend your friends everything was kind of a free for all. There was acceptance, old friends, new friends, some people I’ve come to call family. I met my fiancé in a discord server… 5 years ago I had nothing but good to say about it. However with every update they have put out things have grown worse and worse rather than better. I know why they don’t want negative public reviews and want you to tell them privately… it’s a save face moment. But I have to say… discord used to compress files so well I could pop off 5 photos at once without nitro their premium service. Now? I can’t pop off a single one because they retracted the auto decompression without adding a manual option… why? So you have to buy a monthly nitro. I’m not foolish. I’ve been coding servers there for almost 5 years now. If you can’t be good to your customers and honest to boot? Your customers will leave. They will grow tired of your greed. I won’t pay for something I used to get for free. Especially not when its barely what I used to get for free. I might think different if it was at least twice the value but it’s not it’s the exact same value as before. it’s the free value at a cost now. I’m as disappointed here as I am Facebook now.",1,158.0,SunnyBunny1985,1
us,United States,13744702622,2026-02-13T06:01:53-07:00,Discord making it easier for adults with bad intentions to be closer to children,"Discord is hiding behind the protect the kids excuse to gather more personal information about you and their users. Beside having a new CEO from Israeli, Discord will be moving everyone account into a teens account until proven you are an adult. Discord have had a history of getting their system hacked. They have stated in the past that all personal information will be deleted. It was a lied and all information was stored within it servers. Discord is NOW claiming, once again, all personal information you provide will be deleted from it servers when in reality it will be sent to their parent company for storing. Discord is using the excuse of protecting kids when in reality, it will not work. Those who do not see a problem with this are part of the problem of allowing COMPANIES. Not government officials. COMPANIES. Owning your personal data, such as your face, where you have been, and so on. Discord is not to be trusted with your personal information. Do not be fulled by the false act if protecting kids. Parents should monitor their children from time to time. NOT DISCORD. Discord have failed in protecting it communities by not listening. What makes you think giving personal information to a company would help? It won’t. It would help them sell your data. Not you.",1,315.0,Loser_Brain,1
us,United States,10669479489,2023-12-08T00:13:03-07:00,Update looks like a cheap and overdone version of Facebook Messenger,"It’s overwhelming, unoriginal, messy, and forceful. They now changed the colors when you are in a call, make you see what random people are doing in server you are at when in dms. I personally hate it so much, to the bare minimum it would be nice to be able to choose some things such as where the dms are and the background color of calls. This two things would make me accept it a bit more because I just hate how it looks and how inconvenient some changes are. It’s so uncomfortable to navigate now, and straight up just ugly and just looks like another knock off facebook Messenger, discord was so original and beneficial with it’s set up, now goes backwards trying to copy what it’s being mostly used.

