us,United States,10951162013,2024-02-17T20:18:34-07:00,the best thing about discord,"Discord is an outstanding multimedia messaging platform that transcends its gaming roots. Whether you’re strategizing with teammates or simply chatting with friends, Discord offers a seamless experience across text, audio, and video communication. Here’s why it’s a must-have: It lets you create free public or private servers, making it easy to connect with friends or strangers. It works seamlessly across computers, mobile devices, and game consoles. While it’s not specifically marketed for enterprise-level security, Discord’s end-to-end encryption ensures privacy for your messages. Organize and customize your server to suit your needs. Whether you’re a gamer, hobbyist, or professional, Discord adapts. Discord Nitro offers premium features like custom emotes, animated avatars, and larger file uploads. Even the free tier provides ample functionality. When members boost a server, it levels up, unlocking premium benefits. Discord’s popularity extends beyond gamers, making it an Editors’ Choice winner for online messaging tools. In summary, Discord bridges communication gaps, fosters communities, and adds a touch of fun to your digital interactions.",5,216.0,anomaly 666,1
us,United States,9825577610,2023-04-15T12:00:46-07:00,Confusing And Difficult,"I downloaded discord for school related reasons, at first it worked fine, no issues with logging in and the app seemed to be user friendly. As I started to use the app more and join and leave servers I noticed that discord was extremely confusing and not straight forward what so ever. Correct me if I’m wrong but discord is supposed to be an app for quick and easy communication with people you know or don’t know. A fun place to meet other and talk. If discord is promoting itself to be this exciting and nice app for everyone then they should first fix their issues regarding logins, verifications, emails, phone numbers, and overall user friendliness. I tried going to their support page through the app and even then the app would not give me a clear idea or explanation to fix any of the issues I’ve come across. Now whenever I try to login with email or phone number discord tells me that the email/phone number is already being used for a different account or the email doesn’t exist. Seriously, I get safety and all but it has gotten to a point where I literally cannot even use the app because it will not allow me to login. Luke is aid previously, I need to be able to access this app and account for school related reasons and now I am behind in my courses for the semester because my issues with this app.",1,173.0,Casey Saints,1
us,United States,2122370360,2018-01-24T09:21:17-07:00,Quality App,"Discord has always been a friend of mine. When I first began gaming on Steam in late 2015, I used Skype. But it quickly became clear that Discord was a much higher quality alternative. For a price of nothing this app accomplishes a lot and demonstrates the quality and integrity of Hammer and Chisel. Everything from the non chinglish description to the actual, human written developer responses emanates a down-to-earth feeling about Hammer and Chisel. There's nothing that makes me happier than a development team that represents the antithesis of everything we've seen recently on the App Store. Thousands of apps that all do the same thing, written by Chinese and Indian companies attempting to either scam you or take your money. Discord is not one of those. This app was written well, and has not lagged at all on my iPhone 6+. It even features skillfully coded transitions to segments, making it fully compliant with Apple's new HIG (Human Interface Guidelines). It's people like those at Hammer and Chisel that make the world a better place for everyone, and I salute you. Keep on doing what you're doing now, and never give in to the pressures of advertisements and information-selling. This app is also a great place to find new friends and communities. It was through discord that I made many of my online friends and where I strengthened many existing friendships. It was there that I learned how to be a staff member and deal with troublemakers in a responsible way. This type of experience is invaluable for teenagers like myself as it serves as a preparation for careers and how to behave in a workplace. No matter why you're here, I can safely say you will enjoy the journey you have on Discord.

Thanks for reading, and have a great day.
BlueFireExplosion",5,2.2.0,Bluefire3829,0
us,United States,10699611600,2023-12-15T18:08:37-07:00,New UI is practically unusable,"Usually it doesn’t take me more than a day or two to get used to a new user interface but this update is SO bad and SO illogical that even after a WEEK I’m still struggling to find where things are. There are so many terrible things to discuss, like the new location of DMs and the way it’s laid out with your contacts in a weird row at the top. But the worst to me is the new search “function” - why are there two places to perform a search? Why add a channel-only search when it was incredibly easy to filter by channel in a server-wide search? Why is the channel-only search almost exactly where the general search used to be so a gesture I’ve been performing for my entire three years as a Discord user leads me to incredible frustration until I remember y’all screwed it up? And what even are these search categories - why are images showing up in both ‘media’ and ‘files’ when I’m desperately searching for a PDF I sent but can’t filter to JUST files? Bummed to have to cancel my Nitro over this but I doubt you’ll get the point unless it hits y’all in the profit margin.

Wait omg I submitted this review and then came back because I’d forgotten to mention the glitches!! It lags so badly now, and it WILL NOT clear unread message notifications even when I’ve tried over and over to clear them.",1,208.1,lindsay.c.,4
us,United States,12028089056,2024-12-05T04:00:29-07:00,It WAS really good,"Don’t get too attached to anything you have on discord. It was a really good app. I was really happy, majority of my life was tied to discord. It was one of the only places I could talk to my friends and make new ones. This was until I got PERMANENTLY suspended for age violations. I’m 13, and I’ve never seen nor done anything extremely inappropriate. I’ve never done anything to have a reason to be suspended. I’d understand if I was suspended for a certain time period—like, if I was suspended until I’m of age. However, I was suspended PERMANENTLY. I don’t understand how so many people that are predators, that give their ages, that send nudes, etc. don’t get suspended for the horrible things they do but I was for my age. There are 11 year olds on discord, I’ve watched them say it, but somehow I was the one suspended permanently. Practically my whole life was on discord, now I have basically nothing. What’s gonna happen to all the servers I talk in frequently? All of my online friends when I never talk to them again—will they think I hate them? Discord was possibly my favorite app, now it’s one of the worst things that happened to me. I can’t believe I got so attached to discord of all things after all the things I’d heard about it. I wasn’t even suspended for being 13, I was suspended because I was 12 at one point on the app, which is still stupid.",1,257.0,Yip yip yooray,0
us,United States,10681056854,2023-12-10T22:44:26-07:00,The New Update is Horrendous,"No one asked for the new mobile UI update, I have heard zero positive views on it, and I dislike it so much I almost hate it. I can no longer slide my screen, I have to tap to get places, and it’s so incredibly disorganized. I do not like that I have to click on the “server” or “messages” option to switch between DMs and servers when I could’ve easily swiped to see my servers, my DMs, channel information, DM information, etc. It’s very clunky and serves no purpose. I can’t see people’s statuses very easily, I can’t tell which of my friends are online and offline, and while I think the addition of the icons at the top of the screen showing what people may be playing or listening to is nice, I don’t like how it’s showing users who aren’t my friends. I only want to see what my friends are doing, not random people I DMed once from a server I barely talk in. It’s a pain to get to pinned messages in channels and DMs and now I can’t see previews for links or images/files when looking at pinned messages. It just says the file name and I then have to click on yet another thing to see what image it’s trying to show me or what link I was sent. It’s not helpful in the slightest. Please for the love of goodness, change things back this update is ridiculous and no one likes it or wanted it in the first place.",1,207,DragonRider🐲,7
us,United States,4907621870,2019-10-07T22:01:36-07:00,Mobile app has issues,"Discord works great on a desktop computer/laptop, other than finding the right chat room and general navigation issues like getting a message noise but never seeing the message because you were in a voice chat room.  Could use a redesign.  Like why isn’t voice just enable in the same chat room so there’s no switching back and forth?

However, this review is for the mobile app.  It doesn’t work.  Every time I do so much as sneeze (another app notification/text message comes in, if I get a phone call, etc.) the app stops working.  I get that the voice should stop but after switching apps and coming back or after ending the phone call, the Discord app never recovers and must be restarted, rejoin the room, and then it works...for a while.  Until almost anything else happens.  Worst of all, when my phone falls asleep, so does Discord, sometimes.  It’s unpredictable when I’m just randomly disconnected from Discord.  My friend reported his phone calls not coming through when he’s on a Discord voice channel. Not sure which problem is worse.

I’d highly recommend using a different app. Often, my friends and I just use a phone conference call.  And I can send a text message while on a phone call. So how does this app improve my gaming other than taking bandwidth from my gaming?",2,3.1.4,Jualter,13
us,United States,7199582081,2021-04-08T13:41:07-07:00,"Fantastic on Mobile/Desktop, Needs to Be Ported to Other Platforms","Let me get one thing straight. I love using Discord as a platform for chatting with friends, playing games together, etc. There are a few minor bugs I could do without (the first one that pops into my mind is how if a message is sent almost exactly as I switch to another channel, flipping back to the first channel won’t get rid of the notification unless I switch off it and switch back), but overall, it works fantastically. I especially love being able to search up GIFs on mobile. That was definitely needed.

The only thing I’d request is that the team would bring the Discord app to other platforms; namely, console platforms. Currently, I can’t stream my console gameplay to Voice Channels because I can’t easily access Discord on console. While typing on a console keyboard would be a nightmare and a half, I imagine streaming and voice channels would work beautifully, as that’s exactly how party chats tend to work. I’d be willing to put up with getting out my phone to type quickly in a channel if I could join a Voice Channel and stream to it from my console.",5,65.0,R0NIN707,1
us,United States,10680240332,2023-12-10T16:33:00-07:00,New Dec 2023 Update.,"If you’re expecting the discord you know and love from gaming on your laptop. You’re sourly mistaken. It looks nothing like the discord you know and love, it’s purposely different almost as if it’s a rip of discord of itself. Navigating, managing, and messaging is hard. Those who are easily effected by sensory issues, like myself, had had a hard time navigating the app through all the different colors. At first it blended but now you have your nitro app theme, the whole discord layout, and profile differences. (However ik it can be a fix for profile theme wise but then it forces u into midnight/gray) 
It feels unwelcoming and confusing at the same time, it does not navigate like before and some basic functions are even gone. Discord’s support then mentions about how the user base must get used to it instead of hearing out its live feedback audience. The app bugs worse, it will glitch from the original UI to the new one. It will copy text after it’s sent. I don’t receive notifications between servers and messages regularly. I cant tell whose online or noticing status’ unless I go out of my way to look at them from the user itself. This makes me not want to enjoy mobile anymore, and I’m sure many others could agree. If you’re going to improve discord, don’t make it feel like a separate space.",1,207,Jay loves fishies,2
us,United States,8021790636,2021-11-13T20:03:20-07:00,My accounts,"My main discord account just magically signed me out and i know the password but it said it didn't work so i register and trembling because i lost all my friends, but then it magically signed me out again, i quit using discord, my account ElliottLian#4141 remains dead and never work, if you read this discord please bring my account back, or saying the token expired because i tried making a new password for my main discord account but it never works and another attempt it said token expired, i keep waiting and finally doesn't say token expired, and when i made a new password for my main discord account and remembered it, i was in a joyful mood, ready to login. But when i did, it just said it didn't work, i put it correctly and never work. I was crying, never meeting my friends I've met a long time ago when i started discord. I miss them, discord ruined my relationships with other people. If your reading this discord, please don’t mess this up for other people, you might ruin their day. Also, if you get a chance to revive my account send me a dm in gmail so i can see. You have ruined all my relationships. Good bye discord, its nice having you for a long time, but its time for me to go to another path of light, where it will never crap itself. Goodbye, Discord.",2,100.0,Akward dream,4
us,United States,7568593581,2021-07-12T09:26:28-07:00,Best app so far.,"As for all of the reviews claiming for this app to be bug filled and laggy, it’s not an issue as of discord itself. It’s a personal user mistake and wifi connectivity problem. I have been using discord for years, about six now, and I have never had an issue with lag or bugs. Even with all of the new updates. 
Only once has the calling been unavailable but that was because discord put it on hold to fix a connectivity issue, since discord calls aren’t the clearest out there.
I would definitely recommend this app to friends and family to keep in contact. I’ve created a whole community on discord and brought many people together, even saved lives. And I’m not being dramatic. This app gives people a way to vent and learn new things, meet new people, make connections.
I met the love of my life on this app and now we live together in person, in our own apartment! I’ve never been more happy. And before you call me some old nerd with a joy for gaming, I’m actually not a gamer, and I’m only 18 years old. (:
I recommend discord! It’s helped me through so much!",5,80.0,Ezephel Roman,1
us,United States,13732220612,2026-02-09T16:12:50-07:00,A company willing to risk everything and everyone to gain nothing but hallow honor,"If you haven’t heard or seen the press release yet, discord in its infinite wisdom is setting all accounts to “teen” by default sometime march 2026. This platform has been a lifeboat of culture, community, and companionship for several years now and is choosing to burn all that good will and positive public support to put its own consumer base at risk. Best case if this is truly the path they’re committed to is that the platform is mostly left abandoned as cybersecurity experts advise against following the new mandate and another competitor slides in and we repeat this cycle. Worse case discord is hacked, AGAIN, and the data and IDS of millions of users are leaked into the dark web exposing whole populations to identify theft, and with the “teen” filter now the default bad actors work around moderation guidelines to send or receive harmful content to/from minors. Truly the golden age of social media is over and we are now entering a dark age where companies put their entire consumer base at risk just to appear like they care about protecting minors without actually asking who’s at risk here. The dangers and risks here don’t take a college degree in ethics or computer science to grasp; and what we have is a nightmare scenario waiting to play out. Discord is officially a red flag level 9 security risk. DO NOT DOWNLOAD!",1,314.2,Oswin0526,0
us,United States,11648418954,2024-08-24T12:00:23-07:00,"Bloated, uneven, and inconsistent","Discord mobile is a bloated uneven mess that feels like its never fully working as intended. To start, the main navigation row is barely three buttons, Home, Notifications, and You. 99% of anything I do is under Home, Notifications is an unusable visual disaster that feels like it was thrown together in an afternoon, and You is something I am rarely ever actually using. So why have this navigation structure at all? Why is messages buried? It feels increasingly obvious that the Discord team is struggling to align the mobile user experience with what anyone is actually doing with their app. To make matters worse, it feels as if Discord mobile has been barely functioning for quite sometime now. So often my messages arent sending, double sending, not loading, and more. I pay $10 a month to simply be able to send emotes in my group chats, which feels like highway robbery, but I was willing to forego it in hopes of contributing to app I use everyday to hangout and talk with my friends. But as it stands, it feels as if Im throwing away $10 a month because that money clearly isnt improving UX/UI or performance of this app. Lets reign it on the overpriced micro transactions, and reprioritize the improvements and features that would have an actual impact on users.",2,243.1,Bjorlax,0
us,United States,10675760391,2023-12-09T12:32:08-07:00,"It would be the best social app, if they would just leave it alone.","Discord is a great base service. The idea is really simple and a great evolution of something like Skype and Teamspeak and Ventrilo. I’ve been using comm apps for games and just keeping up with people forever, and release discord was incredible. The customization and usability was unmatched and honestly it was fantastic. They keep updating and changing things that don’t need to be changed and I get changing usernames and everything, because it could be confusing for a different group of people, but completely changing the UI around to where people have to not only relearn it but to make it completely unintuitive for those people that did already know how the system worked is just plain nonsensical. Its constant updates of things that nobody asks for, people don’t like it, they get upset and cancel their subscriptions, they revert it, and the cycle seems to continue. I understand that they want to implement changes, but if you’re making money, which I know they are because EVERYBODY uses discord, and nobody is really asking for all these changes and updates. Why waste the time and effort on them to begin with? I just don’t understand breaking something that works perfectly fine.",2,207,ChasesLounge,2
us,United States,9958506900,2023-05-23T15:29:18-07:00,Opening profiles while in a voice channel needs reverted,"I just updated from a really old version of discord mobile so I don’t know how long it has been this way, but the way you open people’s profiles while in a voice channel is not a good mechanic. It used to be that you would press and hold for a short period of time and the profile popup would appear. Now, you have to press and hold for an unknown amount of time, just some time that is deemed “long enough” defined in the UI design, and then the profile appears (with volume slider, individual mute button etc) on release of the press and hold. I don't understand the purpose of this mechanic, or if this is a bug, but it is definitely not something I enjoy having to deal with when I’m in a voice channel and need to access someones profile popup while in the channel. Otherwise, the app seems to still be well laid out. This was the primary thing I noticed that drastically changed and it is not a short timer for the press and hold as was previously. It is definitely longer, then this combined with the activate on release behavior makes this difficult to use.",4,178.0,Comander fox,1
us,United States,3620236422,2019-01-06T12:03:16-07:00,Simply the best,"I started to use discord around a year ago, with that said I use it for everything, I own a few gaming teams and it is so nice to communicate with other team members, other teams, etc etc, I also use discord to communicate with friends, teammates ( especially in games where a mic is not supported ) discord does not affect my frames which is something I enjoy, I can still play my favorite games with discord open without sacrificing graphics or frame, I also have a few servers which I moderate and using bot support I can easily put up chat filters to prevent people from using certain words that may be deemed inappropriate, setting discord up was surprisingly easy and I had no trouble what so ever, I have never been let down by discord either, there servers have never been down allowing me to always communicate the quality is purely amazing, for any game devs out there I would use this as this app allowed my favorite developers to host polls, show updates, and even do giveaways, simply put this is the best way of communication for any devs, gamers, or fans, and even friends and would highly suggest that you get this app",5,2.4.1,Everett James,20
us,United States,3092468391,2018-08-20T15:54:29-07:00,Amazing App ❤️,"I really like Discord. It’s a great way to communicate with other people who has the same interests as you. I had originally heard about Discord through one of my friends. I was new to it at first, but then I started to see how some Youtubers and comics have a server in Discord. I joined a lot of servers and met a lot of different, unique people all around the world. Discord changed my view on some things. Like for starters, all strangers are bad. That is not true, at the very least for me. I’ve met so many honest and loyal friends online then I have ever met outside of the online world. Discord had helped me because this year, I had reach one of my very lowest point and I got through it because of everyone in Discord. There are many different varieties of servers from gamers to anime to writers. I ,like many others, use Discord as a way to escape reality. I am not really good at placing my trust in others because of my trust thats been broken in the past, but i felt safe with most of my friends now. On most days, I would go home and literally talk about the most random things and I never get bored. If I ever needed help in lets say homework, I would message someone and they would help me. One of my favorite things on Discord is VC also known as voice chat. Its where you basically talk through your device. One small thing that bugs me is whenever I join VC it sometimes crashes, but otherwise I don't really have a problem. All of my servers are friendly. There was rarely a time where I had to leave a server because of drama. Most if not all my servers have set rules and moderators to keep things in tact and not let anything get out of hand. Honestly this is such an amazing app to be yourself and make many many friends. You just have to be careful because this is after all the internet. :)",5,2.3.6,Jane 🍪,0
us,United States,11504029019,2024-07-17T09:33:36-07:00,How Discord Genuinly Is,"Discord is actually really amazing and helpful. I know a lot of people may not like discord but its because when people INTENTIONALLY try to find bad things, it WILL come there way. When that literally applies to any app or platform . Discord DOES its moderation and fast too unlike any other app. Its ment to keep you safe and the report system works. Its just that when you do thinks u know you shouldn't be doing like online dating (the cronically online ones)  or being weird on it you will find other weird people.. Thats not discords fault for YOU misusing the app then not liking it. People like this are easily avoidable and discord WILL keep ur account safe and keep you safe. 10/10 app I got hacked and they got back to me and less then 24 hours🫶 I love using discord to make friends and play online games and find new funny things i enjoy.  Lot of servers fit for my own personalities and its so fun talking to people with the same humor as me. End if the day, on any platform in the world there will ALWAYS be weirdos. But nobody takes care of them better then discord does🫶",5,238.0,elenimooo,0
us,United States,10670959559,2023-12-08T08:47:59-07:00,"Has potential to be good, if they change the UI back…","I’ve been using Discord since 2017, and throughout most of the time I’ve had the mobile app the UI has stayed pretty much the same. However, their most recent update, for whatever reason, decided to completely overhaul the UI and replace it with a new and worse one (think Facebook style.) It’s slow to navigate, hard to look at, and the new art style is just corporate blandness. I initially hated when they removed the ability to swipe left on a server page to see who was online, but grew complacent to it because i have better things to do than whine about one small feature being removed. But this new update completely changed the way the app is used all at once, and not in a functional way like Apple does with their big IOS updates that take a minute to get used to but are better in the long run. They even got rid of the classic Discord gray, which honestly is their biggest mistake. Whatever new shade they used makes the white text stand out way to sharply and glare off the screen even in regular light. Discord devs, idk if you’ve gone corporate because you have a monopoly on this style of communication app, but please listen to your users on this one and change the app back. The new one is really a change for the worse.",1,207,max14321,2
us,United States,10668630559,2023-12-07T17:28:04-07:00,New mobile UI is trash.,"I love discord, I’ve been using it as my main form of online communication for many many years now. Whenever there would be an update where certain things would change slightly, I was always okay with it and got used to it in no time. However, in the most recent update the user interface did a complete 360 from what it was before and now it looks and feels horrible. Discord’s interface was what set it apart from other messaging apps, once you figured it out it was comfortable and easy to navigate. Now, it is not only clunky and unnecessary, but it also forces us long-time discord users to completely relearn how to use the app. Also, the new look of video calls is horrid too. The space for the preview that you see yourself in is now much much smaller, so much so that if you’re more than like 8 inches away from your phone, you can’t see yourself. Changing it from a rectangle to a square is dumb too, because now you can’t see everything that your camera is capturing. You can’t see what’s actually in frame and what’s not. 
I know I’m not the only one who’s upset either. I believe the majority of discord users would agree with me that we want this UI gone. or at LEAST an option to revert it. Stop changing things Discord!! Your app was perfect how it was before!!!",1,207,Bod K.,2
us,United States,9576697560,2023-02-02T17:29:13-07:00,New updates causing more issues and inconveniences,"Back then, about almost soon to be 3 years, Discord had been an amazing app. However, all these updates are proving to bring inconveniences. They don’t bring any help and I haven’t even seen anything that ACTUALLY makes ANYTHING smoother. There’s been nothing. Everyone who I’ve met on Discord had agreed that the people of Discord are only downgrading the app as a whole. I’ve never really been on the web version because I can’t and it’s just not as easy for me to do it. I know there’s been new things and all, but it seems like it’s been EXTREMELY downgraded from how it originally was 3 years back in discord for mobile. Mobile has been worse. I can’t even see my entire screenshot anymore. I know some people may see this new update as useful, but it doesn’t help. It crops out multiple things in the image. The only images I’ve seen that don’t get cropped out most times are PC screenshots and phone pictures. Otherwise, they’re cropped. Discord has only changed mobile of all things, making it worse, which I’m on there all the time. And with these new updates? They’re quite literally making my discord crash more, being MORE buggy, and all sorts of other things. I’ve seen many people wanting to revert back to older versions of discord, which were much easier to use as well, and myself included. Look, I know all I really talked about was how much more buggier updates were for Discord and how the images aren’t even showing fully and are being widened just like PC pictures would. Respond to this as you will, but I’ll say it here. You guys need to change discord back to how it was. All these updates are way too close in my opinion and only make it buggier and worse for specifically mobile users (which I know there’s many mobile users).",3,163.0,Neo91502,0
us,United States,13736559544,2026-02-10T22:01:04-07:00,Avoid this platform like the plague it is!,"Discord had an id data breach, and yet has the audacity to expect us to trust it with our personal information, even after getting hacked?! There’s a dystopian update coming in march, it will require a facial or id scan to even be able to use features you can currently use, those features will be locked. I suggest switching to something else if you won’t be able to message friends without letting this janky platform sell your personal data. If a law passes requiring a facial scan, I would suggest fighting it and not give in. Don’t support this dystopian future, let these companies go bankrupt! It’s not about safety, it’s about money and control. There’s a platform called skylight, I haven’t fully tried it yet, but it’s like TikTok and you should be able to chat without taking extra steps like facial or id scans. It’s a fairly new platform, so give it some time and patience because it’s not run by some billionaires, it’s still in the works, but maybe worth a try. Besides, what have you got to lose, Besides another risk of discord getting hacked and your personal information getting sold by discord or the hacker? It’s a GREAT thing to lose! Because honestly, nobody wants unnecessary deadweight to gain like what discord is dumping out the rear and trying to force feed us with.",1,315.0,Oldturd999,0
us,United States,12402515396,2025-03-09T17:35:19-07:00,So many bugs it’s ridiculous,"Every single time I open this app there are bugs. I delete and reinstall on the App Store. Still bugs. Bugs not being able to hear people on a call or vice versa. Bugs with text showing up in the typing bar when I already sent the message. Calls and messages still going through while on do not disturb. Bugs where you cannot adjust stream volume and if you have muted a stream on the computer, then you are screwed and their stream will be muted on mobile indefinitely. Bugs where people’s audio gets messed up and robotic. Bugs where notifications for messages are delayed by hours. Bugs where messages are sent but then disappear and were never sent to begin with. Do you get the picture? For a company that is as big as discord it is pathetic that they haven’t worked out these issues.

Edit: Discord Reached out saying to check the server notification settings, then change the password to fix it?? The issue is not with sever notifications but direct messages. When do not disturb was on, dms were still going off on my phone. Additionally, when I was not on do not disturb, it would sometimes take hours for messages to show up as a notification on the mobile app. Love how discord support also ignored all of the other bugs I mentioned.",1,269.0,Katiecatt1804805,0
us,United States,12386410853,2025-03-05T15:10:28-07:00,Huge security risk,"I’ve been using Discord for a while, but the app has some serious issues that make it a headache to use. When I’m on a voice channel, it freezes way too often, locking me in the call with no way to disconnect unless I force close the app entirely. Worse, the app has this infuriating bug where it unmutes users repeatedly in the middle of a voice channel. It’s happened to me countless times—every time I get a phone call or open another app while listening in, it unmutes me without warning. This isn’t just a glitch; it’s a huge security risk, exposing private chats to anyone nearby. For an app built around communication, these problems are unacceptable. Until they fix this, it’s a 1-star experience for me. Avoid if you value reliability and privacy.

UX bug: Disruptive Chat Scrolling One of Discord’s most frustrating UX issues rears its head when scrolling through a chat page. As I’m reading or navigating older messages, the app suddenly jolts and jumps around whenever new messages are posted. This interrupts my scrolling experience, yanking me out of context and forcing me to lose my place. It’s not just jarring—it’s unnecessary. If I want to move, I can do it myself or choose to jump to the latest message. A simple fix, like locking the view until I opt to shift, would go a long way.",1,269.0,Manny-n,1
us,United States,11035105941,2024-03-11T20:42:19-07:00,stop adding new features and then taking them away,"discord moves the tabs to the bottom of the screen. ok. i try to get used to that. then they switch it back to the top. then they put a pop out tab for your profile. then they add something else and then change that. muscle memory is a joke for mobile, it will be in that spot until discord decides they want a shiny new UI that no one asked for and then you need to relearn the app all over again (which gets changed AGAIN). they cannot and will not accept that they are making bad choices for their app, will double down and say “you just have to get used to it” and then that thing you got used to? yeah now they changed it again. and god forbid they actually fix a bug. they did the new UI update which broke vc, your stream pop up would disappear, your camera cannot be in landscape mode without freezing the app or causing the image to stretch, they really out here not only making stupid changes to a perfectly fine app, but laying off employees randomly that they probably needed (i mean look at this app, they need the manpower for this sack of garbage). 

stop changing things. stop assuming what your consumers want. stop monetizing every single aspect of your stupid app. just stop. you are ruining the app with each unnecessary UI update.",1,219.1,i hate discord69,1
us,United States,10677905805,2023-12-10T02:57:58-07:00,Forced update,"I like discord-or, well I liked discord-but I didn’t sign up for automatic updates and that’s what they did here. My entire mobile discord changed and when I went to write this review, I saw that there’s an option to update, which was like an insult almost. 
For starters, when I sideswipe to the right now, rather than go to my members list of a server, it replies a message. The reply part would have been a good part but having it replace member swiping was…a choice.
The UI change was also bad. They didn’t even have the decency to do a tutorial of where everything is, I only found out where the members list was after clicking through everything (it’s in the channel name now).
The background of a vc is now a sunset type of color, which again would be fine, but my friend who uses midnight mode and my other friend who uses dark mode both said it looked the same. I use light mode and it looks the same. I haven’t found an option to change it and, I suspect, I will not (in fact, I suspect they might charge for the privilege to change it, which is very cynical of me, but I have no more good will towards this app).
I don’t think I can, in good conscience, recommend anyone use this app or spend money on it, and the second there’s a good alternative to discord, I am going to jumping ship.",1,207,watchdogsunlimited,2
us,United States,10666513756,2023-12-07T03:51:58-07:00,"Discord was good when it was a messenger app, not social media","I have been using discord basically since the beginning. It's gone through a lot of changes, and the vast majority have been tolerable, but the latest update has turned discord into an app I use solely because my friends do. If another messenger app came out, I'd swap in a heartbeat.
The extra dark background on dark mode is harsher against the white text. It causes eye strain.
The notifications tab, one of 4 tabs on the bottom bar, doesn't even get the badge when you get a notification. The badge shows up on either the server tab, or the DMs tab. Why even have a notifications tab if your notification badges don't show up there? If I wanted to find my previous mentions, I would use the search function and find ""mentions: me"". Easy! A whole tab for it is unnecessary.
It used to be easy to get from a server to DMs and back again. Just a swipe and a tap. Now you have to tap twice, swapping between tabs. You used to be able to see who was messaging you just by swiping to the side. You stayed where you were on whatever server you were in, you just now could see someone's profile pic and the notification badge with the amount of messages from them. Now you only see the number badge on the DMs tab. Just the number of how many total messages you have. You have to leave the server channel you're in to even see WHO messaged you, and then to get back to the server you'd better have turned off their ""auto-enter into the homepage of this server"" or else you'll have to go back to the channel you were in manually.
Discord is best when it is used for its actual purpose- text messaging and picture sending. Discord shouldn't be treated as a social media. If I wanted to go to social media, I'd go to reddit, or snapchat, or facebook, or anything else.",3,207,NonbinarLee,2
us,United States,10665225781,2023-12-06T17:53:49-07:00,New Update,"I've been on different accounts on Discord since 2019, many of my friends have been around since 2016 and we all hate the new update. It's a shame to see that the toggle was removed; it was a great choice to keep it for those who were uncomfortable with the new layout while also allowing the ones who enjoyed it to be able to experience the freshness of it. Seeing how Discord has basically told its users, especially the ones who are paying, to simply ""get used to it"", I would no longer recommend this app to people anymore. How can the users get used to something buggy and inconvenient?

Users appreciated the simplicity of the old format and being able to get everything done with a few swipes. Many people are now bringing up the issue of bugs, being unable to upload files, slow messaging, delayed notifications, etc. I personally am experiencing crashes and am unable to navigate the new system. Again, how can the users get used to something buggy and inconvenient?

It's a shame to see how Discord is responding to those who are giving out constructive criticism and feedback. It is no longer worth spending the money on an app that doesn't listen to its majority of users. Bring the ""new layout"" toggle back. There was nothing wrong with the old layout.",1,207,no maidens,2
us,United States,9562918621,2023-01-29T23:46:06-07:00,Help,"This app logged me out several times and it won't let me log in no matter how many accounts I make. It logged me out, but I already saved my acc password and user, so I tried using that. It failed saying that the email was not registered so I thought ""oh it's no big deal I can just try registering again with the same email cause it says the email is apparently 'not registered' yet"" so I did that and THEN sit said that the email was 'already registered' Okay WHAT?! So I tried creating an acc again, it failed. I tried signing back IN again, still a fail. And I know it's not my technology glitching our non kyle and that it's apps fault be no matter how many devices I tried to switch to, it still wouldn't work. I used to like this app a bit before this stuff started happened cause this app is really good for like if your friend dosent have a phone and can only text on pc or something like that and it's also good for gaming and streaming I guess but if you keep getting logged out, there's no point of giving the app a good review, especially if your like me and have been downloading and deleting the app several times with no success and have literally been trying this for over 4 DAYS STRAIGHT!!!! The developers) should really fix this problem before it gets a lot more bad reviews due to this glitch.",1,162.0,I don’t let me use the app,0
us,United States,7449753490,2021-06-10T12:21:58-07:00,Only because it could be better,"Look. Discord is a good place. But unfortunately, it’s money hungry. They have made NITRO a seriously outrageous thing. It costs loads of money to get features you don’t want! 🤦🏻‍♂️ I only want bigger video quality and the ability for banner on my server and that’s it. That alone will cost me a heck of a lot (I think like $54 a month and that’s just for 13 boosts. It’s assumed you’d be on Nitro I guess which has 2 boosts) Unfortunately, I can’t spend $54 a month to get these features. They do come with other features, but I don’t want those nor do I care for them. I want just the two. I think discord would make more money if they offered these individually to it’s server hosts. There’s lots of servers out there like mine that have about 50 or so people and we don’t want much else but a nice banner for the looks and more video sending ability. Perhaps making these features for individual subscription (Example being for a banner $1.29 a month and the aforementioned Video size capability be $3.29) this would mean I’d be only spending about $5 a month which may not sound huge now, but that’s just me. Imagine if the prices were this cheap for the masses? Discord may have about 1,000 servers who subscribe for tier 1-3 for boosts, but imagine having 100,000 servers subscribed for things they wanted and it be cheaper than the other option they currently allow. It would bring in more money from their community and give them what they want. Would I prefer it to be a one time charge and it be permanent? Yes, but I also see why they don’t do that. So I do strongly believe they’d make more money if they simply put these things up for individual subscription. It would help the other 999,000 servers out there. Thank you for your time~",3,78.0,ItsGreat9426104,0
us,United States,6327728930,2020-08-16T16:06:21-07:00,It could’ve been better..,"It’s actually a really good app but once I accidentally Unfriended someone and couldn’t send them request again cause I did not know their tag number , I wish we could see our Unfriended people list but I can’t even when I got the discord data package I even tried emailing the support team but they did not even reply to emails, and still I try to contact that person who is very important to me but I don’t get any response because I know that person always uses discord but yea.... Or instead of showing the unfriended people list I wish we could just search the user or a feel letters of a user and then there could be a lot of users with tag numbers instead of user name and tags number to send that person a friend request but when you search some person up any user with the similar name it still doesn’t show up , and you can’t even have your own profile so others can see who you are and if they want to send a friend request. Id anyone knows anything about the user Superskillz or I think superskills please let me know send me a friend request in discord UnicornLady#0248 thanks bye",4,34.0,XxAlexisWillsXx,1
us,United States,10947514194,2024-02-16T21:32:27-07:00,Mobile update made things a lot worse to navigate.,"Double update: they sent the same bot to reply to the updated review. Not even a genuine human response. Just the same link to the FAQ which i already complained about. You cannot make this stuff up. Im actually convinced they have some poor intern picking and choosing what to respond to, because this is the most petty i have ever seen a company stoop when their own update is being blasted by their users. 

UPDATE: thanks for the worthless developer response! Now i wish I could leave 0 stars instead of just 1. I asked for you to fix your app, not to tell me why you refuse to fix it with a link to an FAQ section telling me all you want is to update the app to please investors. Your investors do not use this daily, they are not your customers, they are not your moderators. Trash app, moving onto other alternatives as they clearly only want Nitro subs and no free users. too many clicks to reach anywhere. even considering muscle memory. getting to pins in channels is a pain. swiping around accidentally causes replies. just infuriating mix of weird UX changes for MOBILE. for PC fine, put everything into 100 sub folders. for mobile i feel like my options within a server, which is why people use this, are worse and complicated. who cares about reaching DMs faster with a tab when people get notifications on their phone to reach DMs anyways?? just weird decisions. No one is using discord as their main messaging app and if they did, no one was complaining about how DMs were placed. Now everything is really cramped despite them freeing up space? Never felt claustrophobic from my phone until this new UI update.",1,216.0,New TGC Fan,0
us,United States,10672716247,2023-12-08T19:21:51-07:00,"awful UI, inaccessible, eyesore","new update went through despite the fact that I have updates for everything turned off. mobile layout now functionally useless and actively frustrating to navigate. no more swiping to see who’s online, group dms/ dms are in a different menu you have to navigate to separate from servers, no more swiping in and out of chats, useless and distracting clutter at top of dms/group dms sidebar. and that’s just what i’ve noticed from my 2 seconds using it since, because i have been unable and unwilling to use it again after the update. not only is it unintuitive and the exact opposite of the previously ergonomic setup, it’s just really, awfully, truly ugly. coming from someone who used to work in graphic design. clunky. inaccessible. so bad i will honestly delete my mobile app and move platforms if it persists, despite the fact that i have used discord near-daily for the last 5+ years. makes opening discord on mobile dread-inducing. there is no option to revert, no response to the two support tickets i sent in, and the new color change (which you also can’t change back) has poor contrast and has been causing me headaches and eye strain. if i could give one star i would. if you want to use discord anymore, don’t get the app: it’s a waste of mobile space.",1,207,solipsismc,2
us,United States,10668066335,2023-12-07T13:14:36-07:00,Please change it back.,"I recently got the new update with the new set up and I’m not a fan personally. I love discord as a app for communicating with friends and I’ve had it for  but this new set up is way to complex. I liked swiping on the screen to see the members in a chat or being able to swipe over and see the servers I’m in. This new set up is just more complicated than it needs to be switching between chats and servers would be as easy as a simple swipe before but now we have to click the back button or swipe out and switch to messages or servers depending whichever you’re trying to access. Don’t get me wrong I get why this change was made but this is just going to continue to confuse old users. I’m even confused on certain things such as how you view all the members on your server. I’ve had discord for a little longer than 3 years now and to have such a sudden change in the format is just going to confuse us and make us unhappy. I’ve seen multiple people complain about it on discord already, so please consider changing it back or letting us have to option to change it to the other format.",4,207,the_local_demon,0
us,United States,10589871356,2023-11-15T17:28:21-07:00,"Amazing app, but terrible update bug.","I love this app, as it it my primary source of communication between me and many of my friends. I use it to play games and have conversations with my friends all around the world. Anyways, onto the point. I updated Discord today after seeing it was in need of one. One issue I've had since the update was constantly having the ""Connecting..."" issue. About every three seconds I would get stopped by this issue, not letting me send messages or watch videos all the way through. I usually wouldn't have a problem with this, since it would usually be a small connection issue that would easily be fixed by closing and reopening the app, but no matter what I do it won't stop saying ""Connecting...""
After talking with some friends of mine I figured out it's not only me that's going through this. Several people who have updated their Discord have had the connection issue and the time in between the times it connects keeps getting shorter. I've checked the connection issues by opening other apps, but all of them work perfectly fine. I truly hope this issue gets resolved soon, so I can continue to communicate with my friends.",3,204.0,DrawnInStyle,0
us,United States,3523424104,2018-12-12T10:31:58-07:00,Worst App I’ve ever used,"Discord app in a word is a nightmare. The first major problem is the captchas. They are completely broken. Let’s say it chooses “buses”. You can click all buses and it will tell you that you’re wrong. It will continually replace the photos you use 5-10 times so you have to continue clicking through them. The whole process takes entirely too long and is just bad. The second problem is if you forget your password you have to go through the entire captcha process before it will tell you if your password you entered was correct or not. So if you try 5 passwords, you go through the process 5 times. Third, if you login from somewhere that isn’t the exact spot you login before the app will not let you log in and instead will “email you” to confirm your log in. Except they never actually email you. I’ve done this a dozen times. My email is my own. The couple times it’s worked it has come hours later and the app will say it’s expired. If you ever actually log in to Discord it’s very difficult to find new communities. Third party websites are much more useful for that. The grey color with white writing is hard to read and it constantly refreshes so if you are trying to get caught up in the convo you are continually brought back to the bottom. I used java run chat rooms as a child in the 2000s that ran like butter compared to this.

Edit: According to Dev advice I used a desktop to get into my account much easier. However, my one star rating stands as it is for the app version and as a standalone app it should be able to help users get back into their accounts without having to use a different device.",1,2.4.0,vx850,0
us,United States,9112265702,2022-09-22T21:32:14-07:00,The app was AMAZING until this happened..,"First off, Discord was super good and I had my old account for like over 2-3 years, but one day I was just chilling listening to music and I go to text one of my friends on Discord, and I was signed out of my account. I thought it was just a glitch and brushed it off, so I went to sign back in and it said my account was disabled! This has been a recent glitch, and it happened to two of my friends and they got their accounts back, so I just wrote the Discord team an e-mail stating that my account was falsely disabled and I wish to have it back, but about a day later they finally responded saying that my account was permanently disabled for “breaking the TOS and Community Guidelines”???? I had that account for over 2-3 years and I had a bunch of important stuff and friends that I still haven’t talked to since on there because I only knew them on Discord and no other app and I forgot their usernames. I also had a whole server, that I now can’t do anything with anymore because my main account was the creator of the server. But I have never broke the TOS or Community Guidelines. But other than the random disabling accounts glitch the app is great.",3,145.0,KuromiDrankMyMonster,1
us,United States,7644319269,2021-08-01T16:04:06-07:00,Maybe it’s Me,"Let me start by saying that I’ve used the mobile app before and had no issues previously. However, ever since I switched to my iPad Air 4th gen, I hav heard nothing but problems with the app. For one, I can’t use it while it’s in the background. Before, I could use the app while doing other things, such as using the internet browser. Nowadays, if I leave the app, everything on my end stops working. I can’t hear anyone speaking, my mic doesn’t pick up my voice, nothing works. This problem persists even if I disconnect and reconnect. Most annoyingly this problem will persist even if I restart the app. The only solution I’ve found is to restart the entire tablet.

The above is already problem enough but I figured if I just stay on the app without leaving, I wouldn’t have the same issues. Nope, I still encounter the above issues after a certain amount of time with no reason for it. The only reason I’m not sure if it’s discord or my iPad Air is that I don’t encounter these same problems on a different iPad. It’s only on my iPad Air do these problems occur. But I have tried everything from updating both the app and the iPad, to deleting the app and reinstalling. Nothing has worked and I’m stuck with the problems.",2,84.0,GodOfPhail,1
us,United States,4416029442,2019-07-05T13:17:39-07:00,"My Favorite Social App, But...","I’ve been using Discord for about a year and half now, the app for maybe a year. They’re been a lot of improvements since then that I was happy to see. The CallKit was definitely not one of them. I wish there was an option to at least disable it. I don’t like my Discord calls showing up in my history. I don’t like Discord calls ringing on my phone like a normal call. 
Also, I’ve had a lot of audio problems since it was added. My alarm goes off? Can’t hear or talk anymore, have to leave and rejoin the call. Someone calls my phone? I can’t just mute my mic and answer anymore. I have to hang up. And even if I decline the call? Audio problems. Can’t hear. I also hardly ever get proper notifications anymore. People send me messages, but I don’t realize I get them because the sound doesn’t go off while I’m in a call. A few times I just never got a notification at all. And I’ve missed a lot of calls because Discord never rang. 
I actually like the new update that lets you choose whether or not to use speaker. I was sad to see the option go, so I’m glad it’s back. Wish speaker was default though. Still, it’s nice to have the option.",4,3.0.4,GreatestDownfall,7
us,United States,2075345436,2018-01-10T05:03:42-07:00,pokémon servers got me hacked,"i got discord for spoofing for pokémon go and i was in several big time servers pokedex poke x pokémon league go sniper     well things just fine for a long time but random stuff started happening like credit cards hacked mine and my bfs . then an itunes purchase.  come to find out this pokémon discords have like master coders and programmers .  so my suggestion is to be careful all it took for me was seeing weird letters they were posting o.o in like 5 of the channels i was in, then i searched them and there were hundred of them all over all of the discords. Which seems really strange almost like they were targeting certain people when they said it . The people were in other discords as well acting like new people . So my suggestion is to be careful on any of those discords. I even signed up for nitro which there was a webhook attached to my personal discord just for account called spybot. Be careful just play the game and i would not talk to anyone there. i made friends with them there and they kept promoting. me to different roles and then i started donating accounts and i gave itunes gift cards to help. Looking back i was stupid to think anyone on the internet actually cared about helping other people . Do not donate and be careful if u join pokedex100
poke ex.   pokémon go league  go snipers go raiders.    dead shrimp society.   unpwn bot.   pokesnipers catch em all . None of them. they are some how all connected and it seems to be not about playing pokémon but making money . I am sad i ever joined discord .",1,2.2.0,tabby45140,0
us,United States,10643926640,2023-11-30T18:50:23-07:00,No-Sign In Bug Problem,"Hey I’ve been using Discord for about a year now, and I’ve mainly used it to chat and communicate with friends, explore and stuff. But I just recently got a new phone and I wanted to install Discord so I could transfer data on it. The downloading part was easy, but as soon as I opened the app, I got stuck on the main screen loading screen for what felt like eons. And no matter how hard I tried to figure out what the problem was it always brought me back to that same screen. I literally did all that someone with that issue would be expected to do, I reset the app, uninstalled it then downloaded it back again, checked for updates, and looked at tutorials online to see if I’d missed a step. Not to mention that when I tried to long into your web browser, it kept rejecting my pass. And there was no “Login with Google” option either. I don’t know whether or not I’m the only one experiencing this error, but I feel it’s happened one time too many to be ignored. Please look into this. But overall, the app works pretty well.",5,206.0,Lilac stone 2008,0
us,United States,7515858451,2021-06-28T08:26:19-07:00,"Great so far, but add updates for mobile.","It’s an amazing app! There’s just some things that I hate, like add some mobile updates? The updates you guys add to pc should also head to mobile too. After all, it’s an amazing app I recommend you guys to download it. I have just saw that you guys just made the app 17+, coming from a 15 year old I think you guys should make it back too like to 13+ because people older then 13 have already downloaded it (like me). Also think you should allow us to type more then the limit of 2000 it gets very annoying, for example your gonna write a paragraph for someone and it’s very important and it’s about 5000 word long. Even though it has some issues, very amazing app and I’m always on there for like 8 hours a day to talk with friends and stuff! I’m always making servers In discord, but I think you should really do something about those hyphens and get rid of it so we can have our own fonts to add and watch out for what you do to your app, because people underage are now faking there age and when they were born, I once saw my 8 year old sister in discord! Please watch out.",4,80.0,TokyoTobio,3
us,United States,10664302285,2023-12-06T11:03:59-07:00,Incredible app BUT….,"Been using discord for years and man is it possible one of the greatest services ever, definitely my most used app on my phone as well as on my computer. I have nothing against discord or the team and am thankful for everything they’ve done,,,, up until this point. WHAT IS THIS NEW UI?!?!?! Why make us tap more buttons for less ease of access. OG design was perfect as is. I’d rather still be able to swipe left just to see who’s online then have to tap the server button on top and be taken to a separate tab that doesn’t even follow your theme. Replies are overrated and shouldn’t be a main focus for a core function, the old way of replying was fine, and replies are ONLY common in massive servers since the majority of users are in either small group chats or private servers to play with friends. I can understand wanting to separate servers from dms but what was so great about the previous layout is how simple it was to navigate. I’m sure everyone along with myself were fine with having dms be right at the top of your server list. Having every page be a swipe away made it very user friendly and brought everything together on one localized page, whereas now we have to manually go to different tabs which just interferes with our muscle memory of being able to see who’s online in a small group chat and join vc in a bigger server in a pretty short amount of time. I’m all for new updates and optimizations but I’m not so sure about this. A community vote for the design change prior definitely would’ve spread more and give the developers a perspective of where we stand. I trust y’all will come together and figure something out, you’ve always done what’s best for the community and we greatly appreciate that, thank you.",2,207,Zander_Flash,0
us,United States,5864187190,2020-04-25T17:39:42-07:00,Good on PC but on mobile...,"Perfect on PC, well... the camera mode on PC nearly broke my PC and broke my discord, so I had to delete it. So I used the online version and it does work and so when it was broke on my PC I was trying to fix it but I gave up after a while, so I downloaded it on mobile to be able to talk to my friend because he can’t call or text. So I go on the mobile version of discord and I like to talk to him and the sound is broke. I can hardly hear him, so I turn up the volume, doesn’t work, turn up the discord volume, doesn’t work, and finally I turn up his volume so I can hear him better, (and you wouldn’t guess this) IT DOES NOT WORK. Only then do I find the online, but I do want to play with him when I’m not at my house and I hope it works this time. The only reason I gave it 5 ⭐️’s because it helps me reach my friends that I can’t call or text and it works well when I don’t use the camera, and I could get in contact with online friends that I don’t know irl without giving to much information but I get to talk with them. I hope to get a developer response explaining why I had problems.",5,18.0,dear pixel gun,0
us,United States,10116657006,2023-07-08T02:03:18-07:00,Major Features Don’t Work For Me,"For some reason, whenever I click on a link to join a person’s discord server, it will direct me to the app and it won’t do anything else. I don’t join their server, and I don’t know how to fix it. The website would always direct me to the app no matter what, so I can’t just do it on the discord website. Also, when I upload an audio file, say from Google Drive, that file is no longer accessible to me. If I download that same file from Discord, it won’t play any sound. It’s just a corrupted file. These two things are how I use this app, and if it can’t function properly, than the app serves no purpose to me. And whenever I do to their website to try to use Discord from there, it keeps “suggesting” me to download the app. It’s just a huge headache that isn’t worth the trouble.

This is just a nit-pick, but I wish there was a feature were there was a search engine to look for public discord servers and join through that, rather than using a link alone. It’ll make things a lot more easier than searching far and wide to see if a particular creator or influencer has a Discord server, let alone a link to join automatically. The links can be used to join private discord servers instead.",2,185.1,ThatOneGuy012,0
us,United States,4634117908,2019-08-17T20:20:55-07:00,"Amazing app, one suggestion though. Please read.","I absolutely love this app. Finding a gaming partner is way easier using this! I’ve actually found a group of people that I frequently game with and talk to that I honestly really love. My experience this past year has been really amazing, and without trouble. However, only one thing really annoyed me in my time using discord. When you want to leave a server you’ve created, you have the option to pass ownership to someone you trust or someone that’s qualified. It isn’t the same for group chats, though. If I had created a group chat, and had to leave, I would also want to pass the ability of owner to someone trusted, but it randomly picks a member to make the new owner. As the owner, I think I should be the one making that choice. Because even though I absolutely love my discord friends, some of them tend to abuse the power of owner chaotically, and I don’t want to be added back into that kind of environment. Leaving a group chat you and wanting to be added back soon just leads to you crossing your fingers and hoping someone worthy got the crown.",5,3.1.0,amyzthesht,4
us,United States,1839585535,2017-10-10T07:57:36-07:00,Pretty Good,"All in all, it's a great app.  In fact, I'd say it's nearly perfect on PC.  However, there are some features on PC that you can just not access on mobile.  For example, you can't change privacy settings to turn off DMs on a certain server, which can be a struggle for people with, uh, fans.  Another thing is that you can't change somebody's role on mobile, which is very aggravating. I'm a moderator on a server and we have a specific role to give to misbehaving people which prevents them from sending messages.  But, I can only do my job as moderator if I'm on my PC, because mobile won't let me change roles.  In addition, for whatever reason, certain pictures refuse to upload, and it’s not the channel settings because it’s only with certain pictures (only on mobile).  The last thing I recommend, which is currently neither on mobile or PC, is having some version of read receipts for DMs.  I know that's probably gonna be controversial, but I personally know that some of my friends are big YouTubers, so they get caught up, and forget.  However, if I was able to tell if they'd read my message, I'd be able to yell at — er, uh, talk to them about it.",4,1.9.2,Ley0301,24
us,United States,11675669775,2024-08-31T20:31:25-07:00,Discord team needs updates (links are hard to find),"Dear Discord Team, I hope this message finds you well. I have some suggestions that I believe could significantly enhance the user experience for server owners and members: 1. Search Groups Feature: Adding a ""search groups"" function would make it easier to find and join specific communities on Discord. This feature would help users discover groups based on their interests and ensure they can connect with relevant communities more efficiently, instead of links that are hard to find. 2. Allow Only Friends Option: It would be incredibly helpful if server owners could set their servers to ""allow only friends"" mode. This would ensure that only users who are already friends with the server owner can join, preventing random users from accessing private communities. 3. Permanent and Temporary Kicking Options: Implementing options to kick users either permanently or temporarily would be a great feature. This would allow server owners to manage their communities more effectively, especially if someone joins before stricter settings are applied. I believe these features would provide more control and flexibility for server management and enhance the overall experience on Discord. Thank you for considering these suggestions! Best regards, Tommy",1,244.0,Verigant Player,0
us,United States,11457245333,2024-07-04T17:58:59-07:00,discord ui,"i have been using discord since 2020 - i used to love the mobile app for ios. it was easy to use and had the same features as the desktop. now i find myself extremely frustrated when video chatting on the new UI. two of the main features that have gone away are the ability to hide your own video and have separate volumes for media and voice when watching someone’s shared screen. the fact that we can’t even change the layout of the videos is also bothersome. when in a shared activity on mobile, the video cameras go between the everyone instead of just staying on my partner when we’re video chatting. i feel like this was such a downgrade and i hope these features get added soon. it makes me not want to use discord mobile any longer - even though it’s the main form of communication between my partner and i. this UI has potential, but i feel like we’re far from it on ios mobile. response to developer: im unsure if you read the review - the issue isn’t the volume, the issue is there are no SEPARATE volume controls anymore like there used to be on the old version.

*iphone pip is no longer working as of 7.1.24*",3,236.0,21Jennlew,0
us,United States,11376674989,2024-06-13T07:05:45-07:00,Go back to the old layout,"I’m very unimpressed as I’ve woken up to Discord updating without letting me know to change the layout once again. The first time they changed the mobile layout, it was actually not bad. The direct messages had their own space, you had your own space for your profile, and your servers had their own space. I liked this layout after I got used to it, as it was very easy for me to navigate and get adjusted to. However, with this new update that I know I’m behind on, I’m very disappointed with how much the layout has changed. Direct messages are no longer in their own area and are now at the top of your servers, extending the server list when you get notifications, and the actual direct messages list is very small and cluttered. Notifications taking up one whole area makes no sense to me, as I don’t get very many notifications for friend requests, mentions, etc. so I don’t see the point in it. Not the mentions the notifications themselves for your phone. They look like a Discord version of Facebook notifications, which is very annoying to me. This new layout will take me a lot more time to get used to and I don’t think I’ll ever like it even after I get used to it. It’s very cluttered and it seems like it was done in a hurry as a way to improve user experience, but myself and others I talk to very much hate this layout. At this point, I’m only using discord to stay connected with some friends and to use a few bots. Otherwise I would’ve deleted it just because of this layout. Please either allow us the option to go back to one of the old layouts or don’t change the layouts in the first place, especially so close together. I don’t think I even had the old layout for a full year and it was already changed when there was nothing wrong with it.",2,233.0,Theoneandonly_Crystal,0
us,United States,10678870640,2023-12-10T08:06:48-07:00,Discord hates their community.,"Let me preface this by saying that I’ve been an active user on Discord since July 2015. I’ve been in countless communities, and actively been invested in Discord’s mission for almost a decade now. That being said, it is becoming increasingly aware that Discord no longer cares about the community that made them what they are. Adding bloat features, such as the nitro only profile cosmetic shop, unnecessary popups for purchasing nitro, or forcing strangers’ activities onto your client, all of this serves to slow down the program, with no option to opt out. Anti accessibility features are becoming more apparent, (one of their blog posts literally implies they know this is an issue, but ‘get used to it’) forcing a new ux onto users with vision problems, with no option to revert to something that doesn’t harm them to use. I am personally affected by this, because a certain friend of mine (who is blind) can no longer use the app. Discord customer service is no longer run by people, only a bot that will paste the same response on every twitter post or app review. I was once comfortable and even proud to use this app, but this company is now actively hostile towards it’s userbase. Check out Revolt Chat for an open source communication app that won’t push microtransactions and bloat onto your device.",1,207,SeaShrimples,4
us,United States,6937538007,2021-01-31T11:52:40-07:00,Great potential for adolescents if used safely,"The app is easy to use, especially on the desktop version. It allows users to really make the app what they want. They can use the app as a very social experience that ensures their connections to friends, even in such a secluded time of COVID. But users can also use it as an individual experience and can find others online who are interested in similar topics. The app's design is excellent, and I had a lot of fun playing around with the different settings and searching through the public communities with topics ranging from mental health to memeology. It is set up like Slack, so I could easily engage and explore because of my experience with that app. I also think it’s great that the user’s profile can be fully customizable and doesn’t come from an option list of user settings, such a pre-selected avatar pictures. Scanning the app, it seems like users can use their creativity with their profile and can use a real picture of themselves or just a meme with no identifying information. 

The weaknesses of the app include its accessibility and its privacy settings. There was no specific mention of accessibility, so it may be difficult to use the app if the user experiences vision disability or something similar. Also, while a user can opt out of certain cookies, there is no way to do a blanket opt out of the app's privacy collection processes. I also didn't like that I couldn't see possible friends that could already have a Discord account because there was no connection to my phone contacts or my contacts from any other social media account. However, I can also see the argument for this being a positive because it can be a completely separate program from all other apps the user uses, which is difficult to find sometimes because of the merging tech companies.",4,58.1,sarcampb,0
us,United States,5581096034,2020-02-25T19:52:25-07:00,The worst form of social media,"Out of all of the social media platforms I’ve tried, discord I would say is the most toxic of them. 
And it’s not because the employees and staff working at discord are mean, or anything, it’s because of the nature of the setup discord chooses to use. Essentially when you join a server, the guidelines you have are the ones the owner sets for you. Larger servers are often governed by mods. But the problem is that these mods generally don’t have too many qualifications to be a moderator. And when the mods are ineffective at creating a safe environment, that’s when toxic behavior thrives. Discord does have some policies, on its ToS but these are generally very simple rules, and are few and far between. I’ve had many terrible experiences on servers where toxic behavior is present and the mods either do nothing about it or they take the wrong course of action. Now this isn’t something discord has much control over, but rather design of the website in it’s entirety is flawed. I wouldn’t recommend this app to people who who are not in a healthy state of mind, or to anyone in general. However I guess discord works for some people and if you find that this style of social media works for you then by all means download it. But do be prepared for possible toxic behavior thrown your way.",2,3.2.0,fkeglyzlhzltal,14
us,United States,11316970448,2024-05-28T09:30:10-07:00,iPad functionality,"I like using this platform and won’t stop anytime soon, but it gets unfriendlier to iPad users with every successive update. I can barely use it on my iPad without some part of the interface breaking and forcing me to restart the app, or sometimes my entire device due to endless crashing. Updates continually break on other platforms, but especially iPad, probably because fewer people use it.

Edit: I removed another star because they remade the iPhone interface for iPad, despite an iPad lacking the compactness that makes phone users benefit from those changes. Now the app is far harder to use, and the black theme causes eye strain even with adjusted contrast and saturation. If you hit the “search” button by accident, there’s no way to exit the search menu other than restarting the app. The member list used to be easily accessible without hiding chat, the main feature of discord, but now you can only see either chat or the member list, and not both at the same time. The “swipe to reply” feature also makes you edit your own messages, and that inconsistency trained me to continue using a long press to reply like I’d been doing before. It’s so much clunkier and harder to use now.",2,230.0,tomaytotomahto1103,1
us,United States,10730613737,2023-12-22T03:33:53-07:00,The UI,"As someone who uses discord mobile for more than 12 hours a day I would like to make it abundantly clear that I would prefer 78 1/2 men break in my house and use my body as violently as possible then have to continue using discord with this UI it is genuinely worse than the old UI in every single measurable way nothing works as it’s supposed to it is easier to just disconnect and reconnect then to stop sharing screens. If you are sharing screens and at any point your phone rotates to the side you will see roughly 1/5th of discord until you rotate your phone to the side and THEN return it to a vertical rotation. On several occasions I have considered forcing everyone to reach me on other platforms such as Skype, Zoom, or GroupMe and I get closer and closer every waking moment of using this cursed UI my biggest gripe is that instead of working on the existing bugs with discord mobile they thought revamping the entire UI which added so many more bugs was the best possible route. I’ve used discord since 2015 and will continue to use it on desktop for the foreseeable future but I can not ever recommend the mobile app, at least not until either some of the existing bugs are fixed or until discord allows people to choose between using the old UI and the new one.",1,209.0,madswordgaming,1
us,United States,4425135840,2019-07-07T06:49:27-07:00,Please help,"Discord is a great alternative to other apps, I got it because I was in a group and that group required you having Discord, and at first it was really complicated but then I got a hang of things. The problem started randomly, what would happen is whenever I open Discord it goes completely black, like the first time this happened I literally thought my IPad died, but nope. I closed the application, and on the screen, it showed “discord” but the app screen was almost empty discord was going very faint, and I can’t do anything on discord, I deleted it and reinstalled it multiple times. Still, nothing changed, idk what to do now, because when my clan is hosting a training or a patrol to get promoted, we NEED to be in Voice Chat. This has been limiting my ability to be a active member in my clan, the only way I can use Voice Chat or chat or other servers is by using my phone. But using a iPad to play games, and a phone to communicate is really hard. Other than this I have had no problems whatsoever. This would have been a five star but this issue has made things VERY difficult. Please Help.",5,3.0.4,i <3 lizzards,4
us,United States,14464708832,2026-08-23T18:50:39-07:00,The fantasies and the depths,"My journey with discord is not one of joy and happiness, but rather of despair and sorrow. Quarantine was where it began, virus infecting the land. It was here that the main character of this series, Jai Shah, first discovered discord. Contrary to its name, this app brought him everything except for discord. His tumultuous life found stability and serenity at last, which simply increased his hunger for growth. All good things, however, must come to an end. Soon after, he realized this reliance on discord was a hindrance to himself. The connections he had made, once his pride and joy, was now nothing more than an obstacle, holding him back from attaining  what he really needed in life. It was in 2023, when he finally realized that this had to stop. Discord, an app for alleviating the discord in his life, was bringing him too much discord for him to function properly. It was only after he made the faithful decision to delete this cancer for good that he realized the stillness that comes with the outdoors. To this day, he doesn’t regret meeting discord, rather instead regretting the reliance he put on it.",5,341.0,Jai “Robert Dillingham” Shah,0
us,United States,1833556905,2017-10-07T12:01:11-07:00,"Please never change, I love you too much","What can I say about Discord? I started using it a year or so ago off of a friends recommendation, and I have no interest in going back to any of the multiple VOIP programs I’ve used in the past (Xfire, Skype, C3, Steam, Mumble, Teamspeak, Razer Comms); Discord beats out all of those for one major reason: Absolute control over everything. The ability to create and manage my own channel with access to just about every detail keeps me coming back, and makes things so much easier on me. Volume sliders on everybody giving me peace of mind on how loud (or quiet) people are being, being able to voice/text mute people that are being abusive in chat, and having multiple text/voice channels is just icing on the cake.

I told myself I wouldn’t write a review for Discord till they rolled out with the video call/screenshare update on PC, and they did so here I am. 

If you’re wanting a reliable, free, all-access VOIP program for your gaming or chatting needs, Discord is for you. With their optional Discord Nitro subscription offer I hope they never run out of money to support this gem.",5,1.9.2,Quizup Fanboy,28
us,United States,13731976948,2026-02-09T14:28:22-07:00,Stealing Identification Images to Train Facial Recognition AI Confirmed by Discord Themselves,"I am a long time user of discord and I use it as my primary social media platform for basic communication, my job, and my hobbies. I just deleted the app and will not be reinstalling in protest to their new AI facial and behavior recognition toolkit being advertised under the guise to ""protect teen's safety"" in which the toolkit will use metadata (who you message, when you message, geographical and platform location of message, and categorized contents of message) to determine whether their AI thinks you're an adult or not. If the AI mislabels you, you then have to undergo a facial scan and/or give them proof of identification AKA your government issued ID.

Discord was one of the last ""relatively safe"" social media platforms meaning that it did not passively harvest your data to enforce surveillance and supply sensitive intimate data to third party companies that will use that data for nefarious purposes. 

All of this information can be found publicly though what they don't make transparent is that Discord trained this AI toolkit by stealing user data of identification images that are provided by users in selective age restricted servers and a breach in data back in October 2025 confirms this. Discord then confirms this themselves after the data breach was made public.",1,314.2,lucifersramen,0
us,United States,12362193350,2025-02-27T11:56:34-07:00,As a server mod:,"Discord is good at what is meant for: a chat program. Join servers, discuss in channels, and send private messages, talk in voice chat. However, they keep adding features that aren't necessary in order to make themselves a one-stop-shop social media despite the siloed nature of servers, and they're too eager to jump on the techbro scam bandwagons like NFTs. Many new features are added without consideration for user impact, such as loud noises from soundboards or flashing lights and colors from animations that can harm some disabled users. Many times it's difficult or even impossible to minimize or turn off features, personally or in one's server. As of this review, they just added a mandatory 3rd party app that allows users to ""remix"" anyone's posted images via generative AI. There is NO way to shut this off on a personal account level, nor can moderators choose not to have it in their server. The ""Disable"" feature only ensures the ""remix"" is sent privately instead. These new features should NEVER be automatic, they must be Opt In only and with ways to disable and disallow them. Discord needs to consider the users before getting hooked in by their own shiny new toys they want to force on everyone, whether anyone wants them or not.",2,268.0,Ablyn79,0
us,United States,12079643650,2024-12-18T18:59:39-07:00,Poor customer support,"Hello, who’s ever reads this I don’t really leave reviews much but here we go; so discord has a terrible customer services like for example like if you where a person who gotten account banned, server issues or whatever the case it is. You get bot responses.. I mean I understand this app has a lot of users but when people makes a report like I’ve seen people say some responses are copy and paste and or takes so long to respond or even resolve issues. And the don’t get me started about discord customer support number.. like you a whole company and no one is even picking up the phone; so like why even have it if you cannot even talk to a rep? Even PlayStation & Xbox have reps and you see how many users in those platforms so you guys need to fix that. Lastly what discord needs to fix is when people are locked out of their accounts with 2 step verification there’s shouldn’t be a reason for people to have to make a new account if they don’t have backup codes, anything could happen technical difficulties or anything they need to have a way to help people to get their accounts back there’s a lot of users who been on discord for quite some time and now they lost everything because discord can’t do this or don’t have that.. you’ll need to do better.",1,259.1,#1 app Review board,0
us,United States,11295717811,2024-05-22T12:40:39-07:00,Updates are ruining it,"Although i’ve changed accounts once or twice, I have used discord since April 2020. Every new layout update absolutely ruins the app, and I’ve pondered moving platforms altogether due to them. This app used to house the best layout I’ve seen of any social media, but with the removal of so many old features, and implements of useless, tacky, and even inconvenient new ones, it’s lost its title as such. eg: the swipe right auto-reply feature replacing the search bar / user list was a bad move. It takes so much extra effort to see who’s offline in a server, and we could already quickly reply by holding down the message. The update was less than useless; it was a hinderance, and in my eyes one of the worst parts of these layout updates. I can’t read text channel descriptions anymore because of the removed search bar / user list. I know one bad review won’t change your mind, but under every twitter post in the last six months, your user base has been actively BEGGING for the old layout to return, or at least a toggle feature to have it for those who want it. Although not all of them are taking the time to write a review, you obviously have a TON of people upset with these layout updates.",2,230.0,（・□・；）??,0
us,United States,14000572979,2026-04-26T16:10:41-07:00,Banned my main account for NO reason.,"A couple weeks ago I was on call with my friend, we were talking on discord to are friends and then my friend told me she got kicked out of her account, so I logge out of mine and tried to log into hers. I checked what was wrong and she got banned till 2028 while she was barely on discord and was in NO discord servers and only had a couple friends added. After that I tried logging into my account and my passkey would not work so I started to panic, I also forgot my password so I tried resetting g y passwor and it said my account was disabled?? I got really confused because I know I did not do anything wrong or disabled my account, so I went to my email and I said I broke community guidelines while I know I never did and they would not give me the reason and how I broke them. So I tried my best and contacted support multiple times and they were not helping me at all, the bots kept telling me the same thing and that I would have to go in my account and get better access and contact support in my account while I clearly couldn't log back in. I still don't know what I did or if I said something wrong, I also had a couple days left with my nitro and lost the chance to use it and lost everything that took gears to get on my 2024 account.",1,325.0,urfav_luckk,0
us,United States,9641568397,2023-02-21T13:58:43-07:00,The new image cropping isn’t as pleasing as it would be.,"As someone who’s in servers where a lot of images get sent, mainly art or other little things, it’s quite infuriating having to deal with the cropping not showing the full images of the images being condensed. From what I know, we didn’t mind the long string of images taking up our screen, especially me, and I would’ve highly preferred if it was a toggle instead.

Yes, this app is quite great and lovely, but maybe put light consideration into making certain things toggles as not everyone may enjoy them. I’ve seen the drama over it, or just merely people ranting about it if that’s a better term, but yes personally I think things like that that would be quite major should be a toggle. It makes life easier on everyone, as it generally seems quite a lot of people had preferred the older image method.

Again, a lovely app, but some things like this just don’t seem too fun. It would be ten times better as a toggle to turn it back into the old way or keep it like that, and I hope you take this into at least slight consideration. Especially since it might be a bit worse on mobile for people.",3,166.0,ValentineGrimm,0
us,United States,8999599271,2022-08-20T15:40:46-07:00,An absolute disgrace of an update,"I’ve used Discord for a while now, and quite frequently. I’ve never had serious issues with it, until this recent update. This new update is the most atrocious thing I’ve laid my own two eyes upon. The new font is disgusting. It makes me want to punch a hole through my screen. It brings forward such an unbridled anger within me, I can’t stand it. Put it back. No one asked for it to change. Please, I swear to god, PLEASE change the font back. If it was for easier reading purposes, then make it a changeable setting, not an unchangeable default. The S makes me want to cry, the longer E makes me feel like I’m about to go insane. This update is honestly one of the worst things I’ve seen come from discord. Myself and many others are disgusted by this new update, so maybe, just maybe, please listen to the community and put it back. 

All that aside, Discord is a pretty decent messenger app. I talk to many of my friends, and have it downloaded on multiple devices. I enjoy how much more connected the company is to its users compared to other platforms. I love it, but this update makes me so angry and upset I think I’m going to throw up.",3,140.0,34566645,1
us,United States,7574265502,2021-07-13T22:26:36-07:00,It’s fine.,"This app is great if you want to message your friends, make calls and have a blast but their is still some issues I would like to be fixed. Discord lost a bit of popularity since the update. The issues I find most annoying is when you are trying to delete messages in a DM you have to go through each individual message and press delete. Instead of just deleting all messages at once, you have to scroll for hours deleting thousands of messages. Knowing you could just put a button to delete all, instead you made everyone suffer by deleting each message. I want to delete all my messages on a DM with a friend and it’s taking too long. Nobody wants to sit here for hours deleting messages when you could literally just click one button, taking less than 5 minutes. Think how easier and happier customers will be with 5 minutes, because nobody wants to delete messages for atleast an hour. Think this through, and please, fix this. I love discord, but at this state mind as well use messages.",5,82.0,Why I like episode,0
us,United States,10725750100,2023-12-20T23:04:15-07:00,i think i would give the new mobile ui a 0 stars rating if i could 👎,"every single person i’ve spoken to about this has told me how frustrating and difficult it is to use the mobile app since this update. you claim you want it appear “simpler” or more user friendly or whatever but the previous ui is what users have been familiar and comfortable with years, not to mention the fact that this was forced upon users without even giving a toggle-able option. I would recommend at least giving users that so they can at least have a choice. i could go into detail about certain features (or what is now a lack thereof in some cases) which are particularly giving users issues, but for the sake of my time, energy, and length of this review, i will  recommend reading other recent reviews left by other users for more information. A vast majority are facing the same issues and frustrations. 

the old mobile ui has been known to reflect the desktop version as like a ‘mini version of the same thing’, and i guess this time around getting rid of something so familiar and easy for everyone to use seemed like a better idea? there was nothing wrong with it. Its similarity and familiarity to the desktop version was the reason that i, along with many other users loved it in the first place. it made the transition from mobile -> pc : vice versa really nice because the appearance was so familiar to us. now our muscle memory is entirely useless, and it’s very frustrating for a mass majority of users. 

 for me, discord on mobile was easily a 5 star rating, but now giving it even 1 feels generous. all i can ask for is to please listen to the feedback other users are giving; access to the previous ui should be at least an option, if not completely brought back.",1,209.0,emily010604,2
us,United States,10696787483,2023-12-15T04:24:33-07:00,Doesn’t care about its userbase.,"I have used discord for many years and it has been my go-to messaging platform, however I’m entirely fed up with the changes they’ve made recently. Not just this last layout change, either - they’ve been consistently making godawful feature and usage tweaks for the past year or so, but at least before there was generally an option to disable or not engage with the changes. This update has been the last straw. They’re actively making the layout more confusing and inconvenient for their users, I honestly can’t wrap my head around what could have possibly prompted this since everything was fine how it was(edit: it was for money. I should have known). Not one person I’ve seen has liked the update and are infuriated at being unable to undo what Discord has done to itself. It’s as if they’re trying to kill their own platform. I’m tired of it and the thought of giving them another cent sickens me, I can only hope whoever’s in charge realises that not every update needs a huge change to keep people engaged before they runs the company into the ground. 

I hope the investors or shareholders this is supposed to appeal to see how much the userbase hates what they’re doing and Discord loses money trying to undo this idiocy.",1,208.1,SupremeDorkLord,3
us,United States,8378390154,2022-02-20T14:06:21-07:00,Unable to Send Messages Glitch,"I use Discord every single day on PC and have never encountered noticeable glitches, but the Discord app is getting on my last nerve. The app has had this glitch where the send button suddenly doesn’t work anymore. It’s not just the send button, but the emoji tab won’t work either. You can still type and even scroll left to right and see your DM info and server list, but all of the buttons freeze up and don’t work. I literally have to copy my message, fully close out of the app 2 or 3 times, deleting the half saved DM still remaining in the text bubble each time I reopen, and then finally, usually after the 3rd time, it will be functioning again and I’ll have to paste and send my message. I’m writing this after having gone through that process just for my phone to lose what I had copied, not giving me the option to paste, losing everything I had typed. This glitch has me asking my friends to download different apps because we’re all getting so frustrated with it while trying to communicate during work or school hours. Y’all have a LOT of money, I know you can do better and fix it.",3,114.0,as-your-body-remains,1
us,United States,3074564792,2018-08-16T16:18:50-07:00,Great but Keep Improving!,"Heya! I just wanna say I love using Discord especially on mobile devices when I don’t have a laptop, and it’s quite a fun app to chat with others.  However, there are some things that I want to have Discord improve on or at least try to help with the app to make it better, especially for mobile devices.  One thing in particular is to have more color choices for roles and to customize role colors on mobile devices.  Another thing is when I see some people’s status when it says something like “Playing Sleeping”, “Playing And 3...2...1..”, etc, I want that option to be available to mobile devices, or if that is already available, please respond to me with how I would do that.  One last thing is when I try to save a picture with a transparent background, when I go look at it in my photos, it doesn’t go from a white background to taping to a black background. I really would like these issues to be fixed in the next update or two.  Other than that, this app is very great and I love how it is improving but by bit! Keep up the great work!",5,2.3.6,DJ Dragon Girl 101,6
us,United States,5382810326,2020-01-09T16:51:39-07:00,Please read,"This app logged me out several times and it won’t let me log in no matter how many accounts I make. It logged me out, but I already saved my acc password and user, so I tried using that. It failed saying that the email was not registered so I thought “oh it’s no big deal I can just try registering again with the same email cause it says the email is apparently ‘not registered’ yet” so I did that and THEN sit said that the email was ‘already registered’. Okay WHAT?! So I tried creating an acc again, it failed. I tried signing back IN again, still a fail. And I know it’s not my technology glitching our non kyle and that it’s apps fault bc no matter how many devices I tried to switch to, it still wouldn’t work. I used to like this app a bit before this stuff started happened cause this app is really good for like if your friend dosent have a phone and can only text on pc or something like that and it’s also good for gaming and streaming I guess but if you keep getting logged out, there’s no point of giving the app a good review, especially if your like me and have been downloading and deleting the app several times with no success and have literally been trying this for over 4 DAYS STRAIGHT!!!! The developer(s) should really fix this problem before it gets a lot more bad reviews due to this glitch.",1,3.1.9,Umm.Hi,9
us,United States,11441937264,2024-06-30T14:17:30-07:00,Can't see incoming video.,"(Post dev response: I *have* restarted my phone/reinstalled the app. The point is, reinstalling it only works for the first couple calls before it stops working again. I've had this issue since, at latest, the UI change in winter. iPhone 12 Pro, iOS 16.? through 17.5.1, if that helps.) I have to reinstall the app every time my friend wants to share his webcam. Otherwise it just shows a crossed out camera icon under his pfp. Why does this keep breaking? Screen sharing is fine, it's just face cam calls I can't see without reinstalling the app every time. Doesn't matter which device he uses.

Original Review: Can finally view my servers and chat in one place, and select them without it shoving me in the top room again! Thank you for taking users' input into account. AND VoiceOver still works with chat (as long as u open the app with VO on, like most apps). That was my main complaint before the UI change. I still see no point in that sidescroll list of people I never talk to above the msg list besides taking up space tho. Some features like swiping are still the same, but I'm glad I can comfortably use servers again!",3,235.0,Laully_,0
us,United States,6108625895,2020-06-22T07:53:38-07:00,great app,discord is a great app to interact with your friends and I’d loved to give this app 4 stars but I’m giving it 4 due to the voice chat issue the voice chat needs works you have to leave call and come back because something happens and you can’t hear the others or they can’t you. So leaving and coming back is only A temporary fix to the problem but happens multiple times through the call it gets to be annoying. other issues is it at times call cuts out when ppl are talking and you can’t hear what they are saying and they have to repeat their self sometimes  to understand what they are saying. seem to have connection issues so if you improve the voice chat that would be awesome being you talk to ppl all over the world be nice to be able to have a conversation without it cutting out and being able to understand what everyone is saying but when it is actually working it’s so wonderful to get to have a nice Conversation with all your friends. this goes for voice chat and also discord private calling. so if you could please look into this and fix the problem that would wonderful! thank you 😊,4,26.0,staceyann39,0
us,United States,8596472315,2022-04-22T21:09:08-07:00,Very pleased.,"I downloaded discord a while back because it was necessary for some of the games I was playing. About 3 years later and it’s become my MOST used app on my phone & desktop. It’s been a place I can find a large array of communities, make my own community, and overall have a good time. I’ve found some of my best friends over discord. Especially within the gaming community Discord is the best option, IMO there are no other comparable options. And it’s free! 10/10 from me, it does what you want it to and more. If your debating weather or not you should download the app. Do it. It’s 100% worth it. I’ve never had any technical issues that weren’t client side issues (layman’s terms: due to my own internet/computer issues) either. Creating a server is super easy and straightforward as well, and it has multiple capabilities that aren’t found in other applications similar, while there is some VERY minor complaints, it’s nothing mentionable and is mainly related to some of the more advanced options in discord creation etc.",5,122.0,Brody Woods,0
us,United States,13773329331,2026-02-21T06:09:29-07:00,Just destroyed them selves with global id. Users mad and leaving.,"Well discord just killed their platform with the global id enforcement bs. I am seeking alternatives as many are. No one likes this dribble and parents need to parent their kids. We don’t need a global pd network policing people of all ages. Not only is this a blatant violation of our first amendment rights it isa violation of the first amendment rights and many privacy violation rights. Bye bye discord. Hello something else. I suggest team speak, stoat or matrix over this bs of global age verification.

