us,United States,11509055119,2024-07-18T18:21:45-07:00,Privacy nightmare,"Got off of Facebook and started to collaborate with freelancers on discord. When I went back to download my Facebook information, after deleting meta products from my phone, under the GDPR CCPA Shine The Light Law, it had a section called “off app activity” Literally tracked every single time I opened the app and sold that information to third party providers, from the time I installed Discord, each phone app pickup, all chats, Facebook had access to all of that data, them and their 1000 or more beloved third party marketing tracking affiliates . It’s more likely to ban you than ever respect your privacy or your data, and according to Tech Lore, the business model has always been to monetize your data interactions to the fullest monetary exploitation potential possible. If that feels good to you, to open up and share intellectual property or deeply personal story on a platform that doesn’t currently respect Do Not Track requests, then by all means, sign up.   Even with a discord nitro upgrade, you don’t get upgraded privacy rights or protection from the prying eyes of big pervasive advertising technologists looking to maximize your data profitability and give you nothing in return for it. Got it?!?! I’m out.",2,238.0,overlandtech.aero,1
us,United States,10771569900,2024-01-01T09:55:28-07:00,It’s ok but difficult,"Since the UI got updated, I have to go into my sound settings and manually turn on speaker every time I join a voice channel. Otherwise, I can’t hear anything. Before, there was a button on the bar at the bottom next to the mute mic button that let me do that but it’s gone. It’s also hard to get to the text part of the voice channels and exiting them is a tiny button in the bottom right. 
I miss being able to swipe left to see who’s online. I’m also having trouble with replying to comments, I will tap “reply” and if I swipe to my notes app and then return (usually I am fetching a link), it will keep whatever I typed but it’s no longer replying to the comment and oftentimes it’s taken me down to the most recent comment. In busy channels, it’s frustrating. 
If I’m trying to catch up, I will sometimes without even touching the screen be jumped back down to the most recent comment if someone else comments something new, which again is frustrating in busy channels and I have to scroll 100+ comments up manually. 
Please improve the UI, it’s not helpful for those of us who have certain disabilities.",3,209.0,KieranLeeTheScienceGeek,0
us,United States,10667964758,2023-12-07T12:30:42-07:00,The Useless Feature Update,"Discord *used to* be the best app for any type of messaging or social media, and my go to for any kind of communication. I preferred discord to any other social media, and would try to use discord even over basic texting. The continuity between all of my devices and the uniformity between desktop and mobile was something you couldn’t find anywhere else. 

However this last major update removed everything that made Discord special. They completely reworked the UI into what feels like a cheap knockoff of what everyone else already has. Every aspect of using the app, except for typing, is so completely different I have to basically relearn the entire app. It took me 15 minutes just to find the settings page in a desperate hope they added a setting to go back to the old Discord mobile layout (which they didn’t)

I don’t normally write reviews for things unless it’s really good or really bad. But with this update, I had to write a review in hope that the devs might see it and hopefully make some changes to bring back at least some semblance of the “classic feel” of Discord I once new and loved. I would really like to write more, but I can’t keep allowing myself to be this angry so instead I’ll just end it here.",1,207,YouFinally,2
us,United States,13668071400,2026-01-23T15:28:52-07:00,This company is incompetent,"I accidentally hit the button to delete my account. I tried to log back in same day, within the hour. It said my password was wrong. I reset my password then. I then tried to log in with my new password and it would not take me to my account. Instead, it takes me back to the main discord page of register or log in. I reached out to their support and they are clueless. They offer zero help. I have spent $100’s on my account and they do not care to help me get my account back even though it is within the 14 day timeline. I call their customer support and they are always closed. I leave a voicemail and no one calls me back. They are completely incompetent in helping me get my account back. I even did some age security thing they said to do and uploaded my ID to prove I wasn’t underage. I don’t know what else to do at this point but the fact they just stole all my money that is used buying things, my month after month of paying for nitro, friends names I don’t remember by heart, and all the convos with my loved ones - just gone and they don’t care. It shouldn’t be this hard. It says you have 14 days so why can I not log back in?? Why are they not helping customers that literally have paid 100’s on their app???",1,312.0,Lulubelle2328,1
us,United States,10897566670,2024-02-03T09:20:33-07:00,New UI has been problematic - Please add option to revert,"The new UI was likely made with the objective to streamline the user experience or modernize it in some way but it has done the exact opposite. I’ve used discord everyday for the last 6+ years. The update that forced users to swap to a new UI layout is easily, by FAR, the worst decision made by Discord. I gave it several weeks to see if I would adjust to it yet I am extremely disappointed and am forced to just use the PC version as the mobile UI is quite poor. Navigating to settings, searching for what a user on a server has said on a server, Horizontal Screen Issues (when i watch a stream and view participants, the app forces into horizontal mode and i cannot leave this despite leaving the stream), and several other issues plague the newest update. I strongly urge you to listen to these reviews and, at minimum, add a feature that allows users to revert to the old version (even with whatever bugs were present at the time). I think the discord community, particularly the mobile users, would greatly prefer having that option over whatever lesser evils are included in the old UI. If you do not believe me, just look at the state of the reviews by sorting them by “Recent”. Speaks for itself.",1,214.0,XyoPlays,5
us,United States,10665209291,2023-12-06T17:46:30-07:00,The new update is horrible and does the exact opposite of what it set out to do,"Just as the title states, the new update is absolutely horrible. They made it to be more simpler, but if anything, the old layout was simpler. All you had to do was swipe left and right, and everything was in front of you. The new layout is claustrophobic, and tucked behind so many uselessly added tabs. They even changed the shade for the dark mode for whatever reason, because yeah, that old shade they were using for YEARS, that is the CLASSIC color, is suddenly bad and they needed to delete it right away (it’s not even an option in themes!! WTH). I wouldn’t even be upset if this was an optional layout change, but it isn’t. They also said they didn’t want the app to be a scaled down version of the desktop app, but if anything it SHOULD be the same so there isn’t confusing when switching between apps, and people who are new to one or the other don’t have to relearn how to navigate again. Could’ve made a “legacy” option in appearances to let you revert back to the desktop layout, but no, discord can’t do that cause that would make their preexisting users actually like the app! Another case of discord not listening to the age old lesson of “if it ain’t broke, don’t fix it.",1,207,Garziez,2
us,United States,7735011152,2021-08-25T19:50:54-07:00,"Nice app, but nitro is driving me crazy","So i’ve been using discord so about 3 years now and it’s such an amazing app, I use it almost every single day, It’s a great way to talk to friends. But I recently got nitro to use stickers cause I think the stickers are cute, but it’s making me so frustrated, I want to have access to more stickers from a discord server but I only have access to like 15 of them, I thought it was normal at first but my friend has 10x more stickers than I do, I thought i needed to get rid of other stickers so I looked up how to get rid of the standard stickers and couldn’t find anything so i’m guessing i can’t get rid of those, But I do REALLY want more access to more stickers from discord servers, I also made my OWN server so I could use my own stickers and I can’t even use those! :( It’s kind of making me upset because I wasted my name getting Nitro just for me not to get what I wanted! If that gets fixed or if someone FINALLY tells me what is wrong with my stickers or how to get more of them, I’d definitely give this app a 5! I love this app so much and I have some of the most amazing friends on there, but this is my only complaint :)",3,88.2,Mirfanator,1
us,United States,4552452165,2019-08-01T14:46:30-07:00,New update on top of April fool's was a massive oof,"I've been using discord since early 2016 & absolutely loved it, but the decisions made during 2019 have left me very unimpressed with the staff's lack professionalism when handling serious issues. I was completely unable to use the app or the desktop version due to the April fool's ""joke"" they decided to pull that completely removed their entire platform's functionality from disabled users, including myself. I sent emails to support only to be greeted with replies of the support staff flat out lying to me about the ""prank"" being a permanent redesign for the platform after I told them that I could no longer use it due to a disability. Luckily it was reverted back, but rather than actually addressing the seriousness of the situation, the team behind Discord's social media played along with people complaining about bringing light mode back. The newest update the Apple version received is just not exactly very functional for most users, options that were once quick to access have been moved to a separate menu & you need to go through that menu to even change your profile's online status. It's just extremely unpractical for most users & the way it's designed & functions just doesn't make much sense.",2,3.0.9,lilpeoplez,6
us,United States,10677831534,2023-12-10T02:29:37-07:00,New UI Ruins Discord,"Mobile Discord has always been somewhat easy to navigate and similar to the desktop version. Now, it’s completely different and impossible to use at some points. If I want to get into a call and put it on speaker, I have to fumble around with the audio tab instead of being able to easily switch it from the pop up menu like before. Swiping/pressing to get out of DMs is so janky and it takes forever to register, even after doing it several times. The process of switching from DMs -> Servers is tedious and also takes a bit for it to register. The activity bar of friends who are online / have a status is weirdly set up and if you click on their profile, their entire profile shows up and floods the screen. The full friends list is also nearly impossible to navigate because it only shows profile pictures and not usernames. The new way to search through media is OK, but the pinned messages section is highly confusing because you can only see what the message was and not who it was from, as it shows the other person’s profile picture and not specific to who sent it. 

TLDR: The UI change is unnecessary, confusing, and barely functional. Please change it back it is so horrible.",1,207,shimemi,2
