us,United States,9028517733,2022-08-28T20:27:42-07:00,It’s good but I have been getting quite frustrated with it recently,"Since the newest update of the discord app I have been unable to change my custom status, I write one and push save and it will only stay for around three seconds and will then disappear. I assumed this was happening due to poor wifi but I have been in places with wonderful wifi and places with horrible wifi and it happens the same way in both locations. I enjoy writing statuses and changing them often so this has been frustrating me a lot. I plan on continuing to use the discord app because I enjoy taking to friends on it but this bug has been bothering me a lot when I wish to express my mood. The custom statuses were a favorite of mine in the app and and quite annoyed they are not working properly. I have also made sure it ain’t just disappearing on my screen and that it is also disappearing on others screen’s too and it appears that that is the case. I would appreciate if this issue could at least be looked into as I would like to be able to change and customize my status.",4,141.0,yyyftsubtxt,0
us,United States,7117378645,2021-03-18T10:24:20-07:00,Pretty much amazing. But...,"This app/service is incredible. It’s aloud me to communicate with people without pumping up the phone bill. It lets me communicate with groups of people and meet new people that I never would have. I love this app. The servers, the (majority of) people, the bots, all of it. Now here’s the but (This is just a single bug though so don’t be scared out of getting this app because of what your about to read, it’s truly worth the (free) buy.) Recently, I’ve been having a particularly annoying issue with discord on iPhone. I don’t know if it’s on any other devices or types of devices but it’s at the very least happening to me. When in calls, the screen on my phone will shut off for a time between 2 and 30 seconds. This happens at random intervals and seems to happen less (though still) the further I get into a call. Even when outside of the discord app with the call going in the background, the screen can still shut off. This is my *sole* issue with this app however. If you don’t have discord, get it. Can’t recommend it enough!",5,63.0,yodlerboi,1
us,United States,11691928820,2024-09-05T08:55:51-07:00,Amazing Application,"This approach towards consumer communication and customer engagement has led to many corporate leaders expressing interest and concerns over their own personal relationships and relationships overall… I give my deepest gratitude and respect to the company and their staff for their commitment towards their customer service and approach towards their current personal comms team… and I can’t assure this enough I willingly give this Advice to my colleagues downtown, DO NOT think this is a simple question of who’s applicable app is better but who is able to reach out to others the most effectively… and Discord hands down isn’t my main source for communication throughout my workplace but it is my personal opinion to say this is the best approach to a consumer interaction interface i’ve seen ever. Please everyone should listen and share your experiences with Discord’s App because it is definitely worth the download and in my own experiences the mindset this app brings has helped many members of mine connects together towards a betterment and goals.",5,245.0,FollowerofC,0
us,United States,10695242326,2023-12-14T17:09:30-07:00,The new mobile layout,"I loved discord, the old layout was perfect. This new layout makes it so hard to use discord for what I originally used it for. Something I loved about discord was that it was easy to multitask. I loved that i could switch easily between servers and dms and have multiple conversations at the same time which is something I frequently need to do. Another feature that I loved was the fact that it was easy to see who was online and who is in servers and group dms. Now I have to use a button (which is for some reason a magnifying glass which used to be for searching for things in the servers which makes no sense for seeing who is in a server)  and scroll through all the people because it doesn't put the people online on top. Also, when you get notifications in the app it doesn't tell you where it was from and it only says the user. I feel like this app lost everything that made it unique and turned into apps like iMessage and Snapchat. Sure there are good things in the new layout like being easier for new users, but I find it extremely hard to adjust to for old users. Please make it an option in appearance to have the old layout.",2,208.1,vinniegov,2
us,United States,10668062529,2023-12-07T13:12:56-07:00,Horrendous UI Update Adds Unnecessary Difficulty to Everyday Use,"The main issue I have with the recent changes, beyond how particularly unnecessary they are, is the decision to move the list of a server’s members, the pinned messages, and threads to a  more hidden menu accessed by clicking on the name of the text channel at the top of the screen.

Whenever I and many others who have the muscle memory try to access the list of members, it instead triggers an unneeded shortcut that brings up the keyboard interface to reply to whichever message you swiped on. To access the member list, Instead of this simple swipe, you have to press the name of the channel at the top of the screen, and scroll through a now noticeably less compact member list, since the buttons where the threads, pinned messages, etc. are now located seem to cut the list off allowing it less screen space. It’s all so wildly unintuitive when it was completely functional before.

Practically everyone hates this update, at the very least everyone who I have talked to. Please at least give us the option to opt out or reverse the changes. After years of good use, the various changes are bad enough to the point where I’m finally considering quitting and switching to another platform.",1,207,Hannah Alexis Nicole,2
us,United States,11719195367,2024-09-13T04:07:57-07:00,Change The UI Back For God’s Sake,"I don’t care if I’m late to the party, I put off updating my apps until today. The most recent layout is atrocious, it’s disorganized and cluttered and insanely user-UNFRIENDLY. I can’t use the search feature without manually scrolling through every possible reply until I reach the one I want (what happened to the pages?! I have years’ worth of conversations on here, I CANNOT be scrolling manually through my entire history of a word’s usage to find something from FOUR YEARS AGO), you added that thing that I HATE TikTok doing where a mere swipe on the screen doesn’t pull up the menu it’s supposed to go to, it makes you automatically set up to Reply to whatever message was in your way, and the server menus taking up the entire screen removed that sliver on the side where you can see a bit of the page you’re set at and determine if you’re in the right place. Among many other things, like the colors being unacceptably oversaturated and the message previews clogging up the DM menus and every possible feature taking two extra clicks to get to IF THEY EVEN REGISTER MY INPUTS. I am just so unbelievably frustrated with all of this, and I can’t even go to Discord to calm myself down because DISCORD IS THE PROBLEM NOW.",1,245.0,"Eff This, Anonymity",1
us,United States,6391454384,2020-09-03T09:54:43-07:00,"Nice app,  but confusing","I have relied on Discord for my game clan’s chat outside of the game. It’s been a nice, stable platform over the years, so I’m very happy with its stability.
