us,United States,3505261015,2018-12-07T14:37:32-07:00,Terrible,"Sometimes I love Discord. The audio quality is much better than normal phone calls and it’s a great way to text my friends aside from Snapchat and iMessage. But a lot of the time it either doesn’t work and I can’t hear who I’m on the phone with, or today for example it won’t connect at all. It’s actually making me very anxious because there may be something important on Discord. In my opinion this is a very poorly made app, I think that if you’re going to take the time and pay the money to create an app as popular as Discord then you should at least make it effective. I looked online and apparently sometimes Discord can be “down” (Which is bizarre. I’ve had it with Snapchat too.) which is very disappointing to me. In my opinion these apps should never go “down”. iMessage is never down, so why are these? It boggles my mind sometimes how poorly made this app is. And no I won’t delete it because I use it often. But I am very strongly requesting a major improvement, because this isn’t working. This is bad. Somebody really needs to get to fixing it. If your apps are “down” that is a major issue, because you’re the ones making the app not us and our use of the app is on our time and not yours. Thank you.",2,2.3.10,Listen it's,17
us,United States,13778001060,2026-02-22T11:41:02-07:00,Horrible support team,"I’ve been using discord for 8 years and have had the same account since I even started using discord. I’ve never been in trouble or even received a warning in all my years. But suddenly I got three violations back to back with no reason or explanation as to why. I appealed it and their team appealed one of them. The other two were left there. The third one didn’t even show up in my account standing it only showed two, but I received three violation emails. More proof that my account was wrongfully flagged and that their system is bugged. Anyways I’ve been contacting and begging for support but each time it’s just an automated bot. I’ve tried reaching out through twitter email, even calling. I have proof as to why I’m being wrongfully banned. It’s all just automated bots. Even when I appealed the violations one immediately got appealed and removed but then I was magically sent another one. All the while my account has been banned. And then I finally received another appeal review and they denied it. This company has no real support, there are thousands of people with this exact issue. Any support you ask for will be met with the exact same bot message and your ticket will be forcefully closed before you can even ask to speak to a real person. There aren’t real people: it’s all automated. On top of that discord leaked my ID and personal information. Horrible app. No support team whatsoever. They do NOT care. I literally had my account for years even having bought nitro for four years in a row. But the exact day my nitro ended, I canceled it because I wanted to save money. But the exact day, February 14th when my nitro would end. I magically get three violations out of nowhere for the worst policy you could break.",1,316.0,ThePotatoPringle,3
us,United States,10668828981,2023-12-07T18:55:28-07:00,The new interface is terrible,"The latest update completely redid the UI without any warning (the app store update notes literally just gave the same rote ""bug fixes and performance enhancements""
with no warning that the update would completely upend and ruin the app), and all of it feels like ""Change made for the sake of change and trying to become yet another duplicate of every other social media app"" instead of actually looking at how people who use Discord want to use Discord.
The layout now no longer matches the desktop app, which forces my brain to stop and consciously hunt for things every time I switch to my phone, instead of just effortlessly bouncing between them. The new dark mode colors are harsh and painful to read on (and just unpleasantly ugly). The new ""Messages"" page inexplicably adds a screen-space-blocking box of friends' activity (which nobody wants or asked for) that forces you to scroll further when trying to actually look through your messages (like,the actual reason for going into an area labeled ""Messages""), and with no way to turn off that unwanted Activity section. The press-and-hold menus for posts and servers now take up twice as much space and give half as many options. The extra separate button for servers instead of just swiping from the left means the bottom menu is claustrophobically crowded if you're still using a smaller phone. Images no longer show up in pinned messages, meaning you have to click through to the message (which defeats the entire point of pinning it!).
Basically, everything about this update screams ""We updated things for the sake of updating them, and don't actually care about our userbase"", and it's already making me avoid using the mobile app as much as possible when it used to be my main way of using discord.",1,207,swordofwit,0
us,United States,4438630838,2019-07-10T07:38:55-07:00,Amazing! (but some glitches),"I love Discord. It’s really addicting, especially with the bots. I can easily talk to my friends on it, voice chat, and even find new people that share the same interests as me. While some people complain at the fact that some bots cost money to gain full access to, I don’t mind. I mean, they have to find some way to fund it and make money, right? Discord didn’t even make the bots. Discord Nitro is the only way Discord has to support itself, so people should really be more grateful that they aren’t required to use it and that they don’t have to spend every minute closing an ad. Discord is one of the only add free apps that I can use, so I appreciate that also.

The only problem I have with the app is when I’m in it, it will sometimes exit me out randomly. While this isn’t a problem since I can just go back into it, it gets annoying at times. I would love if you could fix that. :)

Overall, this is a great app. I don’t see anything Discord could improve on besides the bugs, so I rate it a 5/5 easy to use app.",5,3.0.5,sawakokokoko,1
us,United States,12059526415,2024-12-13T11:11:12-07:00,"It’s a good app over others yes, but also no","Sometimes discord bugs out like crazy, more recently if I hit send twice(my fingers hit buttons sometimes from damage of different stuff) then the message sends many times and I can’t stop it, other things consist of having good wifi and data on all ends and everyone having a hard time hearing each other because it’s choppy, images sometimes sending in singles and not groups, and that I can’t see quests on all my devices. I’m sending this review through my iPhone as I found and charged it just to do the Minecraft quest because this is the only device I own that has Minecraft. I updated the apps (deleted and reinstalled discord and Minecraft even) and I can’t see the Minecraft quest on my iPhone but I can on my normal phone and laptop. This makes no sense and I expect that at least quests are usable (and visible on all devices) come next update if nothing Else is. Besides bugs it’s a 5 maybe 4 and a half.
-de_jay_132",5,258.0,"call me de s from yt .,.",0
us,United States,10924188283,2024-02-10T10:01:44-07:00,New UI Is Baffaling,"I’ve never once in my life left a review for any mobile App, but today I’ve just found out discord forced an update to the UI despite the fact I specifically chose to disable updates for discord just so I could remain on the old UI. The new UI is so much clunkier for me to use, and now whenever I switch between using Discord on PC and Mobile, I have to relearn where the same options and menus are.

This is one of if not the most user unfriendly user experiences I’ve ever faced. There’s no option to use the legacy UI or revert the update, I just have to learn a completely new layout now for an app I’ve already used for years and is STILL THE SAME on PC, and despite using discord every day I’m very nearly tempted to just stop using mobile all together until I can find a means of reverting to an older version. That or years of intuitive muscle memory has to be unlearned now just for the sake of making discord ‘look better’, I guess.

Never before have I been so worried about an update for an app that I specifically chose to not allow updates just to stop it, only for the update to force itself through eventually anyway. Will actively be searching for a way to revert the update in the days to come.",1,215.0,Jon22314,1
us,United States,10668482335,2023-12-07T16:22:41-07:00,New UI Update,"The new UI update is incredibly unintuitive and makes unnecessary and unwanted changes. Searching for specific posts within servers is now much more difficult without the ability to search the entire server; you now have to go to the specific channel to find results in that channel, which means that if you do not know which channel the message was in, you’ll have to go through each one to find it. There is no longer an auto-complete function for search filters. When searching for messages, there is no longer a ‘preview’ feature; it just sends you straight to the message. Personally, my biggest issue is that they removed swiping left to see the members list; it’s been replaced with a swipe-to-reply feature, which is not an improvement on the press/hold option from before and is a legitimate downgrade with the loss of the member list sidebar. You now have to tap the channel name at the top of the screen, which is much less accessible. There is no option to switch to the old layout, and Discord is flat out ignoring any negative feedback. I’d like to say I’m surprised that they could roll out so many changes and handle the backlash so poorly, but I really can’t.",1,207,8888u,1
us,United States,10123640815,2023-07-10T00:38:19-07:00,I can’t verify my account,Last night I was on my phone on discord looking at things until this verification thing came up so I put in my email and password but it says email already registered which I love discord but I don’t understand how it doesn’t understand that this is my email and I’m still thinking someone has my email and idk if it thinks I’m a robot because it says “there has been some weird things on this account” like I don’t don’t know what they meant by that and it’s making me annoyed but I still like discord but not the stupid verifications that are stupid and I didn’t even do anything wrong but it says I did something suspicious and I might be a “spam bot” WHEN I DID NOTHING so please my discord user is Deathkitty_XXX and idk the numbers but please I’m not a bot and I’ll never do anything to hurt anyone and you know when it has a back button and a support button I CANNOT PRESS THOSE EXCEPT THE EMAIL BUTTON OR LOG OUT BUTTON AND IDK WHO HAS MY EMAIL BUT IT SAYS ALREADY REGISTERED. Give me my account back and stop these stupid verification things and the website you know the “feedback” it doesn’t work when I went to it.,3,185.1,mousepillow,0
us,United States,9871218526,2023-04-28T12:22:25-07:00,Apple and or discord Please fix this.,"Hello, I’m a veteran of discord and my account was vally the vallest valentinea #9999 I have nitro on discord, But I deleted the app accidentally. I tried to download it back, But when i tried it said “Verification required”. When I entered my apple id, it took me to the card/billing information. It said everything was valid with my card. There was no done button for me to press for me to conform that it was fine. Only the “Back” and “Edit” button. When I press the edit button it shows me a delete button for my card. When I press the back button it just takes me back to where I started. I tried to look at reviews where apple replied, But I tried to use the answers provided yet it was not clearly worded and did not work. I don’t know if it’s because my cash app card is locked or not??? Because I definitely unlocked it and it still did not work. My nitro isn’t due for paying since I’ve just bought it just a couple of days or weeks ago. And it expires on may 21th. I also don’t know if it’s because of the nitro I bought and it’s trying to charge me because I deleted it??? I’m not sure. But I’d like this taken care of, Thanks???",2,175.0,Valentineasvalentine,0
us,United States,9854865472,2023-04-23T21:29:26-07:00,Some small issues,"I’ve had discord since 2020 and it’s an absolutely amazing app. It has helped me make a lot of friends. But i don’t like how limited of space there is on mobile devices. It feels like all of the text on my phone is smushed into just one small box. I also liked when the profiles weren’t so hard to deal with. They were very easy to change and very easy to edit. I enjoy being on this app but then again, I don’t like the way that some servers have been reported MORE than once by many people and haven’t been investigated. A server i joined almost 9 months ago had been reported to discord support and so have the owners of these servers. Unfortunately these problems were not addressed in the time they needed to be. I wish it was a little bit more of a safe environment and didn’t contain many “adult” servers or images. I remember when the app was recommended 13+ and now they’ve raised it as so many people have uploaded very inappropriate servers, links, and pictures. Overall it’s an amazing app and i love it. These things just need to be fixed for it to be a safer and more fun platform.",3,174.0,❤︎☾♥︎❥𓁹⌫☹︎☦︎︎,0
us,United States,4435692080,2019-07-09T15:34:52-07:00,Really like this app... but,"I’ve been using discord for several years, but every update seems to make the app worse. I see very few people in the reviews actually liking the IOS integrated calling. Please, for the sake of your dedicated user base, reverse it or make it optional. I cannot stand the fact that I cannot lock my phone during a call. Not to mention the constant cutting out during voice calls and connection issues. (Which have just gotten worse, may I add) It’s so bad that me and my boyfriend have considered switching apps. This is ridiculous. If I wanted to have a phone call where I couldn’t lock my phone and the screen goes black when my hand covers the top of my phone, I would have just used the regular iPhone calling system. Fix. This. Or risk losing business. This is turning into Skype and I left that platform for very similar reasons. Love this app but hate what you are doing to it. Really have hope that you will fix these issues and understand that people don’t like the integrated calling system.

UPDATE: Thank you, discord, for fixing your app. Appreciate it!",4,3.0.5,ID anonymous,1
us,United States,3186029683,2018-09-13T14:40:55-07:00,Latest Update,"This latest update has caused the app to awkwardly lag at points. Especially when it comes to trying to use discord emojis. I find myself accidentally sending my message before it even registers that I’ve clicked on what emoji I want. I’ve never had this happen before, and though it doesn’t seem like much of an issue, it also goes for typing as well. It’s like I completely miss letters, and it just doesn’t register that I’m tapping on them. This doesn’t happen anywhere else, and I haven’t had any problems with my phone otherwise.
Also I’d really prefer it if autocorrect went back to the way it was, where you could send things and not have it change after pressing send. The last word becomes drastically changed way too often, and it’s especially annoying when I’m trying to catch a pokemon and it no longer sends what I type and instead what autocorrect thinks I’m trying to say. Maybe this doesn’t pose as a huge deal to others, but I really do hope you’ll reconsider forcing autocorrect when pressing send. I’ve become so used to it not doing it that it now bugs the heckers out of me.
Other than that, I love discord 👍🏻",3,2.3.7,Eire Kirkland,0
us,United States,9393568842,2022-12-13T17:40:22-07:00,My opinion about this,"Me, personally, I love discord. It’s my peace place. I can talk to my friends, meet new people, and best of all, be caught up in all the new things that happen. I don’t really recommend for younger kids as there are some adult ‘predators’ out there. If you do happen to be younger and on discord, I really recommend lying about your identity as there might be some creepers (no not talking about those Minecraft creepers that blow up) that want to follow you (not in a good way). Other than that, you can find great servers with great community. If you play games, there might be server that you can join to check in on events. I don’t recommend doing stupid things though. That’s all really, bye bye. -314.        Edit: it is a good app just kids, don’t get in trouble with your parents(unless you have parents who don’t care). Maybe make a discord that is unblocked by the screen time thing that parents put on your phone, it might work. JUST PLEASE 
, DISCORD IDK IF YOU READ THE REVIEWS BUT PLEASE MAKE A DISCORD THAT EVADES THE SCREENTIME THING.",5,157.0,#CutiepieGaming!,0
us,United States,10902932381,2024-02-04T18:18:50-07:00,Super annoying can’t go to where you left off,"For a widely used platform, this app is severely lacking in simple features. The one that bugs me the most is that app automatically takes you to the newest post instead of starting where you last left off. And there’s nothing in the settings to disable that or there’s no feature to jump to where you last left off. I’ve done some online searches and all the results I’ve found complain about this specific issue going back at least 5 years and ridiculously it looks like the devs have done nothing about it. This is super frustrating if you’re trying to keep up with a very active conversation.

Update: the dev responded with asking if rebooting/using a different wifi would. Not that that has anything to do with the problem I described but regardless this problem persists no matter what network I’m on and whether or not I’ve rebooted the app so obviously it’s an app issue and not something on my end. Further the dev posted a link to a troubleshooting page on what to do if the app crashes on you. Again, NOT the problem I was complaining about. Absolutely ridiculous. If I could change my review to negative stars I would.",1,214.0,Theedie,1
us,United States,10669251465,2023-12-07T22:21:02-07:00,UI changes and the unfriendly behavior discord shows to its users,"Discord's recent UI changes have indeed triggered widespread discontent among users, especially with the overhaul of features like the search function and pins. Notably, users now face the inconvenience of missing image previews in search results and pins, having to click through to view them. The absence of a preview and the ""jump to message"" function adds to the frustration, abruptly sending users to the selected message without a preview option. The lack of saved positions within the pins/search section exacerbates the user experience, necessitating repeated scrolling. The new unified list without page separation and the absence of auto-completed search filters further complicate the once-intuitive search process. Users also lament the removal of the swipe-to-view members list feature, now replaced by the need to click on the channel name for access. These changes collectively contribute to a perception of Discord's UI becoming less user-friendly and more cumbersome in its recent updates. Moreover, Discord's decision to abandon elements that once made it unique—specifically, its simplicity and informal vibe—has further fueled user discontent. The platform's charm lay in its less corporate feel, providing a casual and user-friendly environment for communities to thrive. However, recent UI changes seem to be pushing Discord towards a more corporate aesthetic, diminishing the simplicity that endeared it to users. This shift in design philosophy raises concerns among the user base, as they perceive Discord moving away from its roots and losing the distinctive qualities that set it apart from more formal communication platforms.",1,207,aaa--7,0
us,United States,6233835418,2020-07-23T15:38:41-07:00,Discord in a Nutshell,"Discord is an awesome way to stay in touch with friends, as well as make new ones. It’s basically like iMessaging but it offers a calling system as well. I personally love this app and I’ve been using it for about a year now. You can do some exploring and find servers that you like and/or find new interests! As an example I took up knitting as an inspiration to make a gift for an online friend. 
Though Discord does have safety and privacy settings, it is wise to keep your personal information to yourself while talking with online friends. Discord will not leak your information to any of your friends or anyone at all, so it’s entirely up to you if you want to share anything (such as time zones). I don’t recommend sharing personal information, especially when you’ve just met them. Be careful when messaging unknown users.
Again, I love Discord and would definitely recommend it. If you aren’t at least 13, I don’t recommend reaching out to unknown users other than the accounts made by your friends.",5,31.0,Opalcloud,1
us,United States,1759237740,2017-08-29T06:34:34-07:00,"Excellent, always quick to fix bugs and keep its userbase up to date, only one problem","Works just as well as the PC version, easy to navigate and manage my servers

EDIT: I've changed my rating because I've been running into a problem again that I assumed was handled in the later updates from the early versions of discord. The app will attempt to upload images and then completely crash and close out, even with images that I've sent through it before. The only thing that will fix this issue is deleting and re-installing the app, which can be a timesuck, but this issue always comes back. I've deleted the app 3 separate times prior to this trying to fix the issue and it's a temporary fix. I use an iPhone 6, so it's possible it's some user-end issues, but please look into this and see if there's something you can do or if I can see what's messing with it on my end. The app is otherwise excellent, this is the main bug I've been having.",5,1.9.0,K. R. N.,6
us,United States,4136486259,2019-05-11T19:00:42-07:00,Discord... what are you doing...,"Okay. Let me just state that I love discord upfront. I’ve used the app daily for over 2 years now and overall it’s so much better than things like Skype and I’ve met many new friends. However, the most recent update released today (May 11,2019) there are some things I just really dislike a lot. 
First off, they moved the search button feature and I used that a lot so now I accidentally start calls and would really prefer (at the very least) the option to move it back. 
Second, calls now come up as an actual phone call and show in recent phone logs. It also opens a new tab that is uncloseable and seems to be always on “connecting...” even though I can hear my friend and my friend can hear me clearly. I can’t close this secondary “phone” tab without ending the call and it’s really frustrating and I’m really hoping you guys will revert the call settings to how it used to be. 
On another note, just a mild annoyance, when calls now start, it automatically plays audio on speaker and I wish there was a way to switch it to the private call setting. 
Hope these issues get fixed, otherwise I’ll have to take a break from using such a great app.",2,3.0.1,Emerald escape,8
us,United States,2456025475,2018-04-22T18:03:46-07:00,Amazing app!,"Discord is an amazing app, and I love it. But the mobile version is missing quite a few important features. For example, Discord on mobile (possibly IOS only) doesn't have Audit Logs for server moderation. Audit Logs are very important for server moderation, so that is one flaw with the mobile app. Also, only a minor setback this is, is the fact that there is no emote button on the mobile app. Yes, you can easily tap the emoji button on your keyboard, but if you are in a server with global emotes, you have to type out the names of the emote. But, there is emote prediction, making this a minor set back. Finally, I want to mention this weird bug that happens sometimes; It is a bug when you can't join Voice Channels or Voice Calls; it just disconnects you automatically, and it does this for a loop. When you close the app and retry, the same results will happen. You usually have to wait hours before you can join a Voice Channel or Voice Call again. Thank you for making such a wonderful app! These setbacks can be overlooked, so Discord is STILL my main way of contacting friends.",4,2.3.0,IamCuul,2
us,United States,10668471062,2023-12-07T16:17:32-07:00,Newest update is atrocious,"I’ve used discord since 2018, and it’s my main platform for communicating with people. Usually, I adore it, and the desktop app is still perfectly fine. The newest mobile update though? Garbage. It completely breaks the understanding of the basic UI that discord has had for years. It’s unintuitive and clunky, swipe to reply is annoying, and not being able to easily and quickly toggle to the members list to see who is online in servers is just bad. It also just feels like bad brand marketing because the mobile app has overnight changed to feel like an entirely different platform than the desktop app. In all honesty, if I didn’t need it to communicate with people, this update would be enough to make me completely leave the app. I wish they allowed users to toggle to the old UI if they wanted. I have yet to talk to a single user that likes anything about the new UI, instead, we’re all just frustrated, upset, and can’t promptly communicate in the way we are accustomed because of the magnitude of the UI change. We don’t know how to navigate an app we’ve been dedicated to and told our friends to use for literal years. That’s just bad, no matter how you look at it.",1,207,Shaykippers,1
us,United States,10644040227,2023-11-30T19:39:56-07:00,Will not load at all,"Downloaded this app after a long time and at first it had just taken a few minutes to load. Now it literally won’t load at all on my phone. This would be fine as it does load on my iPad except for the fact I have to use an authentication app as I have two step login. Only thing is, my account isn’t linked to my authy and I can’t link it unless I’m in my account already which I can’t get into since it won’t load on my phone at all. I’ve tried loading it on LTE, nothing. WiFi, nothing. I have redownloaded and tried to open it through every method I know such as through the App Store, right on my Home Screen, web linked to the app. At first these methods worked with still some loading time. But now it just won’t load at all. I’ve seen multiple people complain of this and honestly it should not be a hard fix. It is obviously not just my internet or phone as countless others have said the same thing about their mobile discord. Please fix this issue as soon as possible!!",4,206.0,rived-river-liver-sliver,0
us,United States,8191846657,2022-01-01T04:36:16-07:00,Please add option to disable custom notifications,"Yet another update that doesn’t allow us to turn off the awful custom discord notifications and force the use of the superior-in-every-way built in system notifications. Why force us to wait a minute or more before these kick in? That’s basically asking “how many minutes worth of notifications would you like to miss” during the most important time to not miss notifications—when the user is switching between apps frequently. The built in notifications are ugly, provide no additional functionality, and disappear into the either if you are in the middle of typing something and can’t click the notification the instant it comes in. I’m sure you guys had good intentions with these notifications (like, the web app), but in iOS, iPadOS and macOS, there are built in notifications that work much better.

In the very least add a “instant” option for the switchover. So the moment I leave discord I get system notifications and don’t miss anything. And if you really can’t let go of the discord notifications, let us enable system notifications along side the discord ones. Getting two notifications overlapping is better than missing them.",1,106.0,Pyk,0
us,United States,6392645375,2020-09-03T18:23:27-07:00,Beautiful app and helps you find love,Hi my name is Malay and I love this app let me tell you about it and how I got this app and found out about it so one day i  was playing candy crush and alway an app popping up so I saw this and how many pleople found love and made freinds so I downloaded this app and boy was it a dream come ture I created my account for this app and I started going into some chats and when I found the love of my dream his name is chad he was 19. Like me and looking for love I’d just thought he was the love of my life we talked for about. 3 hours and we had the same thing in common I started to ask are you single but he asked me first...and I said AM I heck to the yes yes yes so affter he said let’s meet up in real life or discord I wanted to do in real life but I don’t wanna let him Konw where I live and btw this is a stanger I never met before and I Konw we talked for hours but I don’t konw it he’s a phoyc so I said discord oh boy we had a ball he was the pertty  he said he had to go eat dinner affter he left 10 mits later affter 6:00 he was online then we started to talk again I love this app affter a few years we started to talk more often and met up and had kids Don’t be scared to find love it’s your choice I love this app this is my rating bye,1,37.0,da hi hi,35
us,United States,4141398791,2019-05-12T16:41:12-07:00,New Update is bad,"Discord used to be really nice and besides the occasional server problem, I rarely had any issues at all. I have a wireless headset and discord will automatically detect and use it as the audio device. When the new update came out, discord decided that it would use my iPads speaker, rather than my bluetooth hands free headset. It is easy to fix, but every time I restart discord I have to change it again. Also, the new update has the same UI as the FaceTime app from the lock screen. It also brings up the UI when you tap the green button in the corner, but it isn’t really an issue. The reason why it’s an issue from the lock screen is because anyone who picks up the device can see who you are calling (also I need to close the UI to unlock the device, which is annoying). Also, there is no start voice call option besides the designated call button in the corner. Doesn’t seem like a big deal, I thought the same thing, but when someone picks up I need to leave the call and rejoin. Again, super annoying. And there is no way to disable the FaceTime UI either, and tbh, I wouldn’t really mind the update if it was an option (there might be a way, but I don’t see anything in the settings that is related to the UI). That many issues and I’m not even done yet :). For some reason when I am in a call or have joined one since I loaded the app, the dms don’t work at all. No typing, scrolling, or starting calls, and if you want to do any of those things you will need to restart the app again! Well at least for me it doesn’t crash, but I might actually prefer it if it did crash. Then at least I wouldn’t need to restart the app every 5 minutes. This is just on my iPad though, haven’t tried it on my phone yet. Oh discord, I thought you were a professional company, but with this many bugs I am starting to doubt that. Please fix this discord.",3,3.0.1,Oflick,0
us,United States,11298795242,2024-05-23T09:48:34-07:00,The new UI isn’t great,"It is more like the UI for pc, which works for pc because there is a mouse and a whole screen. It doesn’t work for phone/mobile because it is far too much information and hard to reach. The old UI was cool because I could keep my thumb near where the keyboard was and still get to everywhere I needed to be. 
This one is extremely inconvenient as there is no longer a separate space for dm vs servers and switching is in the top left hand corner. Most people use their right thumb for the majority of typing. Even if they use their left thumb, they aren’t typing at the top of the screen. 
This greatly takes away efficiency and enjoyment along with adds an unnecessary level of complication. 
Also, although phone screens are bigger than ever, the amount of information on the “home” navigation screen causes everything to be smaller and thus harder to navigate and understand. 
I do love discord and I love having discord on my phone, but I enjoy the mobile version of discord on my phone. Not the PC. My phone is not my PC. Overall, this new UI for mobile is a nuisance.",3,230.0,PeregrineDee,0
us,United States,10670164297,2023-12-08T04:48:25-07:00,the latest mobile update,"The latest update to Discord's mobile app was unwanted, unwarranted, and has ruined the experience of using the mobile app. It used to be fast, clean, intuitive and easy. Now your muscle memory will cause you to accidentally reply to messages on your current server by accident over and over again. DMs and Servers being nearby made checking activity quick and easy. Talking to friends outside of servers was convenient, you could swap right back into whatever server you wanted. The newest update has actively made the app worse to use and I cannot stress enough that no user wanted this. Discord's individuality was destroyed with the last update. I am genuinely sick and tired of every other social media layout being the exact same. There's nothing unique about Discord's mobile app now. If I wanted facebook messenger I'd be using facebook messenger. Not to mention that the change to dark mode was hostile to users with vision disabilities. I don't know who asked for this, other than out of touch higher ups who should never be trusted. Users hate his update, I'm one of them. Return the old layout, this was so not it.",2,207,kingrynn,2
us,United States,10667701135,2023-12-07T10:44:38-07:00,New UI Needs Option to Revert,"The new mobile UI pushed by Discord gets rid of the current color scheme and instead forces a palette that is difficult to read and has been giving users headaches. The new UI is suddenly forcing all their users to unlearn their muscle memory for numerous functions, such as checking DMs, looking at the member list in a server, or conducting a server-wide search. The location of the previous server-wide option is now a channel-specific search, with the server-wide option in a new location, but the app makes no attempt to let you know this and just expects you to figure it out on your own or give up. People are also reporting embeds in pins no longer show up when looking at a list of pins in a channel, meaning pins for some people will be useless.

This update is catered towards a specific type of Discord experience, but also manages to screw those people over as well in an attempt to look fancy without actually improving itself. Discord needs to include an option to use the old UI or listen to its users who made it clear in beta that they saw no benefit in this massive design shift. Their behavior clearly shows that they don’t care about their userbase.",1,207,Superdog4103699,3
us,United States,6454632752,2020-09-21T18:48:16-07:00,I remember the good old days,"I remember the first time I joined discord 5 years ago right when it was starting up. I remember talking to my friends and making new ones on voice calls. I remember being able to just enjoy who I was and play around in servers. I remember when it was a small community, before discord nitro was even a thing. I remember the good old days and have fond memories of those good times I spent with friends.
I’ve seen many friends come and go, and I’ve stayed with discord as a reliable way to make new connections and connect with my friends. I miss the long nights I would spend on discord, browsing through servers and hopping into VCs. I miss the times when I said goodbye to a lot of my close friends for good.
I will always love discord. It’s been a huge thing for me to be able to connect with people and learn new things. I learned about my own life and what I want to be when I become older. I learned that it’s ok to love yourself and who you are.
I love Discord. From the bottom of my heart. Thank you for your wonderful service.",4,39.0,Skidattle,3
us,United States,4312006780,2019-06-13T19:22:07-07:00,Annoying bugs,"Discord is generally a good app that I use frequently to chat with friends. However, recently with the new updates, I’ve noticed quality in calls drop. Granted, the calls were never super great for me, but unlike before, it would consistently mute my friends so that I would have to leave and rejoin, then it’d work. Not only that, but my friends would often cut out several times during call. It could be a network issue and I’m sure this isn’t 100% discord’s fault, however it’s been frequent and annoying at times. Another issue I’ve been experiencing is really annoying. For some reason, discord has completely stopped working at random intervals. What I mean is that even though I get notifications, when I try to launch the app, the loading glitches and I’m forced out. The only way to fix this to my knowledge is deleting the app and downloading it again. It is happening more and more frequently and is an issue I’ve experienced ever since the latest update
Other than that, discord is great. It’s an easy app to use to chat with friends and I would give it a higher rating if not for the issues I stated.",3,3.0.2,yoitsbuffy,0
us,United States,11210371456,2024-04-28T10:07:41-07:00,recent unnecessary ui changes,"giving this three stars because there are some great communities on here and it’s very easy to organize your own communities. also, the desktop app is still good. 

my problem is with the mobile app specifically. removing the friends list from the navigation menu at the bottom of the screen was unnecessary and frankly an awful choice. now, to see if a certain person is online, you have to scroll through your DMs list or swipe through the status thing at the top. if it’s a person you haven’t DMed in awhile (which could be for a multitude of reasons), it makes it far more difficult to tell if they are online or not. sure, you could use the search bar, but it still requires far more gestures than it once did to complete what should be a simple task. 

there is and was absolutely no reason to remove this and i am baffled they did so. using the app is far more awkward now. after what discord has been doing to the platform over the past few years, i find myself wishing more and more there was an alternative.",3,226.1,renjamiin,1
us,United States,14346776176,2026-07-25T08:03:07-07:00,Use this NOW.,"It is actually insane that literally everything is in one chat app! I love how you can see what people play and what they want to play. Nitro is just a whole another level in discord. It’s really cheap for just 1 year and it makes it so you unlock 100% of the customizations. It also gives you a separate early access section. You even get 30% discounts on items that are listed as decorations, profile effects, and nameplates. You can create whole fandoms and a community in discord. It has heavy moderating features. And you can adjust everything you want in servers. With boosts that come with Nitro Super it’s makes your server even cooler like your profile. Even if you don’t have nitro you can still do Quests that’s about playing games for 15 minutes or watching videos. Discord generally makes quests for free games so it’s easy! I recommend downloading this app now if you want to have a great time linking games and friends with chats and communities.",5,338.0,nuh_uh12345,0
us,United States,8417672386,2022-03-03T18:03:25-07:00,Got banned twice,"So I’ve had it for around 6 months or so, and there was no problems, it was great! But around at mid-Jan I got banned, and I wasn’t really sure why either. So you know I asked about them on gmail but they just said they will look into it. A month or so later I find my account deleted. And even though I only had discord for 8 months, I had over 50 friends, I spent a lot of time messaging them, and now I can’t. I have no other way of contacting them. So you know I tried to get over it and made a new account. And I made a few friends, but of course I got banned. It said I got banned because I was being “abusive”, I gotta admit, my humor isn’t the best it has a few suicidal jokes here and there, BUT THEY ARE NOT TOWARDS ANYONE AND MAINLY ABOUT ME. I didn’t think I would get banned again, and the only place I did those jokes were through DMS. And if you aren’t Daimler with that word it means direct messages. Meaning they looked through my direct messages, which I’m pretty sure is illegal. And I am a minor so I don’t work and cannot afford to sue discord. Now I have made a new account, I will update on the account in a month. Hopefully I don’t get banned, again.",2,116.0,SiimplyMoonlight,1
us,United States,7219376214,2021-04-13T17:29:50-07:00,"April 13, 2021. (NSFW Discord Ban)","Today has been the worse day to be fairC hearing that NSFW channels will be removed and will not given access to those who are in IOS devices, I’ve read the article already about how IOS does not support any inappropriate or pornographic material/apps on the store, but we still have hook up apps where you can literally check out for a one night stand, or even other apps which “keep the privacy of one secure and deletes any archives for their safety” like Telegram that is fulfilled with illegal stuff. 
