us,United States,12323631602,2025-02-17T15:33:58-07:00,Careless production team constantly breaks app,"I'm so tired of Discord's production team constantly pushing updates that at best make the app frustrating to use (random features no one asked for that change how to navigate or prevent me from finding things, incredibly ugly UI changes no one asked for including making everything super small visually) or breaks the app entirely at worst. Today's the final straw for me - if it weren't for other people I talk to being on Discord I'd have left already. I opened Discord to find that none of my categories for servers could open or close, so I sighed and went to update the app, figuring they just pushed something that wasn't backwards compatible again. Nope! None of my servers would appear after the update! And when I tried relogging, I couldn't even get in because 2FA appears to be either broken or down. 

Can whoever manages the dev team get it into their heads that the reason Discord got popular was STABILITY and all these brand new changes are a problem not features? I'm sick of being leashed to an app managed by people who clearly do not care about user experience or what users actually want.",1,266.0,Darkmekmon,2
us,United States,12244735556,2025-01-29T04:39:51-07:00,Long Overdue Bug Fixes,"This app is great on many levels but there are also many bugs that have been an issue for a long time that have yet to be fixed. To name a few, app randomly crashes at times, unable to embed videos from places like Instagram, gif search is all sorts of messed up. I can’t tell you how many times I’ll be actively typing in search for a gif and the search box will just close and my keyboard will just close and it’ll force me to accidentally press on a random perhaps risky gif that immediately sends in the chat. I’ve learned to know when this will happen so I’ll type cautiously and sure enough *poof* it disappears but once this starts happening if I try opening the search again and typing I’ll only be able to do 1 letter and then it *poofs* again. So I have to type like this: F *poof* *reopen* I *poof* *reopen* X *poof* *reopen* T *poof* *reopen* H *poof* *reopen* E *poof* *reopen* G *poof* *reopen* D *poof* *reopen* A *poof* *reopen* P *poof* *reopen* P *poof* *reopen*. You see how ridiculous and annoying that is? Until then 3/5.",3,264.0,Waffle Ranger,1
us,United States,10665522841,2023-12-06T20:08:43-07:00,Great idea taken over by corporate greed.,"As of the last year or so discord has completely ruined their app with terrible updates. From useless features to the ugliest UI possible, it’s insane how bad they’ve been making it. Discord started great, as a simple instant messenger, and instead turned into a competitor for social media, without the social media aspect. The new profile features, ids instead of numbers, basic colors locked under paid subscription, 5mb upload limit, have ruined what this app was designed for. I first used discord back in 2018, all I used it for was talking with friends. That’s still what it’s used for, and what the majority of people use it for, however they’ve decided to make it “community oriented,” designed for gigantic servers. We’ve seen how this plays out with past community servers becoming Petri dishes for crime and cp. Unfortunately the devs aren’t willing to come to terms that they’re not going to make billions off of their app alone, even though they earn $450 million a year, and $1,000,000 in funding. They add the most useless, unnecessary updates and lock them behind Nitro, begging for your money. Useless at this point.",1,207,GamingReviews!,0
us,United States,8886667769,2022-07-18T07:09:09-07:00,amazing app but one problem,"first i would like to say i absolutely LOVE this app and its features, very unique. theres just something i want to clarify/find wrong.
 i want to talk about the random verification pop up. i get it, you need to make sure things about privacy is ok, but its REALLY complicated to use. when it popped up for me, i couldnt exit out of it. my only option was to log out or change email, so i changed the email. nothing happened. then i kept resending the email but there was no notification on anything for me. then without thinking, i decided to log out and maybe try making a backup account. i made a backup account then soon later i realized i didnt know my main accounts password (doesnt really have anything to do with this) when i logged into the backup account, the verification popped up again, now im stuck on the verification screen, on a backup account. PLEASE take the verification away, ever since i havent been able to use discord☹️",4,135.0,jiyeongy240,0
us,United States,8804684786,2022-06-23T21:56:32-07:00,Great but missing key feature,"The app is fully functional as far as discord's functionality is concerned, presuming all of your device's internal hardware is working. BUT. The iPad version has no means of switching input or output sources, as the desktop versions do. So if there is something wrong with your microphone and/or speakers all of a sudden, good luck on trying to use any audio interface-esque connected external peripherals as you might do on desktop. And yes, I acknowledge that I'm rage-reviewing because this happened to me, but I'm still giving the app four stars. Discord on iPad is great by and large, but it's missing a pretty ubiquitous feature in every other app I've experienced.

As far as troubleshooting replies I might receive are concerned: yes, iPad is on latest OS (15.5 at time of writing), discord mic access is enabled in settings, the exact setup works with every other microphone related app, I tried toggling the suppression options, etc etc. Just discord's lack of connectivity, it seems.",4,132.0,Seven Thousand,0
us,United States,8370220567,2022-02-18T11:18:54-07:00,The worst app on iPad,"With the constant upselling of Nitro and a dedicated Nitro gifting button, you think that they would have enough budget to buy an iPad Pro and actually test their app with a hardware keyboard and split/slide over views. The state of this app on iPad Pro 11” is nothing short of an embarrassment for Discord. The UI constantly breaks and slides messages or the text input off screen, you have to scroll up and long press on the closest message in a channel to for the app to redraw correctly in slide over. The image/emoji/gif picker is all over the place on whether it draws above the keyboard or stays within the app dimensions, depending on what you tap/click. The spelling suggestions window when using a hardware keyboard, regularly covers up the text input area in slide over/split, and the software keyboard does the same. Worst of all, the return key on a physical keyboard will start a new line instead of sending a message, with no apparent way to change it. The return key issue is new for me, but the other issues have existed for the past few years without any apparent fix. I’m considering cancelling my Nitro subscription because the experience is so bad.",1,114.0,Dean S...,3
us,United States,7625844699,2021-07-27T19:27:03-07:00,Needs Work,"Before the new update Discord was fun and easy to to use. Now however with the new update the relaxing, welcoming tone of the app and artwork changed into something more like Google and the other generic companies out there. Basically oversimplified compared to Discord’s unique style. I don’t mind the logo (besides the blue palate) but that and the call quality still needs work since it can be very glitchy/not work at times which I know does depend on the persons connection but still would be helpful. Lastly this could just be me but I tried changing my profile picture and for some reason no matter what I do it’s so pixelated?? That one is minor but other than that I like the app but I don’t love it like it’s good for calls, friends, gaming, and art but sometimes can be a bit frustrating to use. Just please don’t drastically change the app because that would just take away what it was made for and lose people who’ve been on Discord for years. It would lose the nostalgia and comfort that it gives to others.",3,84.0,DiamondET,0
us,United States,4696109264,2019-08-30T06:46:50-07:00,Call Update is Inconvenient,"I have Nitro supported Discord since the beginning. I love everything about it. Usually the updates are great and if they have problems they get resolved quickly. I was hoping this call display update would be improved somehow. The call acts like a real call on iOS and it’s really annoying. The status bar at the top of the home screen, the full screen display when the phone is locked, etc. When my phone is locked, I have to press the home button 3 times rather than once with finger print. First time wakes up the phone, second clears the call screen to my lock screen, third to get to the home screen. Second of all, every. single. call. shows up on the recent calls list. If you disconnect the call and start it again it shows up as a new call in the list. My recent calls is more discord than actual calls. 

This feature would cause me to uninstall any other app. An app needs to stay inside the app, not take over the rest of my phone. If other people like this feature, maybe make it an optional setting.",3,3.1.1,KimberlyBlue,0
us,United States,4374735824,2019-06-26T19:02:46-07:00,Very buggy now uncomfortable to use,"Now I’m gonna give this 4 stars because I used discord for quite awhile and I love this app but the recently the API has been very glitchy and the new update didn’t help for me. My biggest complaint is that the phone calls now save to an actual phone log when you call someone....really? You had to add that. Just why? Now I’m uncomfortable using the app because I don’t know if the app is going to get inside my phone and monitor my information and monitor all of my contacts outside of discord so I had to uninstall and write this review :/
I also don’t feel comfortable if it gets saved to a phone log that the phone company can now see  who I’m calling on discord.(cause monitoring everyone these days is out of control). So I don’t feel comfortable using the call feature on discord because now my phone company has to see me calling a friend on discord. Everyone has a right to privacy and this app just doesn’t seem private at all anymore and just gives info out like candy",4,3.0.4,ripnail,2
us,United States,7701031100,2021-08-16T16:29:12-07:00,It’s great but a few glitches,"Ok so dont get me wrong, I love discord I’ve been on this app for a while. The thing is, yesterday my group chat with my friends was gone, like it just disappeared. No one had even been awake and the owner of the group didnt delete the group chat because she knows that there are a lot of memories in the group chat. We had to create a new group chat and it was a little upsetting to us. Anyways, the next day we we’re talking in the new group chat while the owner of the group chat was offline. And she randomly started removing one of our friends, but the thing is, she wasn’t even on any device and she was sitting on the couch because she had a headache. I believe she is hacked or this is a huge glitch. I love discord though, I’ve made so many friends on this app. For those just scrolling through reviews, download it. This issue is probably just a mini bug and will be fixed in no time! :)vv",5,87.0,NotEmerald,0
us,United States,10295612693,2023-08-24T15:33:46-07:00,Horrible app.,"Someone threatened to doxx me and all she said is this. Not even helping at all. 1. Select the Message you wish to report. On mobile, hold down on the Message, and on desktop, ""right-click."" Please note that if you have already submitted a report, our team is currently experiencing increased volumes, and response ! help us focus on the most pressing requests, please only report behavior that presents significant risk, and that requires Disco resolve, We encourage users to explore the following tools that enable users to moderate their experience on Discord: - How to Diock Server spfety. settings Please note that if you have already submitted a report, our team is currently experiencing increased volumes, and response help us focus on the most pressing requests, please only report behavior that presents significant risk, and that requires Disc resolve. We encourage users to explore the following tools that enable users to moderate their experience on Discord: - How to block -Server safety settings - Contact server owners to moderate actions where possible KEEP in mind I was on a incognito window so they didn’t have my ip or info but that’s crazy that they don’t even do anything about it.",1,192.0,nbds_,0
us,United States,2950877088,2018-07-22T15:05:42-07:00,Great app but needs more greatness!!,"Hi! I know you won’t have much time to read this but I will really appreciate it if you do. First of all, this is a great app! There are so many things that I like. For example, you can make your own name and it will always be free to use! This is also a way to talk to all of your friends, make new friends and talk about your favorite things (gaming)! But to make this an even better app, I would personally recommend a few new features that I think everyone will enjoy! I think that there should be a feature that says when the person that you were talking to was last online. This can be used as a safety feature as well as a feature to see what’s going on because it can say if someone went missing when they were last seen or talked to. I would also recommend that you can tell when someone has read the message. And it’s for the same reasons as the other new feature. This is what I hope you can add to discord to make it a better app!",4,2.3.5,Bunnys boom,1
us,United States,3055474302,2018-08-12T12:54:54-07:00,Update over past review,"Since Discord Mobile has been updated several times, I’ve decided to return to this review and check out what has improved the most.
In my last review, I complained about the rediculously slow loading times. That has seemed to have been almost completely eliminated, which is probably the most positive change. And that’s really about all the good changes that have happened. Some minor complaints I have on the mobile port is the fact the app seems to not be as up-to-date to the PC version of the application. Most of the other complaints in my past review still remain unchanged. For example: All users are able to post whatever they want without the worry of a filter (unless a bot is set up in the server.) I’m still shocked by the fact that NSFW channels are able to be created on Discord when the app is rated 12+.

Most of the updates were mostly major bug-fixes. But at least the program is much more usable. All what I could really do is give the app another star for is efforts on keeping the app bug-free as possible.",3,2.3.5,BloxStar180,0
us,United States,11071319075,2024-03-21T21:28:57-07:00,Annoying,"I’ve enjoyed the app for a while, it’s good for communication between large groups- however, with every coming update I keep hoping and keep getting disappointed. The mobile app is so extremely buggy these days that I’ve been tempted to delete it and instead use the browser version of discord on my phone which is obviously quite hard to work with on it’s own because it wasn’t made for phones. Well in the one that’s made for phones it’s hard to find the pins of threads at all. It’s extremely frustrating that one cannot search threads but instead has to search the channel. As well, any channels that share names might have their pins swapped so then you have to go into the channel settings and look at the pins through there. Finally, and the biggest cause for my frustration, is even when my phone’s rotation is locked, if I try to search a channel or look at it’s settings/members then the screen will rotate some random way. It doesn’t matter if I’m holding my phone straight, sideways, upside down, it will rotate, it is especially annoying when trying to find something quickly.",1,221.0,SusieQ🙃,0
us,United States,8134503795,2021-12-15T18:08:45-07:00,"I love Discord, but I have one issue..","Okay. Straight to the point. Discord is great. I have been using Discord for years and absolutely love it. It lets me talk with my friends out of school, and lets me make new friends online. Great app if you want to keep contact but don't have their phone number.

Slight issue though. You see, I mostly use Discord on mobile, and I'm starting to have an issue with the status thing. I set something, then don't want it anymore. Yes I clear it, but then I closed the app to check for updates, none, so of course I went back to discord, but the status was still there, even though I removed it. I tried to remove it through my computer, but it did the same thing.

I was wondering if this could be just a Discord mechanic or a bug? I just want to make sure in case anyone else is experiencing this. And again, Discord is one of the best social apps I have ever downloaded onto my phone.",5,104.0,Valiel_,0
us,United States,10909069111,2024-02-06T08:42:39-07:00,The “new” and “improved” update,"Everybody’s talking about the new update, even a few months after so I thought I’d pitch in.  The only thing that effects new users are some features that are missing that weren’t there before, because most of the ui updates just frazzled current users muscle memory. Alongside that, there are various features that I’m still trying to find on the app that are not there, and if they are, discord has made 0 effort on explaining where they were moved to. This new update isn’t even helpful for most mobile users, and discord even used the old layout at the GOTY last year. Moments ago as I’m typing this a subtle change was made to the ui for attaching files and images. Once again, frying muscle memory and an unnecessary change. I’d like to see discord explain why. I don’t mean that in a defiant, sarcastic way, I mean that as in I want to know the reasoning behind it, and reasoning that ACTUALLY FOLLOWS instead of seeming like a blatant lie. Regardless, a lot of people agree the update was bad and I think discord needs to finally do something about it. This isn’t what we want, not in any way shape or form.",1,214.0,BlueInklingBoi64,1
us,United States,8550085110,2022-04-09T14:40:44-07:00,actually really cool,"Hey! I don’t usually rewrite reviews, I usually keep them as-is because I’m lazy or just delete them, but this is different. Discord is a very good app to talk on or make new friends :) I’ve had discord for about 4-5 years and it’s actually been a pretty good app to be on. I’ve had a really bad experience or two that wasn’t resolved (not sure if it will be) but despite that, I still use discord daily! My only issues are as follows.
	1) The report feature feels like it doesn’t work. I’ve reported a couple people because of a multitude of reasons, but they never got disabled and it’s .. not really good.
	2) Why is discord nitro only obtainable as a gift ONCE, and then you can never get a discord-provided gift again? I’ll be honest, I don’t actually understand. It’s a little weird in my opinion.
	Apart from those reasons, the app is great! Definitely recommended. Only thing is to definitely watch that block button, because some people deserve it instantly.
-Eirie",4,121.0,emzterz!! ★,0
us,United States,2267769810,2018-03-03T13:53:44-07:00,I hope you like crashing.,"I’ve been using discord for roughly a year or so now so it only made sense for me to get the app. While the interface is high quality and the community unique, I hate to say it but it has a tiny little problem with constantly crashing my phone. Initially this only started when I tried to load certain photos or gifs. Sure that was annoying but it was tolerable and rare. And then it took a nosedive for the worse. Now when I open up discord and enter a certain chat my phone spontaneously crashes. Now the problem is when you crash you still are left onto the same chat. Thanks to that I am forced to not be able to use the app until I either get messaged of uninstall and reinstall. In false hope I tried to access said chat once again. To my dismay it lead to the same cycle. I desperately want to rate this app higher than three stars but until this issue is fixed it will stay that way.",5,2.2.4,That one random review,2
us,United States,7437123384,2021-06-07T05:53:16-07:00,Parent Alert!!!,"This is NOT an app you want any child under 16 to have free access to...especially if you are not tech savvy.  Basically, you are allowing your child to chat with anyone.  I discovered some of the direct messages that were being sent to my son and they were completely toxic....memes about where to hide a knife at school, disturbing images, explicit content.  Oh, and some of the other  “friends” he was chatting with talked about how their parents just thought they were only communicating with other kids from school.  Do not fall for it parents!   There is one thing you can do (which I wish I had realized to do sooner) and that is only YOU, the parent, have the password.  Go into Privacy settings and set it so that no one can direct message your child, no friend requests etc.  If your child has the password, they will just change the settings back.  Make a condition of using it that your child doesn’t get the password.  Then they will have to ask you before adding anyone as a friend.  You will also be able to monitor everything they are doing which, sadly, you 100 percent need to do with this site.",1,77.0,svye7,9
us,United States,11943943639,2024-11-12T20:19:33-07:00,Bugs need to be fixed asap !,I have been using discord since 2020 so me and my friends could all chat and play some Minecraft together! And the app was actually running really smooth that year . But starting last year there was a huge bug that would cause me and my friends to not be able to hear each other. And there’s another bug that is causing me and a few members on my discord server to not be able to unmute because of discord all of a sudden freezing. So my advice to make the app run smoothly is to fix the problems that are causing discord to act weird and bring back the status thing that you can use while in a vc with your friends to inform them what you are doing ! Also I would really like to see and improvement for streaming Netflix movies with your friends and make it to where we can watch the movie without not seeing the movie being shown .,5,254.0,Starclothgaming,0
us,United States,13111917146,2025-09-07T19:47:47-07:00,Annoyances,"Discord is a fun way to communicate with my friends, however, there are some things that annoy me. Discord wants me to “verify” LITERALLY EVERYTHING. I cannot access the app right now without it asking me to verify my email/number. This is hard to do because your email/number can only be associated with one account. You’d have to delete, disable, or remove your number or email from one account to add it to another. Example, account 1 is logged in under my phone number. It asks to verify my email, but oh no! Account 2 is logged in under my email therefore my email “cannot be associated with” account 1. 

I recommend writing down a digital and physical copy of your password because forgetting it would be awful with how much work you’d have to go through to change it. 

When changing your password, Discord takes you to several different browsers and links, either having major sensitivity issues with what’s associated with what, and/or giving you a “rate-limit”. My number was put on a cool down for discord, I was trying to fix my two accounts. Back to the example; I wanted my email under my first account along with my phone number. Yet before I could even get to settings in my second account, the screen was taken up by a very stubborn notice that I had to verify my phone number. There is no way to exit out of the notice, only a link to get started. 

These things annoy me, otherwise the app is fun and I like it. Please fix this discord.",3,295.0,zzsunfl0wer,0
us,United States,7543148237,2021-07-05T14:06:24-07:00,Discord Reviews by Andrew Reynolds,"Don’t get me wrong, I love Discord and it really has a lot of nice people and people to talk to. But there is just 2 problems that make me uncomfortable with the app. There are a lot of Discord Predators out there and they are getting kids in danger or maybe kidnapping them. The next problem is the Toxic People on this app. I have a bunch of different friends on Discord, but there are a lot of mean people and hurting people on the inside. Some people don’t care about the ones who get bullied. But you don’t know what they feel, just like my friend left me because of a game. We was friends for 2 years and this happened about 4-5 days ago. So just don’t bully others on Discord please.

(P.S) some people won’t care about this review but it doesn’t matter. I focus on the ones who do care about the post and want to help with the Discord Community and what they are doing that wrong. 

Thanks for Viewing!",5,80.0,Down break,0
us,United States,10665137771,2023-12-06T17:14:48-07:00,This new update is NOT good.,"Listen to me when I say CHANGE THIS APP BACK TO ITS OLD LAYOUT. It’s amazing how you went from a simple and easy to use app, to a terrible and unnecessarily difficult app which consists of so many glitches when trying to move around to get to messages. I understand this update may have been made to be beneficial, but seriously, it is so slow and frustrating trying to figure out how to do even the most simplest things like screen sharing (and yes I know how to screen share now) but taking almost 15 minutes to find where a button is, it’s kind of funny.💀

Of course this is only just a review asking to resort back to the old discord layout. However, I think it would be appreciated if there was a way to resort back to the old discord, and I apologize if this came off disrespectful, but please reconsider that not everyone will know where everything is with this new layout, as it’s also a bit slower to configure with all these new things on my screen now, compared to the old and simple discord. Again this is not to be disrespectful, but many people including me, are not liking this new update.",1,207,effectedOx,0
us,United States,8627010009,2022-05-01T13:43:49-07:00,anyone else have this bug???,"so the app works fantastic most of the time, i’ve been using it for almost 4 years now but i recently broke my phone and i’m currently using a substitute from my family member until i get a new one, but for some reason on this phone i opened discord and the icon was just a discord stylized happy face and the profile edit page was only “log out”. i figured this account was disabled or really old so i did, and i tried logging into my own account but i got an “ultra rare error” or along those lines and i couldn’t log in at all. i deleted the app to try again since i sort of disregarded the error, but every time i redownload the app it goes to the page when you first open it then keeps loading forever. i’ve uninstalled and reinstalled multiple times and it keeps doing this, wifi or no wifi, fully charged, i’ve tried everything. does anyone know why this happened or what the source of the error can be?? (phone build is iphone X, near brand new)",3,124.0,myrrhvin,1
us,United States,7729650293,2021-08-24T09:00:26-07:00,Why do y’all hate privacy??,"For some background I have to use discord for school clubs and homework groups. It’s ok in the regard that it allows you to text with large groups of people for free. 

But my big problem is that there is no privacy from discord. Your friends can see basically everything you do on your device, including exactly what game you’re playing and song you’re listening too. There is no easy way to turn this feature off, especially on the mobile version. As someone with social anxiety, I can safely say that this was an absolute dealbreaker for me. I’m a super private person and I believe that I should have privacy on my device. Just because I’m in a discord chat with someone doesn’t necessarily mean I’m their BFF, and even if it did I still wouldn’t be comfortable with sharing my every move on Discord. 

PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE add a feature on mobile that allows you be completely private on discord. In fact, this is something that you should ask people if they’re ok with when they’re creating their accounts. I shouldn’t have to worry about facing social exclusion or bullying for my personal choices on my device!",1,87.0,~vibeyreviewgirl~,0
us,United States,4310799703,2019-06-13T12:15:44-07:00,Once-in-a-while apps,"Discord is one of those once-in-a-while apps that come along and completely implant itself into your life without you even noticing it. Like TV or something. You kinda take it for granted, I think. Like you sorta forget that there’s a dedicated team of folks working tirelessly to provide it.

But this is actually a compliment to the folks who’ve worked to create this app. This app is so stable, high-quality, easy to work with, and so infused with gamer/nerd/etc love that it just becomes a part of your life. Just, “Oh I’m gonna hang out on Discord,” is a perfectly good way to spend a night. You wouldn’t say that for any other app. You wouldn’t even say that for Skype. Who even uses Skype anymore?

This is one of the few cases where I felt compelled to throw money at these folks. It’s so dang good. I can’t even begin to describe the appreciation I have for being able to stay in close contact on a regular basis with my gamer friends across the world.",5,3.0.2,michaelgazzola,0
us,United States,6765673837,2020-12-17T23:24:08-07:00,Discord is certainly a 5 star app,I started using discord around June of 2020 and I must say that it’s definitely done good to my life. I’ve met so many amazing friends from servers and just through mutual friendships that had already existed. It helped me get through a lot of quarantine knowing that I had people to talk to and had a  reason to get up everyday. I could share and discuss different sorts of interests I had like gaming and anime. I could even create my own custom servers where I could toggle around the settings and fixture it to my own liking. There are just so many endless possibilities and opportunities on discord that I don’t think I could get anywhere else so easily and helpfully. I 100% recommend getting discord if you wanna socialize with people just like you or wanna call up some buds to game with. Discord is definitely the app that I think highlighted majority of the year and I hope it does for the most part too in everyone else’s shoes.,5,52.0,Cat lib,1
us,United States,13749125237,2026-02-14T10:14:57-07:00,going downhill fast,"This whole scan ID has been recorded as a disaster for any company that attempted to roll it out prior, the local scan option would have made it semi bearable considering this company has has multiple  security data breaches  last year that leaked everything on their drivers licenses, so the local option was a smart choice, but now I’m hearing that they switched to palantir instead of K-ID, are you kidding me? You could have picked any other verification company on the planet and you pick the  Orwellian data mining and pro surveillance state  company with an abysmal track record and CURRENT ties to assisting both domestic and international government spying and aiding them in other endeavors ,anyone’s that’s curious can search for the company’s name and see what I mean, I cancelled my subscription for the time being for nitro and have been looking for alternatives since everything’s going to be set to baby mode because I don’t want to hand my ID to one company that’s famous for its data breaches and the other company that’s famous on spying on people and selling their data",2,315.0,Ffs73855,0
us,United States,10921958924,2024-02-09T20:26:42-07:00,WHOMP WHOMP for Wumpus,"The new UI is so bad that I’m deleting the app… and actually remembering that I need to cancel Nitro. In what world does it make sense to put the member activity list at the top of the screen?? It looks bad, prevents you from seeing a consolidated list of who is online/offline without having to scroll (because SOMETIMES I want to see if multiple people I enjoy hanging out with are online within a specific channel and I don’t want to check each of their individual statuses and scroll ten thousand miles down a drop-down screen!), and did I say it looks bad? Because it does. Also WHY do you have to double tap your profile just to go to settings??? Like oh yeah, “there’s also a gear button at the top of the profile in the corner”, well why do we need a gear and a double tap feature when you could just access settings normally by clicking ONCE on the settings/profile tab?? There’s nothing convenient about the new UI! It’s terrible! Awful! Atrocious! Alongside every other stinking word for horrific there could possibly be. Instead of being “built different”, Discord mobile is now built like an inconvenience.",1,215.0,Bambi Bones,0
us,United States,10817473911,2024-01-13T07:09:31-07:00,Fire your entire mobile development team,"The mobile version of this app just two or more months ago worked fine with basically zero issues, aside from the very occasional crash - to be expected with any app.  Now after these “improvements” which have been pushed out recently, images and videos constantly refuse to load, you can’t preview images and videos when searching or viewing pins, the app crashes or freezes constantly, UI regularly becomes unresponsive and requires restarting, among a multitude of other issues.  There also seem to be a bunch of features which have been quietly removed for no reason, like the ability to perform complex message search queries with filters, and others.

Pro-tip, guys:  if nobody is complaining about the existing layout or functionality of an application, DON’T CHANGE IT!  I know that’s might be a shocker; I’ll give you a bit to let that sink in.  Might be time now to escort the monkeys you have banging away at keyboards on your mobile development teams out of the building and find a few replacements who actually know what they’re doing.",1,211.0,rm04567812,4
us,United States,10738244889,2023-12-24T00:05:02-07:00,"Really good app, few suggestions","I joined discord back in like 2019, and I really do enjoy it, it’s helped me keep in touch with a lot of friends and make even more. The most recent update with the entire layout change, I admit was pretty unnecessary, but I don’t think it’s bad. There’s quite a few things I find pretty useful from it, the only issue I have is that now when you’re in a server and look at what’s pinned in a channel, any image that’s pinned doesn’t pop up anymore, it just says that there’s an image attached to the message and then you have to jump back to the message to see what the image even is. Otherwise I find it rather easy to navigate.

I also wanna suggest being able to move your favorites emojis around, I have a lot that I love but I’d prefer to keep them more organized. Unfortunately to do that I’d have to unfavorite and then refavorite them repeatedly to bunch the ones I want together. It would be cool if I could just drag a favorited emoji before or ahead of another one.",3,209.0,luneymoonchild,1
us,United States,8372308932,2022-02-19T01:41:58-07:00,"App DOA with Magic Keyboard, no response from support","Have been happily using the app on iPad for years, but as of writing this review, it's been at least two weeks (and several app updates) since I've been able to press the Return key on my Magic Keyboard to send messages. Have to reach up and press send. Every. Single. Time. I don't think I have to tell you why that's unacceptable in a chat app.

I moderate several servers, including one tied to my workplace, and my iPad Pro is my primary device whenever I'm out of the house. As a result, this bug has been extremely frustrating, and despite submitting a support ticket and trying to reach out every way I can find, I've received no response of any kind. 

I almost never rate apps, unless I feel like I have something to say, positive or negative, and this time, what I have to say is this: Apps break, and that's okay, but don't ghost your users. Say something, anything, in response, even if it's just saying you're aware of it. Silence is just going to give people like me an excuse to start looking at alternatives instead of waiting.",2,114.0,Hiro the Fox,0
us,United States,13675679930,2026-01-25T14:26:27-07:00,Please help if you can,I love discord I have been using it for years. And me and my girlfriend have been using it to make our long distance work since it have the best volume and also js overall best platform for us since it is so well at being adaptable for the user’s individual needs. However. Since the last update we have been experiencing a weird bug. When we use a video call the call will make one of us freeze for the other. No sound or moving video. And the one who is frozen can still see and hear everything from the other person. I really love this app and I have extreme separation anxiety with my girlfriend so this app helps. But every time she freezes it makes me break down uncontrollably. If this is fixable could we possibly look into it? Since the update 5 days ago it’s been weird and i genuinely feel more alone now because of it.,5,312.0,Thętä,1
us,United States,14120214855,2026-05-29T10:12:27-07:00,Broke Discord's Community Guidelines,"I’m extremely frustrated with Discord’s handling of my account. For the past several months, I’ve repeatedly received emails and notifications claiming that I violated Community Guidelines, yet I’m given little to no explanation about what I supposedly did wrong. My account keeps getting locked or I’m kicked out of the app entirely, which has made it almost impossible to reliably use the platform.

What makes this even more upsetting is the lack of clear communication and support. I’ve tried to resolve the issue, but it feels like I’m stuck in a cycle of automated warnings and restrictions without any real answers. As a user, it’s frustrating to feel punished without transparency or a fair opportunity to understand and fix the issue.

Discord is supposed to be a place where people connect with communities, friends, and gaming groups, but this experience has honestly made the platform stressful and disappointing. I really hope Discord improves its customer support, account review process, and communication with users because no one should have to deal with months of repeated lockouts and unexplained violations.",1,330.0,Eagle-P,0
us,United States,9781310603,2023-04-02T22:49:56-07:00,New Feature Request,"I’ve been using discord for years now since I was a teen and I love using it, though an issue I’ve come across recently is hackers or certain scenarios occurring which result in deleting channels and categories that have a lot of history or important info within them that’s needed, which is why I believe a new feature could be made to help with the damaged.

An undo feature(similar to google docs) would be very useful in my opinion, where once a category or channel has been deleted, there is a time limit of at-least 30 days for it to be restored before the information is permanently deleted. This feature could be added in by making it so whenever someone presses the reorder button (by going through settings-channels and pressing the reorder button on the top right), a 4th option will show up that either says undo or restore, in which it’ll show recently deleted categories and channels that were deleted and also show how much time is left before its forever deleted. You can either choose to restore one at a time or select them all by dragging your finger down from the first category/channel you wish to restore and all the way to the bottom, in which you can press restore again(which can replace the reorder button for this since it’ll be showing a new screen without the already existing channels and categories) to restore any and all categories and channels that have been selected. 

I’d imagine it’ll take a certain amount of time for it all to be restored depending on how many was deleted, and possibly a limit on how many can be restored at a time, but I believe adding this feature could be a very beneficial addition to discord that many people could benefit from, especially largely-moderately populated servers that experience troubles among their own server members such as hackers and such. So please consider adding this feature to discord, I understand the possibility of this feature taking a-lot of time and effort to be implemented, but I do truly believe that it could help. If you’ve reached the end then I thank you for reading this review, and please consider this.",5,171.1,Joestar dada,0
us,United States,10715773194,2023-12-18T22:03:39-07:00,New update isn't worth it,"I've been using this app for nearly 5 years now and Discord recently just got a new UI update for the mobile users. At first I liked some of the changes such as putting the DMs in a new section so I can tell whether I get server pings or DM pings, but that did nothing to outweigh the cons (coming from an iPhone user with a newer iPhone):

-The app is very laggy now even on newer devices. If you move too fast, it'll take quick inputs as you pressing a spot that you don't want to go to or taking it as a second input to go back from where you came
-You have to manually clear the ""New Notification"" banner instead of it clearing when you get to the most recent message of a chat
-When you load a chatroom it sometimes loads you way further up into older messages, forcing you to scroll down just to see the new one AND THEN MANUALLY CLEARING THE NOTIF AGAIN
-Swapping from the DM interface to the server interface takes a solid few seconds, which is noticable compared to the previous UI taking seconds to swap between DMs to server messages

All in all, the new UI is just... Bad. It's not worth using or getting used to, as the browser and desktop version keeps the old UI which still works better than the new one. Discord is very much worth it to use as their previous updates were worth it, but for those of you that truly read reviews, I beg you, save yourself your sanity and use the browser or desktop version if possible.",3,209.0,Juloxia02,0
us,United States,10701613075,2023-12-16T02:27:18-07:00,I want to go back to the other version.,"I like using discord. I genuinely do. It’s one of the social media platforms I use most often. Unfortunately the update that I didn’t agree to getting since let’s be honest the previous version worked just fine makes discord work less well. The fact that the blue banner at the top of my screen that tells my that I have messages even when I am caught up on messages stays on my screen is really frustrating. The fact that there are now different tabs for messages and servers is really frustrating. This review is not me wishing ill on Discord. It’s not coming from a negative place, because like I said at the beginning of my review I like using discord. I have no ill will towards Discord as a company or platform or any of the people working there. I just think that the update that happened recently made the platform worse and slightly less usable. I really hope someone does something to make it better. Unfortunately I don’t expect that.",3,208.1,dstonemeier,1
us,United States,10700016663,2023-12-15T19:33:54-07:00,New update is bad,"I'm willing to overlook a lot of the changes that have been made in the past couple years-- I've been a user since 2017 and I understand that as apps grow, they need to center themselves more around money and less around the users themselves. That being said, there is no functional use for an unremovable new layout update, especially when most of the features are completely useless. The (probably ai generated) discussion topic notifications feel like such a waste of development and programming, and the ""new look"" does nothing for me-- it seems like it was made just to say they've been doing something. I'm of the firm belief that if something is good, you shouldn't feel the need to do anything to it. I understand that the feeling of stagnation is difficult to overcome, but all this app is doing with these updates is driving users away. Tl;dr, I haven't been a fan of the direction they've been moving over the years, but this update (as well as the other layout changes they've snuck in as a secret feature) has made me no longer willing to overlook it in the name of a decent app and concept",1,208.1,Karkatfan69,0
us,United States,10675976516,2023-12-09T13:56:45-07:00,The new redundant update,"Discord’s latest update to create a “fresh” “new” other buzzwords “mobile experience” has instead created several redundancies within the app, making it irritating to use at best. It used to be that all your servers and your direct messages were accessible in the same tab in just a few clicks (and discord also held your place in one while you checked the other), you could swipe left and right to perform most functions, and it was easy to search and pin messages. Now left swipe functionality has been removed, forcing you to navigate through new tabs that you did not need to access either servers OR direct messages, neither of which hold your place, as you have to back out of messages to get back to either tab. You cannot see image previews in your pinned messages or see who sent which message that was pinned, as all messages show up under the name of the person whose messages you’re searching. Notifications are redundant as a tab and it is actively more difficult to find and adjust settings.
I will be using the app as little as possible.",1,207,foxskullaltar,2
us,United States,9411692258,2022-12-18T21:59:23-07:00,Worked Fine Until... (iPhone 6),"I've been using Discord since 2020 and it's been great!

