us,United States,10668626268,2023-12-07T17:26:12-07:00,Awful Updated UI,"The updated UI is completely impractical and unnecessary. Discord was fine how it was. Now I barely want to use it. I’ve had reoccurring nitro for about 5 years now as I really enjoyed using Discord but this has to be the worst update ever rolled out to users. The functionality is terrible. I feel like I have to learn how to use the app all over again, which was already difficult in the first place. No one wants to put in the effort for that. The fact that DMs and servers are completely separate now has to be the worst part. Having everything in once place was so much easier and more efficient. Everything feels incredibly clunky, and it seems as if Discord is trying to update their platform to be more like other social media applications. That isn’t what Discord users want. If this UI really is staying, users should be given the option to use the version of Discord prior to this god awful update through the appearance tab in settings. Everything about this update is awful and unnecessary and the majority of the general public believes that. I wish Discord actually listened to their market.",1,207,miniaturesuga,0
us,United States,9344036301,2022-11-29T21:38:34-07:00,Latest issue,"Personally, I enjoy discord very much. From helping extend my personal view of various hobbies, to chatting with people from all of the world. I originally installed discord to use for better communication during game-rounds. But recently, it’s become an easier way to learn new things, and meet people with similar interests. But, the latest update regarding the setting of ‘DM spam control’ has caused my devices some issues. When I click the app, it opens and gives me the pop-up mobile tab. Once I click ‘got it’ the app then proceeds to stall on a half-loaded friends list, before closing the app automatically. It even does this on my pc, despise the amount of times I’ve restarted my devices, restarted the app, and re-installed the app. This is extremely frustrating, and is happening to both my german, and canadian friends. It has led to us all deleting the app temporarily, until this problem has been resolved.
Please fix this issue.",4,155.0,Mia8492,0
us,United States,6449491627,2020-09-20T08:17:32-07:00,Links and third part web sites used by discord members to stalk our children. DO NOT GET.,People are making servers trying to force people into dangerous situations. I joined a server this morning and I got a alert from the server saying that I was required to give certain information to the provided link. Long story short the link tracks you and taps your device and lets certain people with access watch and listen to you potentially whenever they please. I do not recommend discord to anyone due to my attempts to make light of situations like this have been ignored. I ended up buying a new line of device’s because of the possibility of them watching my children. You need to crack down on this discord it’s wrong and gross. Ive seen it in multiple servers most are game related such as factions or based in a child’s game such as Pokémon. I was met with hostility and was removed by every owner or administrator of the 6 servers I joined just for not using the link. This is bad discord no person should be able to send links like that to anyone something needs to be put in place to prevent people from preying on others who are using the app.,1,39.0,King Equinox,5
us,United States,6018411653,2020-05-31T09:54:09-07:00,Sharing Screens,"As a mobile user, it is unfortunate that we cannot share our screens on the mobile app. On an iPad Pro, I would honestly expect someway to share our screens; for business, art, help, etc. Google meets and many other programs/apps allow you to share screens. Why is it that the computer, laptop, PC program of Discord allows a share screen tab and not the mobile? I understand that it may be difficult to add features like so, but this just seemed like common sense. 
As a mobile artist, I would like to share my work progress with my friends and others. I do not use computer programs therefore I cannot share my screen to show my artwork process. This would be a very convenient and nice feature to add and I assure you it would be used regularly by friends, artists, businesses, etc.
Thank you for your time and I do hope you consider my recommendation.

As a side note, Discord works incredibly well! Very functional and smooth.",4,23.0,SalmonEnigma,3
us,United States,5772721517,2020-04-06T14:14:16-07:00,Verification did not work: useless,"I tried to set up Discord.  After getting the app and installing I tried to use it.  Two things failed; 1) I got an e-mail for verification.  When I verified it I was presented with a button to click marked “Continue to Discord.”  When I check on it the button responded visually but nothing else happened. 2) When I tried to launch the app on my phone I was greeted by a screen claiming “Something going on here,” and asked me to verify by phone.  I selected the country and entered my phone number and then received an “invalid number” response.

I then went to the support section and filled out a report about this after reading the requirements; no “burner” number, no landline, no prepaid numbers.  My number is a regular subscriber cell number.  After sending that in I got an automated response telling me the same info I had already read and responded to in my initial support request.  I was required to now respond to this bot response to get actual support.  I did so.  It has now been more than 48 hours since I sent that request and I have heard not a peep.

I have deleted the app from my phone and will never download it again.",1,15.0,Grameðla,2
us,United States,2305004310,2018-03-14T05:02:35-07:00,"Some good, some bad","Love all the features (like drag and drop images), customization, I am warming up to the interface... but the voice chat digitizes often, and my group (representing every time zone in North America) always ends up defaulting to Team Speak for the clarity of voice transmission. Which is a pity; it doesn't have nearly the features, and the interface is miserable. We've noticed that voice seems to digitize worse when playing a game... which is the point of the app. I paid for a year's subscription to Turbo, hoping that this will help improve the app; if you can fix the voice transmission issues, you'll have my group's loyalty.

Thanks for the response! I just want high quality sound that doesn't digitize and break up constantly. If you offered a higher-quality connection for pay, I'd pay for it, because I really like the text message interface. Thanks!",5,2.2.5,copper9lives,0
us,United States,10530252627,2023-10-29T20:52:51-07:00,uh help? 😭,i think discord is a good app for communicating with friends and for work which is why i’m kinda sad i can’t log into my account. Maybe a month ago i went to log in but it said that i was in a different location before which happens frequently for me. Usually i turn my wifi off and try again but this time i hit “forgot password” bc i’m a little slow in the head. Now i cant login unless i change my password via email. Simple i can just go do that except i have quite literally 17 emails and every email has the same password except for this one which was meant to be an email linked to an account i was going to give away so i couldn’t use my personal password. So now i can’t login into my email and i can’t log into my account until i log into my email. I’ve tried using devices that are already signed in but it’s no use. what do i do?,5,201.0,unhappy person >:(,0
us,United States,13037748542,2025-08-19T20:24:28-07:00,All they want is Personal Private Information now.,"It’s sad really, I used Discord for many years, but now they demand my phone number to be able to use their services. In an age where governments are forcing real ID and sending police to citizens homes for having the “wrong” opinion online, I rather have privacy. You know? The core feature that Discord was built on. But now all they care about is appeasing their bigger and richer corporate overlords for a slightly bigger cut of the pie. They completely turned on the customers that got them to where they are today. I wouldn’t doubt for a second that if you give Discord your phone number like they demand, not request, they turn it right over to those bigger companies so they can make a more complete profile on you. I will never be on Discord again.

Update to developer response: I reviewed your article and all it states is “for safety and verification purposes” it doesn’t provide a real reason. Why does it NEED to be my phone number? What does my number do for safety? Why do you need it for verification when you have my email? Also it states why you may get the request for verification and none of them apply to me whatsoever. It’s even more clear, this is just to grab customer data in preparation for a real ID push and to share with the bigger corporations to get even more money from. This is against everything that made Discord what it is to this day. Also another footnote, this isn’t optional, it blocks my entire app long as I don’t provide my number. It’s a method to try and force data out of consumers. You like playing with your friends don’t you? You don’t want to be left out? Well you better give me your personal identifiable information or you’re screwed. Nah, I’ll just use other applications with a focus on providing me good service without costing my privacy via blackmail. Terrible disgusting company.",1,293.0,ImJustBusted,2
us,United States,12367957722,2025-02-28T23:06:40-07:00,Frick AI / Cancelled Nitro,"Cancelled my Nitro (3 years) because of the recent AI update. Discord basically added a button to do AI renditions of images posted including a ‘ROAST’ option that will absolutely encourage bullying. When your image - your artwork, face, and sensitive images are put through AI Image generators that data, YOUR DATA is part of the dataset now and the pattern of your artwork, body, or face can be used to create new images without your knowledge or consent. This is not just disrespectful to artists but to everyone. Do you want people up make any image of you that they want? Of your kids? ANYTHING? Discord makes that incredibly easy and BAD news, there’s no way to opt out or disable it in your servers. They make it easy and encourage this behavior by putting it front and center to let users have final say on what happens to images you share only for the sake of being viewed and connecting with others. ALL FOR PROFIT that is hair brained at best as consumers have said they do not want ai and companies do not listen. Also it’s straight up illegal in some countries. Looking forward to seeing this app crumble under lawsuits someday.",1,268.0,klorent,4
us,United States,10509621919,2023-10-24T01:41:01-07:00,"Discord is great, the new app update is dreadful.","I hated it the second I saw the new interface. Nothing stands out, all the servers and all the channels just kind of blur together. Even server groupings, which were great, have become waaaay useless. Groups just look like another server. Discord was always a lot of information to process and the interface was never great, but was reasonable for everything it needed to handle….until the update. I took a step back and gave it a try. Maybe it will grow on me….no, the same issues of everything just being hard to identify at a glance is too much. Definitely don’t enjoy using discord on mobile now, will probably use less than I have and try to put off a lot of interactions until I can get to a desktop version.

Edit: Found out there is an old/new interface toggle. GOODBYE NEW INTERFACE!!! You were nothing but hot garbage.",5,201.0,Meamone,1
us,United States,6026560136,2020-06-02T09:48:33-07:00,My discord nitro is suddenly gone? help.,"I’m going to cut right into the chase. Overall this is a very good app and i’ve been using it since January 2018. I use this app to contact my friends and have a nice time in vc’s and stuff, but i’ve just encountered something so irritating. When I was making emotes in my server, my nitro just suddenly disappeared. Also, i’m fully AWARE that my nitro ends somewhere around June 27th, June 28th, because I just bought another like a week ago. I feel like my money has been robbed because this is the second time this happened to me. It’s strange because I had nitro and I was using my emotes, but suddenly it just doesn’t work anymore. If you’re reading this, please solve this problem and regain my nitro back. My discord is Dark..#1590 I’m not sure whether this is a glitch or not, but I can’t fathom what’s happening right now. Please solve this case, or at least give me a refund.",5,23.0,subscribetoWillyWilmer,0
us,United States,12880643777,2025-07-11T14:40:16-07:00,great app to call and text,"sound and video quality are consistently excellent—much better than FaceTime or Zoom, which can be unreliable. Plus, it doesn’t require a phone number, which makes it super convenient to connect with friends from other countries who can’t use FaceTime. It works great for me overall.

That said, the experience really depends on who you interact with, some servers and users can be toxic, so it’s important to be mindful of the communities you join and the people you add. Another downside is the media sharing limitations: unless you pay for Discord Nitro, sending videos and pictures can be a bit frustrating due to file size and quality caps. And while the cute stickers and customizable profiles are fun, they definitely tempt you into subscribing.

Despite a few downsides, I think Discord is a great app—especially for communication and building communities.",5,287.0,isa ibiza,0
us,United States,14370500600,2026-07-31T06:00:39-07:00,"Lazy, trash support","I edited my original comment for a response to the developer but it didn’t go through.. The lack of transparency and accountability is astonishing. They had a World Cup promotion where if you gifted nitro to somebody, you could select one of two rewards(an avatar frame and nameplate.) Well, I wanted both so I gifted nitro twice thinking I could get both. I looked for ANY kind of message indicating only one was redeemable. When I contacted support, it took over a week for a response saying I was not eligible for a refund. In NO way, shape or fashion did I ask for a refund or even imply it!! Another week has passed and still NO response!! The extra $10 spent on the second gift is something I can get over but these people don’t have the guts to apologize for their lack of transparency and simply just say “hey, we’re sorry but only one reward was redeemable.” So it’s the principal, especially knowing if I disputed with my card my account would be banned. I WILL NOT be subscribing to nitro again nor gifting it. I WILL be advocating to my friends and as many people as possible to do the same and not support this company.",1,339.0,uDontNeedMyName…,0
us,United States,13730963247,2026-02-09T08:13:51-07:00,Face Scan/ID,"Be aware: Discord is rolling out mandatory Face Scan/Gov ID uploads for age verification in March, and if you don’t, you’ll have your features reduced. 

I’ve been a big discord user since about 2016, and never had an issue really. Works great, all the function for free with only fun bonuses for a subscription. But forcing everyone to provide a face scan or government ID to fully utilize a chat service? No thanks. 
Especially after September/October of last year, in case you forgot that your own company JUST HAD a data breach. User IDs, and personal info were leaked through a third party vendor (Guess who’s handling these new scans/ID photos 🤡). Now only four or five months later, you’re forcing global mandatory face/PII uploads? But it’s okay because the corporation has assured us in an interview with The Verge that “We’re not doing facial recognition, or biometric scanning. We’re doing facial estimation [by ai]. The ID is immediately deleted. We do not keep any information around like your name, the city you live in…”
Sure, just like all of our PII was safe with the last third party vendor you used to store our info that “wasn’t saved.”",1,314.2,OPAFGinger,0
us,United States,10671942985,2023-12-08T14:44:39-07:00,Discord's nee update is terrible.,"I've been using discord for years, so I'd like to make it apparent about how much I like the app, but how terrible it's nee revamp is. To start: the color schemes are too dark and hard to see things in, I don't know why the also added a midnight mode on top of all that. The new interface is too restrictive now forcing me to find and open up several modules just to see if I got messaged or of someone in my dms said something, or even just to see if my friends are online. The previous versions allowed me to see all I needed to with a single swipe, why does it now have to be locked behind several worse mechanics? I usually never write reviews for mobile apps because it's a waste of time, but this update convinced me to tell everyone reading this not to use mobile unless you like using hard-to-use apps just to contact a few friends.",5,207,Fives16,4
us,United States,11415726954,2024-06-23T16:19:56-07:00,The reason why I put 3 stars,"Okay so first of all I love the app, it's a great way to communicate with your friends or online friends and what not. But the thing I hate is when I get a Discord Email Verification, 2 days ago this happened to me AGAIN for no reason at all. This has happened 8 times already. And this time it randomly popped up for no reason. I want you to improve this because I've made MANY gmail accounts and they kept on logging me out. This is why I'm filing a complaint to you about this because this is ridiculous. I didn't do anything bad nor sexual for it to do that again. This has probably the longest time it hasn't done it and it came back. Do better because now I can't talk to my friends, I have to figure out how to fix it, maybe make a new gmail account or delete the app. I feel like Discord is targeting me and I did nothing wrong to deserve this. Fix your app please. Because now it's making me stressed and I have to keep trying to fix it. Bad review",3,234.0,TheartistKaelyn,1
us,United States,11296336479,2024-05-22T17:15:06-07:00,UI Changes,"Let me preface that I enjoy using the app, it’s a great way to stay in touch with friends or play games together. It’s also great for finding and joining communities.

That said, as developers tend to do, in pursuit of improving UI, changes are being made often enough that by the time I get fluent in the new format, it changes and I have to get used to the change. As an example, in a previous update, Discord’s developers elected to alter where the friend messages tab was, moving it from a window at the top left of the screen to a tab near the bottom. Now, they have changed it back. Why? It seems like if the interface being in the bottom was superior it wouldn’t have gone back. If it was changed due to negative feedback, maybe it would be better not to make major UI changes. Find a format that works and keep that format, update small things. Not major things, again, like the friend messages tab.",4,230.0,Mjkinser16,0
us,United States,10920933809,2024-02-09T13:11:08-07:00,Bring back the old UI or the toggle for it,"The new UI is incredibly buggy and doesn’t let you quickly change between servers and DMs. Removing the option to change to the old layout was a horrible option. This new layout has significantly lowered my opinions about discord even more.

