us,United States,11624091431,2024-08-18T05:05:36-07:00,New layout,"I updated discord recently because my call kept crashing repeatedly for no reason. Big mistake. I can’t collapse the sidebar anymore and the layout feels extremely crowded. It literally makes me feel claustrophobic to open discord. Collapsing the servers on the side should be an option, like what is this layout? I hope the next update fixes this.

Update:
Discord responded with a link to information about the new layout. While I appreciate the response, the link basically says that the new layout is here to stay and has instructions on how to use it. Very unhelpful answer, I can intuit how to use the app, I’m saying that everything feels cramped and ugly and small and I hope that they will consider readding the message button to the bottom and swipe feature in the future because THE APP FEELS VERY VERY CRAMPED. It has not improved the user experience in my opinion, and if you search “new discord layout” there are lots of people echoing this very sentiment. At the very least, there should be an option to have this mode versus the other. I hope you will consider this in the future.",1,242.0,I<3Scams,1
us,United States,11446806021,2024-07-01T20:56:56-07:00,Accounts getting Banned,"Discord has been banning accounts based on age verifications for accounts that are 8+ years old. They're not answering their tickets and many people who've paid for nitro aren't getting compensated for their time lost on their subscription. The company needs to do better when people are paying money to fund their company. Even when following all the directions provided in the email they still have failed to bring back many many accoutns which I might add have a TIME LIMIT on when they can come back. I recommend everyone who paid for nitro to either keep trying or call their bank and claim fraud because this is exactly what it is, you didn't get the full month/year you paid for. Please try to understand as your consumers we have built communities and have connected with many people based on this platform and for that to be taken away and potentially deleted because of suspicion on being underage is crazy, if that was really the case you guys should make everyone do an age verification PRIOR to making an account. Please find this message, thank you.",1,236.0,Cowlei on insta,1
us,United States,11293644662,2024-05-21T23:44:39-07:00,"Please discord, hear our pleas.","I absolutely LOVE discord. My friends are on it, and we use it 99% of the time to communicate. However, I just cannot understand why this new UI update is not reversible?? I absolutely loved the old UI, it was clean, unique, efficient, and no one had any issues with it. I could say the same thing about the #tag situation but that’s just a small thing. Discord mobile is just garbage now. I can’t even navigate it half the time because all of my muscle memory is useless. If optimizing and making the mobile app more app friendly was in mind, why does it take like 2 more button presses to do the same things I could’ve done with just a swipe? None of this makes any sense. Discord please, there’s a plethora of people disagreeing with this ui change and you’ve yet to address it. What happened to the discord that actually used to take in feedback from the people, Not a single person wanted this, it really wasn’t necessary. I really hope you at least add a toggle so people can chose which discord ui they prefer, because this new one is so useless it’s not even a joke.",1,230.0,Djhhchh,2
us,United States,10700605708,2023-12-15T21:57:00-07:00,Why this update,"The UI is so much less intuitive and clunkier to use I don't even know where to start. ""Dark mode"" being significantly darker and higher contrast, while dropping what's basically Discord's signature colour scheme at this point in the process, is massively annoying and worse in terms of accessibility — I use low contrast colour schemes on all my apps, and this new dark mode is actively giving me migraines to use. Not to mention, why even have dark mode *and* the black with white text setting when the new dark mode is barely a couple shades lighter than the black? It's the same thing at this point, there's no reason to have three options when two of them are only negligibly different. The fact that there are other colour schemes but they're locked behind the $10/mo paywall is also terrible— I can have basic accessibility settings like low contrast but only if I pay for premium? Garbage. All this, and the new layout just looks like Discord wants to be X. Put the DMs and sidebars back where they were, remove the swipe left to reply thing, and put old dark mode back at *least*.",1,208.1,CorvusxCorone,1
us,United States,9156579781,2022-10-06T03:35:21-07:00,Basic Functionality Issues,"Voice chat randomly breaks where the people I talk to will suddenly not hear me when I’m still talking. I won’t notice till it becomes apparent that nobody is responding back to me. When I switch from Phone internet to Wifi internet the same thing happens. I’m still in the call and can hear people, but they can’t hear me. Also, the feature where when you’re watching someone’s stream and tilt the Phone sideways so you get a larger wide screen version of their stream stopped working. Before I could do a workaround where tapping the multi-person view icon then double tapping on the screen would fix it. But now that doesn’t work. This specific feature works just fine on my older iPad, but not my newer iPhone 11.

This phone app is gradually becoming more and more broken with it’s basic functionality. These issues have persisted for many months and have never been fixed.",4,147.0,Rabidkanid,0
us,United States,7878816738,2021-10-04T17:22:09-07:00,More Colors Please??,"Hello. I have been on Discord for about 2 1/2 years now if not a little more. I have enjoyed the convenience it has provided when it comes to interacting with friend who don’t share the same devices as I do. However, most of the servers I am in the members have designated colors. One is Rose, I am Cyan, another is White, and so on and so forth if you catch my drift (aka Among Us colors) and we are wanting a more expanded response to message coloration. So if we respond with a heart I would like to use Cyan, Rose would use a light pink, and so on. There are some colors already offered. But we want a waaaaaay bigger color spectrum to be offered when it comes to certain emojis. The same thing with the tags or roles in the servers. More colors please. This would be much appreciated. That is really the only issue I believe I have with the app/program. Other than that I love it and it is very useful.",5,94.0,ScatCat101,0
us,United States,8964596657,2022-08-10T07:13:55-07:00,Just No,"I wouldn’t even give it a 1 star. Low privacy. The backgrounds are bad. Light mode hurts my eyes and just overall quit due to realizing how bad it can be. Apparently now you can’t direct email them you have to submit a report And wait and hope they respond. I don’t recommend it and even though I’ve been waiting for a response back I just rage deleted my email so if they responded I wouldn’t even be able to tell. Support and help service wise and email wise seems slow in my opinion but it did say 24 hours-48 hours response or so if I remember correctly so I guess I’m not really complaining there. 
But I’ve heard lots of bad things about the app from my friends who are way more tech savvy and have more knowledge than I do. I’m not very up to date on phone stuff and laptop stuff anymore but it seems like it has more bad news than good news and it just doesn’t sit well with me in general. 

Sorry for the long paragraph I have a tendency to ramble lol. But to summarize I guess what I can say is just download with caution Id rather stick to different social media apps than this gaming Chatting app thing.",1,139.0,Goonymcgoon2164,0
us,United States,8532608087,2022-04-04T17:54:01-07:00,One little problem,"I don’t usually leave reviews, and the app works great, but as you can probably infer from the title, there is one little problem that I haven’t seen anyone else mention. I downloaded the new update, and almost immediately my app found a new way to glitch. When I go into the app to check notifications, they’re immediately marked as read, no indicator next to the server that there’s any new messages at all. Unless I’m in the app when they’re sent, channels don’t light up and it does not tell me where new messages begin. 

I’ve uninstalled and reinstalled the app three times, which allows me to see new messages, but continues doing exactly what it was doing before. It’s not hindering, but annoying, and I had no similar issue before installing the new update. I’ve searched settings extensively just to be sure it’s not a problem on my end, and it doesn’t seem to be. 

Fix this, thank you",4,121.0,its_Veronica_L,1
us,United States,10444994700,2023-10-06T05:57:43-07:00,"Listen the Reason I Put 5 Stars is to tell you, don’t download","Ok, maybe it works for you. But it took me over 50 tries to get in. Once I got in and got a group. I tried to verify, I changed my password because it wouldn’t let me in AGAIN. Then after that, it wouldn’t let me talk to my group, and basically do anything. When I tried to change my password it wouldn’t load, and it kept on saying “Connecting” even though I had good internet and connection. I tried so many times to change it but it just wouldn’t load. Sure you might say “but- you changed your password! that’s why!” Maybe, but it would still let me have access to everything. And let me choose my Password. Redo it, whatever. But it doesn’t work. So Discord. If you are reading this, please fix it. So that way I don’t have to redownload and repeat the same process of your mistake.",5,198.1,DensitySquared,0
us,United States,14409216259,2026-08-09T21:53:12-07:00,A bad habit,"As a longtime user, Discord got popular by a lot of coincidences, and has a bad habit of falling into every tech company's trappings as a result. The history of the program and later app involves a stunning amount of trial and error, yet a continued refusal to be up front about the errors. It's not the fault of any individual who might read this, but it's really an app we use because we have to, not out of preference. I used to support it and stopped because of these failings; I've never spent or even looked at the currently existing micro-transactions because they feel antithetical to the part I supported.

A captive audience isn't a loyal one, and eventually a poorly thought out decision like a games market, an nft system, a crypto market, and so on will stick and we'll find a new program, like we did with Skype. Unfortunately one of the best ways to encourage loyalty is also inconvenient, being transparent user-support communication. You know, so we would be able to give feedback without relying on private emails or third party review systems.",2,340.0,FLKNX,1
us,United States,11400940964,2024-06-19T18:05:41-07:00,ouh thats not..,"The new layout is actually the ugliest thing ive ever seen. My update usually comes in late so I already saw from others how bad it is and im displeased myself now thats its updated on my end. Im annoyed mostly by most of the changes to the dm part. Now you can’t simply swipe to the side to see whos online and all the extra buttons, now it takes you fully away from the chatting part and is fully unnecessary?? I think swiping over was more simple and took up less space. The profile changes are a little less but is still infuriating. First, now theres two buttons instead of just editing it once your there. As well with the status button, now trying to change your status from the little icon in the corner isn’t possible it just takes you to your profile. This also seems unnecessary when going to your profile in the first place isnt that difficult of a task, its easier to new users I guess but just kinda stupid at the same time.",3,233.0,hot milfs in ur area,0
us,United States,10669307475,2023-12-07T22:49:10-07:00,New Mobile Layout,"The most recent update has completely altered the way mobile works on Discord. It is not an inherently bad idea in itself, however, I and many others have complained about its features. Pinned messages do not show images nor full messages if they are long (without ANY indicator that there is more text added along with the said message), making pins ultimately useless. At the very least starboards can fix this issue, but in DMs, it is simply trash.

Additionally, the ease at which you can accidentally swipe off DMs/channels without the ability to switch back by pressing the server/messages button on the bottom tab is inconvenient. Rather than making these tabs do little emotes when double-tapped, why not have it so that double-tapping these will swipe it to the latest group chat/DM/channel?

DM pins are odd. Even if a message is pinned that *I* sent, it shows up as my DM partner’s message. Why? It’s stupid. 

Getting rid of the ability to search for messages before/after/during certain dates, in specific channels, mentions of certain users, and with specific embeds/links/files and making it a separate tab is inconvenient as well. If you wish to keep that, at the very least let users type “before:” and have the command WORK.

The links and files tab is also useless if you have a feature where you can search for links and files already. There is no point in having two tabs for that.

I have never had any issues with Discord glitching, crashing, nor have I experienced many bugs. Now, that is no longer the case—an incredibly frustrating discovery.",3,207,P0TAT03S,0
us,United States,10668440357,2023-12-07T16:03:35-07:00,The Fall of Discord,"don’t get me wrong i love discord as it offers things many other apps don’t but the recent updates have left me furious. 
     completely changing the mobile UI and refiguring a bunch of stuff like the placement of DMS and servers while these changes were entirely unnecessary and not wanted or needed by any users of this platform. alongside this you can’t view the server members list directly anymore since you need to find it by clicking the channel name instead of just swiping to the right. i despise these changes, as well as the search feature being utterly useless compared to before. why am i not able to view pictures through the search feature ? that defeats the purpose entirely as i cannot even view what i’m searching. also the search feature no longer auto-completes text so you need to search entirely by memory. in addition to this you are unable to search for messages sent throughout the entire server, instead you can only search channel by channel, which also makes no sense whatsoever.
     the smooth and clean look doesn’t bother me at all but the major changes to the UI and search features have made me irritated as this makes navigating the app and using it way more difficult than how it was before. that’s without mentioning the increased amount of bugs and glitches discord mobile has been receiving along with the terrible updates. meanwhile the developers and support team have addressed the incredible backlash from the new mobile UI by telling us to “get used to it” when no one wanted or asked for these changes. 
      this is ultimately the fall of discord, as their team purposely makes their app more difficult to navigate all the while ignoring their users as we voice that these changes are absolutely terrible and ridiculous. that being said, i hope that the developers can listen to their user base and hopefully bring back the features that we loved before…",1,207,COOLawesome3456,0
us,United States,10392649431,2023-09-21T13:01:26-07:00,What do you want. What do you need.,"I’ve had discord for a couple of years, never really had a problem with it. 
One day I decided to delete discord for personal reasons, so I canceled all my subscriptions to Nitro and deleted discord. Then I decided to redownload discord, but it keeps asking me to verify to see my billing information. 
I don’t want to see my billing information because I’m not paying for anything right now. But when I close out of the verification thing Discord just doesn't download. What. 
So I try downloading again and this time I verify to see my billing information, I see that everything is fine. So I tap out of it, Discord just doesn’t download. 
So as I’m about ready to break something, I go through the whole process again and this time removed a card from my billing. Discord still doesn’t download. 
I go through the whole process again and I re add that card, then it says I still need to verify to see my billing information. 
If I hit cancel, Discord doesn’t download. If I hit continue it just sends me back to my billing information and discord still doesn’t download. 
So right now I need to know what discords wants from me. I don’t have any active subscriptions and I’m definitely not subscribing to anything anytime soon. 
So why do I need to see or put in any billing information.",5,196.0,Aubriel.breezy,1
us,United States,8348894009,2022-02-12T14:48:58-07:00,Good App Bad People,"I have had Discord for years and years. Not sure how many but probably around 5 years. I have loved Discord and making new friends, hanging out with people, and finding people who are interested in the same things I am. The sad thing is that recently more and more Sexual Predators have been reaching out to children on the app. Yes I do understand that children shouldn’t be on the app but it doesn’t make it okay. I’ve seen it happen several times and have even gone out of my way to get them in trouble. I had reported these account along with many children (7-11 years of age) and Discord did nothing. They asked for more and more and more proof. I gave evidence of them talking about their age and gave evidence of what the predators had done. They took 0 action to protect their members on Discord. Although it’s a great app you truly do have to watch and be careful who you are talking to. People don’t always have the best intentions.",4,113.0,💊Klaus💊,0
us,United States,7240933083,2021-04-19T12:04:01-07:00,Honestly expected a better experience,"I am a discord user, and I have to say I have never been more frustrated and surprised. For an app that everyone uses that works for everyone, I never thought I’d have this experience. I used to have an account, but I wanted to make a new one simply so I can use it for a certain website. So I decided to put in my information and make the account. I didn’t know at the time that I already had an account that had the same exact info. So it told me another account has this info and it can’t be used. So I decided to delete the account that already had the info. (Side-note:  Really? 14 days just to delete 1 account?! You guys are out of your minds!) Once I waited 14 freaking days, I decided to try and make the account again. Still didn’t work. So I was really confused on to why a DELETED account is still in their database?! I figured since they are still keeping the account alive, I might as well just use it. I tried to reset the password and it worked, but it still being me to the screen where it thinks something weird is going on! FIX YOURSELF DISCORD!!",1,69.0,Its_RachieXD,3
us,United States,10667929579,2023-12-07T12:15:57-07:00,New UI is completely unintuitive,"The new UI is extraordinarily cluttered. Switching between DMs and servers had previously been a seamless and easy process, but now it takes even more steps. You cannot see the friend list by swiping anymore. And swiping tries to reply to messages which is a function no one needs as replying was already simple. Pins no longer show pictures, which is almost entirely what most of my server used pins for in the first place. Also, the new night mode is physically painful to look at. Like it truly strains my eyes to pain. As someone who doesn’t own a computer, I rely on discord mobile to be able to talk to my friends in general, since many of them live in other countries. Frankly, this update almost made me uninstall despite that. The ability to have something that worked decently like the desktop version had actually been refreshing, but instead of simply fixing the issues the app had, they decided to overhaul it to a version that just makes usage harder. I don’t know what they were thinking with this, but they need to fix these issues ASAP.",1,207,Kattat1661,0
us,United States,10098587567,2023-07-03T00:51:30-07:00,Please do something about this,"Hello I’m not gonna lie I love discord but I’m kinda wondering are you guys checking chats cause I literally got traumatized because of a server, so I was getting asked to show pics of my body specifically my legs, which I’m very insecure about and this man did not only ask me but pretty much every girl who joined the server to show their legs to prove their a woman, and I was a minor and he also told me he could impregnate me just because I said I wanted to have a family in the future, he also showed animal abuse which is why I said I got traumatized he showed a kitten getting it belly beat open and sliced too, and the other people on the server not all of them were defending him when I took a screenshot of him telling me that he could impregnate me, and that same man was also body shaming, and I know there are more servers like this so please do something about this!",5,184.0,Candyglaa,0
us,United States,3649207601,2019-01-14T05:23:01-07:00,Better than Skype by a lot,"I use Discord often on my computer and sometimes on my phone and I absolutely love it! Discord is easy to use and the fact that they let you make your own servers completely free is pretty cool, especially when compared to a specific VoIP application.. (stares at TeamSpeak) Anyways, one you make a server, adding new channels, roles, and categories is a breeze! All you need to do is click a few buttons and type a little bit to setup your very own server! You can also add friends where you can use Direct Messages (DM) to just have a 2 person conversation with your friends, or start a Group DM instead of making a server that can hold up to 10 people. Voice channels/calls are a big part of Discord and need reliability, but unless you have bad internet, most of the time the voice servers are pretty reliable. Overall, I love Discord and will probably continue to use it for a long time.",5,2.4.1,Robloxlover1025 456,0
us,United States,7448487799,2021-06-10T05:25:04-07:00,Completely Useless,"I started a thread with a suggestion. Someone asked we why I made the suggestion. Then everyone started labeling me a ‘complainer’ amongst other awful things. So, let me get this straight…They asked me why I was making the suggestion and I answered it, now I’m a complainer? All I wanted to do was make a suggestion and have a meaningful conversation about how to improve the game. There are a lot of hateful and spiteful subhumans in this app. If your looking for meaningful conversation about game improvements, this is not the place. Just send your suggestions directly to the company that makes the app. People are ignorant and disrespectful. Honestly, the interface is a complete train wreck. People have nothing relevant to offer. It’s very tribal and the moderators are just as bad. It’s just a steaming mess of hot garbage.

Stay away from Discord, it’s toxic and a waste of time. Just when you thought the human race couldn’t get any worse with Facebook and other social media…enter Discord. I just deleted my account, removed the app, bleached my phone and took a long shower to scrub off the remaining slime from using this app.",1,78.0,Jeff----,2
us,United States,5370366482,2020-01-06T18:13:05-07:00,Amazing app just a few minor problems,"Great app, I’ve been using it for a long time now but in these resent updates there has been glitches with the calls and notifications. If I’m in a call with someone on Discord it will show up as two separate tabs on iPhone, and when I lock my phone it shows up as a call so I won’t be able to see the time or any other notifications and it’s a struggle to get it to close just so I can see the lock screen of my phone. And with the notifications, there’s not a problem for when u mute a server or chat, u won’t get a notification because that’s what it’s suppose to do, but even when u don’t mute or turn off notifications for a server or chat it won’t give you the notifications. And I know it’s not just me with this problem my friends and basically anyone I talk to on Discord has this problem. I hope this problem can be fixed in the future and I appreciate all the hard work that’s been put in this app.",4,3.1.9,Aslice06,0
us,United States,5584373021,2020-02-26T13:14:23-07:00,It’s pretty decent,"Honestly I love discord.  I joined it a while back and use it almost every day.  I love the idea of bots too, I haven’t seen many other apps do something like that.  It has so many features and consistent updates.  Though it has (somewhat rare) issues like the entire app not working for a bit.  It can be very inconvenient depending on what you’re doing at the time.  Though this isn’t too bad as it’s often fixed very quickly, within a day at most.  It’s no worse than any other chatting app at the very least.  So it isn’t worth docking a star.  It’s not perfect, but no app is.  It’s next to perfect, and isn’t that the best something made by definitely 100% humans who aren’t actually robots gathering our info as they slowly find ways to put the human brain into a trance therefore mind controlling us so they can finally take over the world can get?",5,3.2.0,Ponnukio,0
us,United States,12988176453,2025-08-07T11:55:50-07:00,Terrible service,"My account was hacked by a hacker who impersonated my friend. So I went to discord and  told them and They emailed me saying that any purchases made to the account won’t happen and any Changes made to servers that I’m in won’t happen. Yet my friend says he is no longer in the server that is under my ownership, but he says he doesn’t know why which makes me believe that the hacker kicked people from my server or he deleted it. And I told discord about it and they told me if I believe my account was tampered with to make a couple steps to adding protection, I told them my account was tampered with and after they sent me a survey to rate how I felt about the service so far and I told them the service was bad and so they told to fill out the survey again and it repeated the entire system to me again and for the third time they sent me the survey. Since emailing discord isn’t working and they are making no progress in helping me fix my situation. Now more people are getting hacked and the hacker is hopping from accounts to others. They don’t have good service and dont listen to their users",1,291.0,S¡nJi,0
us,United States,12090306075,2024-12-21T13:50:49-07:00,Make the old discord interface an option again!,"In mid-2023, when Discord first started ringing alarm bells about a major update, I gave it a test run. I was horrified. The update I saw completely reconfigured the interface, removing the features I used the most and adding “features” that only served as distractions. This was a genuine accessibility problem for me. I tested the interface several times over the course of a month, but I was simply unable to get used to it. So just a couple days before Discord was due to update, I disabled automatic updates on my phone. I haven’t regretted it for a moment. I am aware that in the time since this update was first launched, Discord has modified that version I first saw to more closely resemble the one I use right now. However, the new interface still does not solve the accessibility issues I was worried about (I’ve tested it on others’ phones). So, Discord, despite your efforts to remove aspects of the app I had access to before the update, even though you’ve locked me out of playing games on calls and using soundboards and fancy text and hyperlinks, even though I can’t see polls and forwarded messages and games in chats, I will stand firm. You could strip every feature except calling and chatting and I would still not update. And if you ever tried to remove one of those, I would move on. I have no interest in supporting an app that willfully destroys accessibility for its users despite feedback and outright protest. The only way you will ever get a cent of my money is adding an option to use the old interface. In the meantime, I’ll ask for screenshots and play games on other services. Services that don’t think some nebulous vision of progress and modernity is more important than their users.
Edit after reply: the feedback site you’ve linked is so poorly designed that a full hour of searching and sifting through posts turned up nothing. I really don’t know why I expected otherwise.",2,259.1,bluesky the competitive,0
us,United States,10902943070,2024-02-04T18:23:08-07:00,Nitro is the best & full review,"So I have nitro and for those who are wondering about nitro and if it is worth it, it is. I have it and I love it. It features are the best. 2 server boosts is the big thing. Now there are some downsides. Like none of the tutorials I use to try to get 1080p and 60fps streams work. Now emojis and animated emojis are the best ngl. Now please if any person is reading this, this app is 13+ there is some s*x, swearing, bad users, etc. so if any kid goes on there make sure there isn’t any of what is said. There is different age requirements in each state make sure you read what your state requirement is. If your kid is on a Minecraft, Roblox, etc support server that is fine some people can’t afford support websites. These servers are ok. Some other servers are not like e-girl servers. There are bots that trick you to join by free nitro. Make sure it is from discord before you click on it. Bots are ok especially verified ones. Well that is it. Have a great day!",4,214.0,ziggyminecraft,1
us,United States,10672117569,2023-12-08T15:49:33-07:00,UI Update,"I really miss the old layout. The new layout looks very cluttered and I wish there was a way to disable it. The “online” tab was very useful and I much prefer it to having to use the search option instead. The new messages tab is also very irritating and clunky to navigate.

Additionally, the new colors don’t match the (much better) colors of the desktop app and to make matters worse, numerous users have reported that the new colors can make using the app quite painful, especially for those with astigmatism or other visual conditions. Please consider making a “classic” or “gray” mode with the old colors!

Discord is starting to feel like a “social media” app akin to Snapchat rather than the niche networking service it used to be. It feels more “childish” now, perhaps trying to appeal to a “TikTok” audience. Out of everybody I’ve talked to, nobody likes the new interface. Discord is beginning to lose its charm for me, and I am not the only person who thinks it. On behalf of your whole community, please consider making a change, or at the very least, allowing users to opt out of the new layout.",1,207,bozeman2000,0
us,United States,9751986379,2023-03-25T16:30:40-07:00,I love it but one thing,"Discord is, well… to say the least it’s good but not the best. I mean, don’t get me wrong, I do like it overall, but I’d rate it like, an 8/10. There’s a few flaws. Or maybe just 1? Okay, I have this one friend in particular on discord who had an account but made a new one. It’s ‘ they_call_me_melanie ‘ but without the quotations if they count. So basically, we like to chat a lot and call a lot, but lately I’ve noticed something. So I wanted to call, but for some reason it just said I wasn’t friends with her, which was weird because I still had the server. It told me to send a friend request, I clicked it but it just said she’s not accepting friend requests and she needed to friend me again in order for me to be able to call again. I thought my brother was the culprit, but he said it wasn’t him. I confronted the friend once at school, she said it wasn’t her. Could somebody PLEASE help me out here? I’m, like, really confused.",4,170.0,maennd,0
us,United States,6352174994,2020-08-23T06:16:52-07:00,Some Newly-Found Criticism,"I've been using discord for a few years at this point, and I want to make it clear that I use this app every day. It's how I've met some of the best people in my life, friends across the world I would have never otherwise met and learned from. However, after the most recent update I can't help but have noticed the glitchy behavior of the app (on mobile). When I go to the emote button my whole keyboard stops working for a long amount of time I didn't usually experience, likely due to the influx of keyboard functions just recently implemented, and finally the discord connection servers in general have been acting super unusual. This might be a thing only I'm experiencing, I'm not sure. It feels as though discord has outages every week, and it's starting to get frustrating. I do enjoy the app and will continue to use it regardless of these opinions, it definitively can offer experiences with people that might change the way you see the world.",4,35.1,beansybee,0
us,United States,11299208011,2024-05-23T12:17:40-07:00,i love discord... but,"i love discord, im on it all the time, its my fav social media platform & there is nothing else like it. however they really should stop trying to always like add new things & changing the app, i still preferred some aspects of the old mobile layout over what it is now, and they keep changing certian things back and forth. i prefer the new message/dm tab but they moved it back above the servers, i like the new ""your profile"" tab much better. but i hate the new beta channels thing, where you have to select what channels you want to see. it really interfere's with interacting with servers, especially as a moderator, tickets wont show up until days later sometimes. we already have the ""hide muted channels"" option, this new beta feature is just in the way. i also miss the old swipe left to view the members tab, that will be a feature i will always want back. it was so much better than the channel search tab we have now, it was just easier & more pleasing to look at. i also dont like how there is just a nitro gifting button next to the msg bar, it just isnt necessary & in the way, nitro is like an extra feature that not everyone can afford let alone just give to other people, i just don't see any benefit having it there really. but thats all my complaints, other than that i still love the app & its like nothing else out there.",4,230.0,kiva the wolf,0
us,United States,7786697271,2021-09-08T23:35:07-07:00,Emoticon to Emoji,"while i love using discord and i often use it as a means to contact some of my friends, i have noticed one issue that i’ve experienced. when i type “:) or <3” or other emoticons it automatically changes it to “🙂 and ❤️” or whatever emoticon i’ve put down. i’ve searched and searched and searched for ways to fix it on mobile, but i cannot seem to fix it. i have an iphone 11, and it won’t show me any possible way to prevent it from changing emoticons to emoji’s.
i personally detest emoji’s. i don’t like using them unless i’m using them ironically/as a joke or there is absolutely no emoticon that fits the conversation. i would MUCH rather have to manually put in emoji’s rather than have it constantly change my emoticons. the only time it doesn’t change is when it appears as part of a word. for example: “hi:)” rather than “hi :)” which i prefer the space in between. it really irks me. i hope y’all get this fixed !!",4,89.0,Awakeboar,0
us,United States,7750831926,2021-08-30T01:36:08-07:00,It's pretty good.,"I'm not saying Discord is bad, it definitely isn't. Discord is a place where you can chat and hangout with friends, and it does that job very well. Well enough that I use Discord mainly to contact my friends, there are some times where my computer isn't available/with me and I have to use my phone. Sure its not a smooth as PC but its still smooth enough that its usable, the reason I'm giving it four stars is because of a few issues I have with the voice calls on mobile. There isn't many but one issue is that most of the time when I'm calling someone the call causes Discord to make the screen unresponsive and black for a few seconds and then disappears, it does this rapidly to the point where it Isn't usable. Its hard enough to use the screen that I can't even end the call, it doesn't affect other apps and it does stop when i get out of the Discord app. I was hoping the next few bug fixes would fix it soon, it didn't.

Still, everything else works smoothly. I hope this gets fixed soon.

Edit: Somehow the update made it worse? The black screen is still there, now its a bit more manageable but not a lot. Theres a certain position my phone has to be in, or else the black screen occurs. Wearing headphones stops it, but there are times where I have to charge my phone. And since iPhones no longer have the head jack things I can't do both, how does it get worse? Every time the screen goes black, when it goes away. It sets my phone's brightness to max for a second and goes back, then goes away.

Jesus christ. It was like a flash bang to me when I was just trying to mute myself, it was 1  am in the morning.",4,88.2,Your Local Reviewer Guy,0
us,United States,3905245793,2019-03-20T13:21:40-07:00,Discord is hot as heck,"Discord is a great messaging service for anyone. Developers,    G a m e r s, and anything else you can think of, the possibilities do have an end but it’s a pretty high amount of possibilities 👌. Discord images deleted or not no matter what server is selected appear in your Discord cache though. Might want to clear it every once in a while. Discord has screen sharing, video calls and the ability to stream a single page or game in decent quality with good FPS depending on your computer. The amount of servers you can join at once is pretty endless, maybe I don’t know. This can allow to connect with a lot of communities at once and connect with others on your favorite subjects. Besides a few incidents with the Trust and safety team and the ToS. Besides that, Discord is a pretty spicy app.
                                                                       
                                                                             Yee",5,2.5.0,Mlg doge 999999969,1
us,United States,13309052773,2025-10-24T11:50:02-07:00,I give up.,"This apps moderation is absolutely horrible. Someone can just click buttons and spam report you and even if you literally said nothing wrong EVER, just because they clicked some buttons you’re banned and the spam reporter is perfectly fine yet I have been banned and have NEVER broken discord TOS. I have read every line of discord tos and have NEVER breached the terms of service. I’ve tried appealing the false bans in every way but The discord support portal and other methods are useless, always just a worthless message about how they won’t change their stupid decision. Discord is riddled with horrible disgusting people, and yet the app chooses to spend its time hunting ME down, someone who literally just says hello to their friends on the app. Genuinely broken moderation… depressing every time I lose my contact with the real friends I’ve made on discord. I would’ve given 5 stars if not for myself and the dozen friends I know being falsely banned and spam reported while just being genuinely kind not disgusting people. I really just wish to keep the contact I have with the nice people I meet.",1,301.0,Dintaifung🥟,0
us,United States,11915667221,2024-11-05T07:29:04-07:00,Terrible User Interface,"I use this app everyday yet the interface is clunky, critical buttons are small, media breaks, channels fail to load. And the overall User Interface is difficult to navigate, and almost nonsensical at times. You can't arrange the tab at the bottom, why would I need quick access to my profile and notifications? Why can't I just access DM's and some other useful quick launch button of some sort. I have to say as much as I love the app for what it is the UI is so bad at times it's downright frustrating. It's a straight copy of the desktop app...which works for desktop and not for mobile. It's very unimaginative, and the community throws a collective fit every time it gets updated. Worst of all you can't use third party apps/clients to access discord (which I understand), I just really dislike the UI.
