I hope these problems get resolved quickly or as soon as possible.",3,118.0,ChellyBelly888,0
us,United States,5648451439,2020-03-11T20:48:19-07:00,Actually life changing,"I made a discord account back in late 2016, I started a server in early 2017. Thanks to a lot of amazing people it ballooned to nearly 500 members and turned into a full fledged community that is still thriving to this day. 

The point isn’t to brag (mostly) but to illustrate that my Discord server has become a permanent fixture in my life, I have met friends who are just as close to me as any other, it’s almost like a big online family, so much so that some of us have even met up in real life to hang out. The app has its issues but it’s frequently updated and so the utility of the app has massively inflated since I joined.

This review is honestly a bit of a mess and I’m probably not giving anyone any useful information. So my bottom line is essentially this: 

Discord is an incredibly versatile, functional, and easy to use app on both mobile and PC. It is distinctly aimed towards gamers, but it could be useful in just about any application you could need a social networking platform for. The developers possess an awesome sense of humor, and clearly care about the platform they’ve created. Don’t be put off by its reputation as having an entirely gamer-centric, younger demographic. Because as far as social networking goes, Discord has no equal in terms of functionality, it does everything you’d need for free, the premium account only does bonus features (like increased file size limit for file sharing), that are very useful, but don’t gimp the experience to not have in any significant way, especially for the cheap subscription. 

11/10 would allow it to consume my life again.",5,12.0,jmgdog66,0
us,United States,9892615411,2023-05-04T11:36:54-07:00,I love discord but I would just like to make a small suggestion,"I absolutely LOVE discord I use it to talk to all my friends and call them, the calls are always a bit laggy for me but it’s really no issue. I’ve had discord for I think almost a year now and there has been a lot of updates which I like when they add a new update. If you want to use this app to talk to your friends and stuff like that I DEFINITELY recommend discord. But i would like to add a suggestion for the app. My suggestion is basically if like when you tap on a message like if you can see if the person has seen/read your message. For example, if you sent a message to your crush and they haven’t responded yet you could check your message and you could see if they had seen your message or if they have not. I just think it would make it a lot better.",5,175.0,Oki_Boomer,0
us,United States,4355120442,2019-06-22T16:50:06-07:00,Fix some glitches.,"I’ve used Discord for years now and I’ve loved it but lately I’ve noticed some glitches with the app. There is a glitch where you can be typing in one server and then next thing you know the same text will appear in your keyboard on a totally different server like you typed it out for that new second server when you never had the ability to type in that certain channel in the first place. The only way that you can fix this is you have to uninstall and reinstall the app. That has happened to me multiple times and it needs to be fixed. And now there is a glitch with the newest version where my Discord information at the top of the screen is clashing with my clock, battery percentage, and so on at the top of my phone. Also now there is a glitch where I can’t get notifications for messages when I’m not using the app. I have tried everything. I would appreciate it if this issue was fixed.",4,3.0.4,nfkenxksnshxhdh,0
us,United States,1851321063,2017-10-15T13:49:10-07:00,Dissapointed and may not come back...,"I’m a gamer and many players use the discord app. A few months ago, I had issues logging in, actually I could not so I reloaded the app on my iPhone and it worked. It returned to its old habit within a few weeks by not allowing me to log in and so I deleted it. Our group has other apps, one old, and others suggested so I stayed away from discord. This morning I found a need to download it again because of another gamer....and yes, same issue. When I was unable to login, I went to my browser and changed my password just to ensure I wasn’t typing it incorrectly. When I returned to the mobile app...nothing. APPS SHOULD NOT BE THIS DIFFICULT TO GET INTO. I have googled the issue and there’s been MANY complaints of this. My problem is that most of the online resources posting possibly fixes are for PC/MAC’s......I think I’m done. I hate to leave negative reviews but it’s become so disappointing and frustrating that I felt I needed to warn others of this issue. I hope Discord fixes this in the future for others who may run into this problem.",2,1.9.2,Uabflightrrt,10
us,United States,14141324965,2026-06-03T19:20:28-07:00,Bad community for finding friends,"I have used this app off and on for several years. And honestly I’m very disappointed. I thought communities would get better As the app got more developed and more people used it. But if you’re looking for friends. Or people to like be understanding and also be online friends with. Don’t use this app. A lot of these groups in discord are very exclusive. And extremely toxic. I’ve known a couple of people who went to the psychiatric ward for mental breakdowns because of this app and how exclusive and violent people online in discord or that have discord can be. First of all, I am not at liberty to tell who these people are. Secondly don’t ask me for that information. All I’m saying is there has been a lot of people including myself who have used this app and came back on and off it several times and each time it made their life’s harder then it needed to be. If you want, my opinion, this app is clearly not a good place to be making online friends. I’ve had to delete this app several times as well and it would be off and on.",1,331.0,Violet Andra,1
