in,India,6104684990,2020-06-21T07:35:05-07:00,"It is a really good app, but needs improved moderation","Discord is a really good app. While most people use it to communicate with each other for games and such, it can even be used for school competitions and such. But the reason I have given 4 stars is because the moderation is very cringe worthy as most moderators abuse their power, or use it for very small reasons even though this app is 12+. There should be valid reasons and proof for bots to ban people from discord servers, and a strike system should be used instead. I feel that this app should really change its moderation and make it fair for a 12+ app, it just doesn’t seem mature or compulsory, and it is very abusable. That is my review, and this is just my opinion. Someone else might say the moderation is good or outstanding but I don’t think it is. Anyways I hope you found this helpful.

Yash Raj Mehta",4,26.0,Yash Raj Mehta,24
in,India,8737623714,2022-06-03T10:53:01-07:00,My account got hacked,"I have received notification regarding changes to my account I haven’t requested
And have been receiving messages from users neither in any of my servers or from my friend group. I recently received a friend request from my own account which I don’t think is possible unless my account has been tampered with. I have changed my password three times since this event and have seen no change. This was not expected of such a usually good app and has disappointed me very much how easily a persons account can be accessed by a third party. I hope to see a solution to this issue as soon as possible. 
A discord user by the name of hacker2.0 could also monitor my activity while neither being my friend nor having any previous chat history with him.
I hope users such as them get investigated before more innocent people like me lose their accounts",1,129.0,Sj1429,6
in,India,13992033251,2026-04-24T07:07:04-07:00,Screen share for PS5,"Discord is an amazing platform for communication, but one major limitation on PS5 really needs attention.

Right now, if you’re using Discord on PlayStation 5, there’s no proper way to stream your screen directly to a Discord voice channel. Instead, you’re forced to use PS Share, which only works with other PS5 users. This completely breaks the experience—especially if you’re in a Discord VC with friends on different platforms.

The biggest issue is that you have to leave your Discord voice chat just to share your screen through PlayStation. That defeats the whole purpose of Discord as a cross-platform communication tool. It makes streaming gameplay to friends inconvenient and honestly frustrating.

It would be a huge improvement if Discord added native screen streaming support on PS5, just like it works on PC and mobile. Being able to stay in a voice channel and stream your gameplay seamlessly would make the experience much smoother and more enjoyable.

Please consider adding this feature—it's something a lot of users would genuinely benefit from.",4,325.0,Ghost_king141,0
